{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races","id":1212058,"title":"Non-Human Races?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T16:58:06-07:00","id":1212058,"title":"Non-Human Races?","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Non-Human Races - have you ever included them? How? Why?</span><br /> <hr /><br /> Yes, we have <b>Mountain Folk</b>, <b>Dragon Kings,</b> the <b>Lintha</b> and <b>Crafted Races </b>- but these are all so geographically desperate that it's unfathomable to think of them ever having &quot;popular stereotypes&quot;. Games with them will usually be <i>about</i> them, unless you're just visiting as a one-off adventure. <b>Humanity</b> has always been king in Exalted - and I <i>appreciate that</i>. <br /> <br /> But do I?<br /> <br /> I mean that &quot;racial tropes&quot; in other games have built-in problems.<ul><li>Races have gradually lost social relevance - an &quot;Half-Orc, High Elf &amp; Dwarf&quot; party (unimaginable in another era!) is all par for the course now.</li> <li>Races have mechanical bonuses - so you usually see each race play 3-4 specific classes. Not really diverse.</li> <li>Races discourage themes <i>without</i> mechanical bonuses. Not many Orc Wizards or Tiefling Barbarians, right?</li> </ul>So by dodging races altogether, Exalted has done something lovely. And I <b>love</b> how other tropes are absorbed into mega-tropes - Centaurs, Harpies, etc can be Beastmen tribes (Lunars thus providing one clean creation-myth for all of them); Banshees, Zombies, Ghosts, Nephwracks etc are mostly the same undead with different powers (not a dozen different and conflicting creation stories).<br /> <br /> But <b>then</b> I noticed &quot;Plane Shift: Ixalan&quot; (a D&amp;D supplement for MtG settings) - and the temptation is back. <b>There's something useful</b> in these tropes. Four factions, six races - a glance at a single art panel and you instantly can tell if you might vibe or not.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are Genasi with a thicker Culture. And even in 2E, I remember Lookshy having &quot;recommended stats&quot; to represent the military culture. <b>And maybe that's the solution</b>. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Race not as skin-coloring and biology - but as region-specific cultural templates?</span><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>The only obstacle I see is the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">scale</span> of the map. </b><br /> <br /> Non-human races seem far-flung in Exalted - so there are few places one might find a cosmopolitan mix (maybe working for a Guild Caravan, carnival-style? half-divine offspring of some travel-god? a zoo in Yu Shan?). Or they're all human - but somehow have radically radically different cultures (enough that you can't simply strip them naked and confuse them for each other)? Ritual tattoos, scarring, something?<br /> <br /> Have any of you ever mulled adding fantasy races in?<br /> <br /> Or have you used existing mega-tropes (Beastmen, Undead, etc) to create cultures?<br /> <br /> Or maybe a Lookshy/Dragon-Blooded style set of &quot;here are some base stats people from this city have - then spend X points customizing&quot;?<br /> <br /> How would you do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:16:47-07:00","id":1212072,"title":"","content":"Exalted is a very humanist setting; as in, humans are unique, interesting to the gods. We are given their divine spark because they see something in us that even they cannot attain. It's part of the entire theme and aspects of Exalted. The few other sentient races all are defined by their relations to humans--the Gods sit above in their divine affairs, so far above, yet something to be attained. The Fae are the jealous forms, despising and yet desiring what we have. The Jadeborn and Dragon Kings are what came before--something close to us, but missing that last spark that makes humanity special. Beastmen and mutants are what happens what we are twisted beyond recognition.<br /> <br /> That is why it is difficult to place <i>meaningful</i> races into Exalted. There are ways you <i>can</i> put the races in--beastmen and anything to do with the Fae, for example. Or just rewrite the history for your own canon--a shard of existence where humanity was not alone.<br /> <br /> I think the question you have to answer first with different races, more than anything, is &quot;What narrative purpose do they serve?&quot; I think from that flows the way to do what you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic","name":"Dragonmystic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar845_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:22:06-07:00","id":1212075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races#post1212058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Non-human races seem far-flung in Exalted - so there are few places one might find a cosmopolitan mix (maybe working for a Guild Caravan, carnival-style? half-divine offspring of some travel-god? a zoo in Yu Shan?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll note that this is part of why places such as Nexus, Great Forks, Chiaroscuro and... oh God I can't remember it, the new place, the Western city in the core book's opening fiction, exist. Being cosmopolitan will attract a variety of people, and so they're places in which such oddities might be found hiding in the cracks.<br /> <br /> \u200bYu-Shan has also been written in previous Editions as a place where many of the few surviving Dragon Kings who retain their intelligence have sought refuge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:23:16-07:00","id":1212076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonmystic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212072#post1212072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are given their divine spark because they see something in us that even they cannot attain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like having not been given a geas to prevent attacking their enemies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:40:01-07:00","id":1212080,"title":"","content":"Exalted has humans, people with pointy ears, short people, panda people, hairy people, animal people, etc. In fact, it's got more diversity than many RPG settings. They're all still considered human though from the perspective of the setting because of one fundamental fact of the setting - non-humans (Lintha, Mountain Folk, Dragon Kings, etc) cannot Exalt and don't have an Exaltation. Which means that if you want to introduce a new non-human race and have it be playable, you sort of need to come up with a set of Charms or other supernatural abilities and mechanics so that the player doesn't get left behind by the people who are Exalted and have those supernatural abilities and mechanics.<br /> <br /> Honestly I like the way Exalted works, in that if someone wants to be a human with pointy ears, and cat eyes or whatever, they just describe themselves that way and you can play it off as a quirk of genetics, a wyld mutation, a demonic ancestor, or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:47:17-07:00","id":1212084,"title":"","content":"When you look closely at the playable non-humans they pretty consistently have their own equivalent to Exalts, the thing that's actually missing are mortals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:50:03-07:00","id":1212085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races#post1212058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Non-Human Races - have you ever included them? How? Why?</span> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, i did use them. A made-up underbrood race, a mash up of greys with nosferatu for visuals. A pair of them came to the surface to investigate something, but it has been a bunch of years and can't really remember right now.<br /> But there was some nice, goofy fun with that duo of &quot;subterranean vampaliens&quot; involving among other things a big, bad kaiju battle royale between a Behemoth, a Warstrider and the &quot;inquisitors&quot; growing to giant size with strange silver powersuits (that resembled Ultraman) amidst the streets of Nexus (Emissary had been eaten and was kind of powering the Behemoth, so could not intervene). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212075#post1212075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll note that this is part of why places such as Nexus, Great Forks, Chiaroscuro and... oh God I can't remember it, the new place, the Western city in the core book's opening fiction, exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wu-Jian, i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212075#post1212075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being cosmopolitan will attract a variety of people, and so they're places in which such oddities might be found hiding in the cracks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or even standing in plain sight as simply a particularly exotic foreigner. Remember the peculiar fantastic people described in Herodotus' Histories or the Travels of Marco Polo? Not to mention those of such odd people with cosmopolitan places of their own, like the Ixcoatli Empire or Serpolet for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212075#post1212075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bYu-Shan has also been written in previous Editions as a place where many of the few surviving Dragon Kings who retain their intelligence have sought refuge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, got some use out of them in a Sidereals game a few years ago in fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212084#post1212084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you look closely at the playable non-humans they pretty consistently have their own equivalent to Exalts, the thing that's actually missing are mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't quite say that. More like races like the Jadeborn, Dragon Kings and Lintha occupy a sort of middle ground between Exalt and our definition of &quot;mortal races&quot;.<br /> <br /> Though those three were something like the top tier of the Primordial races, with people such as the &quot;generic underbroods&quot; in Scroll of Fallen Races being lower in capacity, while others such as Pelagials or Alaun were very much mortal overall. The Alaun in particular were basically smart sword-wielding Austrech with basalt castles and some thaumaturgy, at least based in the tidbits one can colate from Oadenol's Codex and CoCD:Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-09-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:19:41-07:00","id":1212093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212085#post1212085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't quite say that.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think she's got a point. They do carry a certain baggage from the need to constitute a society that ostensibly consists of everybody having supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">one fundamental fact of the setting - non-humans (Lintha, Mountain Folk, Dragon Kings, etc) cannot Exalt and don't have an Exaltation.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bWellll, that at least applies to the existing classic Exalted. The developers have said that the Spoken were Chosen from among non-human beings among the Niobraran League.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's not really a fundamental fact so much as a marginal emergent property, in my eyes. Whether or not they can Exalt matters less to the definition of whether a Dragon King is human or not than the fact that it's a sapient dinosaur who hatched from an egg, spent the first few decades of its life as a ravenous wild animal, and as it grows older and stronger, has an increasingly sharp recollection of previous lives.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven the powers thing... the mythology of the setting holds that humans weren't subject to the geas because they were regarded as too weak to be a threat, which does establish a baseline by which the abilities of others are measured, but so long as a race can have <i>something</i> attributed to it that might qualify for the geas, even if it's not hugely significant, then the bigger priority is in making the species sufficiently alien in biology and the manner in which that affects outlook.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd even for the powers thing... it can be plausible that there would exist other alien races in the setting apart from the designs of Primordials.<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, with the tone of how the setting is established, what there isn't necessarily room for is these beings living in societies that can be readily slotted in among humans. I'd say that there has to be a barrier of seperation, even if it's one that can be crossed for the sake of exchanges.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:27:29-07:00","id":1212094,"title":"","content":"Also please note, playable. We didn't have support for playable Lintha (save as their modern incarnation as demon blooded pirates) let alone Pelagials or Alaun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:56:59-07:00","id":1212103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212093#post1212093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI think she's got a point. They do carry a certain baggage from the need to constitute a society that ostensibly consists of everybody having supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the game did focus in those who were special and offered new options of play or as antagonists (the whole Lintha as Creation's Melniboneans coming straight from Blood &amp; Salt, as far as i can remember, them being just mutant pirates with some Yozi worship on the side before that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212094#post1212094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also please note, playable. We didn't have support for playable Lintha (save as their modern incarnation as demon blooded pirates) let alone Pelagials or Alaun.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, what we have on the last two and others does not paint a image much different from mutants or beastmen in play potential &amp; options. Though admitedly only so far and could certainly change if the right fancy or idea hit one of the devs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-26-2018, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:04:19-07:00","id":1212114,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>re: Mutations</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Yes, we can have pointy ears, weird skin and other fun features in Exalted - but these do not imply nor confer a culture, values, language, traditions, norms. <i>They're superficial</i>. They're phenotypes, not races. Ergo, it's shallow. <i>It's fun and useful</i>, but boils down to being a slightly mutated human.<br /> <br /> At it's core, having the same skin color (or whatever) doesn't constitute a race. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>re: Lintha, Pelagials, Alaun, etc</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Being playable / not-playable is a different set of problems. Even if they're just NPCs, they can be useful. I did more googling and found a compilation from Exalted:<ul><li><b>Extinct:</b><ul><li><b>The Alaun</b> - bird-like people who sang Primoridal praises all day, whose ghosts now haunt the Underworld</li> <li><b>The Ereta'een</b> - alien-like people smelted by Autochton into Soulsteel</li> <li><b>The Kyzvoi</b> - crafted hybrids of men/scorpions/wolves whose ghosts haunt Marama's Fell</li> <li><b>The Mazriki</b> - telepathic mantises who fed on fear who &quot;taught the raksha much&quot;</li> <li><b>The Scathacs</b> - humanoid-giants of worm-colonies that Raksha loathed for their &quot;false complexity&quot;</li> <li><b>The Sheedai</b> - crafted aquatic love-slaves made by a Twilight, now floating in the underworld amid murder-fish</li> <li><b>The T'Shay'I</b> - unknown, hunted to extinction by the Dragon-Kings</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Survivors:</b><ul><li><b>Humans</b> - weakest, numerous but geas-free (and thus favored for Exaltation)</li> <li><b>Eyeless Nation - </b>birthed from a behemoth, exiled and now only summoned by sorcery</li> <li><b>Dragon-Kings</b> - closest to gods by design, based off giant scaled beasts</li> <li><b>Lintha</b> - humanoid, favored by Kimbery, essence-users</li> <li><b>Mountain Folk</b> - born from a behemoth (Clay Man) or made by Autochton (Dwarves)</li> <li><b>Pelagials</b> - humanoid, &quot;beneath Lintha &amp; Mosok, above Humans&quot; - Yozi-worshippers who speak to a Neverborn</li> <li><b>Pineys &amp; Chaun</b> - two distinct races of sentient plant-people (Pineys are nice with poor memory; Chaun hostile &amp; xenophobic)</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Crafted &amp; Odd:</b><ul><li><b>Elemental: </b>Air &amp; Sea Folk, Dune Peoples (slave race), Tree Folk (eugenics), Earth Folk (bred themselves out of existence)</li> <li><b>Djala / Minikin: </b>Another humanoid variant</li> <li><b>Hura: </b>A &quot;fleshy artificial race&quot; that became &quot;plasmic entities&quot; after fleeing to the Underworld to escape the Usurpation. Exalts designed them. No mention if they could survive in Creation still.</li> <li><b>The Indwryth</b>, the Exquisite Prey - deer-like creatures in Malfeas (but not demons) who make wonderful expresisons &amp; music</li> <li><b>The Singers of the Deep</b> - Wyld mutated humans</li> <li><b>The Unju</b> - Birds of Burden, not properly demons. Featherless avians with manlike bodies.</li> <li><b>The Rapace</b> - Southern ape-like-men. No word if mutant, beastman or other.</li> <li><b>Demons?</b> &quot;Pre-Yozi Deva races included the Gilmyne, Angyalkae and Agata&quot;</li> </ul></li> </ul>The problem with <b>most</b> of this list..... is that they're written as <b>extinct horrors whose tombs or ghosts </b>you might trip across. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>re: Narrative Purpose</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/845-dragonmystic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar845_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"845\" data-vbnamecard=\"845\">Dragonmystic</a> really hit it on the head.<br /> <br /> I think one benefit is &quot;narrative shorthand&quot; - and another is &quot;bulwark against assimilation&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, someone playing a &quot;savage barbarian&quot; or &quot;surly drunkard&quot; might feel pressure to assimilate to group-norms (especially within a city) - but in D&amp;D, if you're a Half-Orc or Dwarf and the rest are Humans or Half-Elves, there's a certain &quot;it is what it is&quot; because certain behaviors might be <b>cultural, biological or both.</b><br /> <br /> In other words, fantasy races create a sort of &quot;social armor&quot; for the player to stick out form the group during RP. And people can't just be upset and irrational about it. No one <b>needs</b> to play to stereotypes, but you're <b>unlikely to be shocked</b> if the Orc is violent or dumb; if the Dwarf is zealously-honor-bound and drunk; if the Gnome skulked around while the team fought on the front-line; or if a Tiefling does something unethical. <b>In fact</b>, the racial tropes help remind you of the differences - and you even start playing to those stereotypes (maybe assigning the Orc and Dwarf into a drunken violence spectacle (as a distraction) while the Gnome is sneaking to rob the noble who the Elf is seducing (or whatever).<br /> <br /> <b>It also</b> helps verbalize biases. People are more comfortable saying &quot;I hate Orcs&quot; or &quot;I loathe Dwarves&quot; - I've never seen someone (even experienced players) say &quot;I can't stand Sijanese people&quot; or &quot;Great Forks needs a good genocide&quot; (okay, maybe an Abyssal group). <b>And without going to those extremes</b>, <i>the point is</i> that it gives you a solid idea. Story hooks arise. <i>Why do you hate Orcs? Could this character be baited into a quest via word of Orc marauders? What if they saw Humans acting the way they accuse Orcs of acting? What if they met an Orc Wizard or Bard? </i><br /> <br /> In other words, <b>cities (and their inhabitants)</b> aren't just backdrops for the ST to tell stories - with races, players see archetypes of those inhabitants (and are more prone to interact with those stereotypes). <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>re: Great Forks, Chiaroscuro, Wu-Jian, Nexus - and An-Teng</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Some of these I imagined as mere &quot;trade hubs full of diverse humans and a few beastmen or god-blooded&quot; - yeah &quot;diverse&quot;, but not necessarily enough for there to be <i>races</i> that people have stereotypes about. <b>Nexus</b> is the lead example I think. <b>Wu-Jian </b>too (almost everything described still <i>looks human</i> which is why Dragon-Blooded can't just spot and purge them).<br /> <br /> But reconsidering some of these, <b>Chiaroscuro and Great Forks</b> work great.<ul><li>My mind's eye always pictured <b>Great Forks </b>as having 3 groups of people from the Scavenger Lands merging into 1 people.... but why not keep their individuality? It could be 3 truly distinct ethnic groups (different dress, customs, accents, looks, etc) each with their &quot;main god&quot; (of the 3) and a couple personal sub-gods.<ul><li>So it's still a city of a thousand gods - full of a mix of Scavenger Land mortals - but with 3 major enclaves loyal-to-each-other but committed to their distinct traditions. Maybe even mutated enough to breed true? I could steal Autochtonian mutants! So maybe Dayshield has a lesser forge-god as an attendant (whose favored mortals have smoked-skinned descendants, etc).</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Chiaroscuro</b> also has 3 people. I previously thought &quot;it's just Aladdin&quot;, but it could have Indo-Aryan Caste-system vibes.<ul><li><b>The Dead</b> are the first generation - it's wards provide a unique way to showcase &quot;ancient undead&quot; as a sort of local &quot;race&quot;; <b>The Warlords </b>are the second generation, the warring peoples who previously fought for the city; <b>The Tri-Khan</b> are the third generation, the Iranian-inspired invaders with distinct culture and clothing. They're not as exaggerated as D&amp;D races - but they could be portrayed distinct enough for stereotypes.</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>The Sweet Spot </b>seems to be <b>An-Teng</b>.</span><ul><li><b>The Dragon-Blooded</b> are obviously distinct culturally.</li> <li><b>The Families</b> - instead of blurring them into &quot;locals&quot; - should divide into the 3 Princes influence.<ul><li>Shadow-Puppeteers? shadow-magic</li> <li>Elephant-Riding Ghost Generals? more Heroic mortals / heroes</li> <li>Animal-Commanding Masks? maybe famaily mascots/pets</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Serpent Men</b> - 2E mentions beastmen, &quot;more man than serpent&quot; now, confused for god-bloods</li> <li><b>Silver Crowned</b> - 2E had an insular, hair bleached white, wearing steel jewelry</li> <li><b>Seven Stranded Vine Heirs</b> - not merely a cult, they have heirs of the original royal lineages..... inbreeding + demonic influence.... so they might make a distinct ethnicity with mutations (without revealing they're actually a Yozi cult of course - use another excuse)</li> <li><b>God-Blooded &amp; Ghost-Blooded &amp; Kaleyi</b> - all 3 tucked into the local religion</li> </ul>PLUS<ul><li>WEST: Lintha ? Pelagials ? Singers of the Deep ? Sea Folk ?</li> <li>SOUTH: Dune People ?</li> <li>SHADOWLANDS: Hura ?</li> <li>OTHER: Djala ? Dragon-King?</li> </ul>In other words, An-Teng is mostly human - but culturally split (and rigid) enough that you could differentiate them into much stronger stereotypes. <b>This doesn't mean turning them into Orcs and Elves and Dwarves</b>. But give each ethnic group slightly different garb and accents - maybe mutations or phenotypes - and it quickly splits into the &quot;racial shorthand&quot; that might be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:24:02-07:00","id":1212121,"title":"","content":"So, I'm going to sidestep the idea of using fantasy races to encourage what reads to me as racist characters, for the purpose of questioning that racism. Briefly, those story hooks exist without orcs, dwarves, and elves and are more effective when there isn't this weird combination of culture and biology that a lot of DnD settings employ(I have lengthy problems with DnD's presentation of 'race' as a biologically distinct classification, with bearing on phyiscal, mental, and social capabillities.)<br /> <br /> Rather, for narrative, what <i>purpose</i> does a race serve? Orcs, in Tolkien, exist to give the legions of evil minions who aren't men and are therefore acceptable to kill on mass (and even then, tolkien was uncomfortable with the notion for years). Why <i>can't</i> the race just be humans?<br /> <br /> Also, on Nexus: Culturally diverse areas have stereotypes. Different cultures, when they meet, do have stereotypes of each other, even without mutation. Racial and ethnic stereotypes aren't even entirely dependant on apperance. <br /> <br /> To more intreasting points: Serpentmen are, I believe, beastmen. For purposes of exalted, beastmen are metaphyiscally human (capable of exaltation). <br /> Daja are human, just odd skin tone.<br /> the current devs have mentioned that non-demon inhabitants as fauna of Malfeas are unlikely. Exquiste prey will probably be demons.<br /> &quot;<ul><li><b>The Mazriki</b> - telepathic mantises who fed on fear who &quot;taught the raksha much&quot;</li> <li><b>The Scathacs</b> - humanoid-giants of worm-colonies that Raksha loathed for their &quot;false complexity&quot;</li> <li><b>The Sheedai</b> - crafted aquatic love-slaves made by a Twilight, now floating in the underworld amid murder-fish</li> <li><b>The T'Shay'I</b> &quot; Do you have a book for these? I'm curious.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T23:45:07-07:00","id":1212165,"title":"","content":"I enjoy your response, Epee - even though I land on the opposite end of the spectrum! =)<ul><li><b>Non-human races side-step real-life baggage.</b><br /> <br /> I work with a director who <i>loathes</i> magical realism and fantasy - even if a film sells well, he can't grasp why. And I stress - over and over - that fantasy is good <b>because</b> it is divorced from real-life preconceptions. Do a realistic play with realistic people and viewers will insert their own real-life experiences into the story.<br /> <br /> But add Orcs or Gnomes or Golems? - <i>that's new</i>. Preconceptions and stereotypes <i>have</i> to go out the window. <b>And then</b> you can have a conversation about real-world social problems without the knee-jerk: &quot;you can't say that about Dwarves!&quot; or &quot;this is a negative stereotype about Goblins!&quot; or &quot;are you saying Elves don't have problems?&quot;\u200b Marvel uses Mutants as stand-ins for issues of race, gender, etc <i>and it works wonderfully</i> because it's unexpected when the fantasy-lessons line-up to real-life relevance.<br /> .</li> <li><b>Non-human races <i>shouldn't</i> always be the centerpiece</b><br /> <br /> I get what you mean about differences among humans. I can discern a Cuban, Puerto Rican and Dominican <i>-</i> a Columbian vs Venezuelan - a Mexican vs Honduran - a Jamaican vs Haitian - a Lebanese vs Omani. I love my city even if most Americans see &quot;uh, Latino&quot; or &quot;White?&quot; or &quot;Black!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>But</b> the typical English-speaker <b>won't</b> see those differences - and it'll be difficult for the ST to portray it - let alone for players to then grasp it. So why deliberately avoid a useful tool?<br /> <br /> So Orcs serve a purpose in LOTR that Humans <b>never</b> could. Because as humans (in the theater) viewing the enemy from the perspective of humans (on the battlefield), <i>one glance at the Orcs</i> and you know they're <b>not-of-your-tribe</b>. Games like Warcraft have 8 Troll, 5 Elf and a half-dozen splinter variants - <b>all related</b> - but the typical lvl 15 Human will only see &quot;Trolls = Bad, Night Elves = Friend, Blood Elves = uh.... badish?&quot;. The cultural and biological evolution of the Troll-Elven species <b>is irrelevant</b> to a story about &quot;Warcraft&quot; or &quot;Battle for Azeroth&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> Have you played the Elder Scrolls? Humans have 4+ distinct races - elves have more,etc - and each <i>mechanical set</i> of racial bonuses helps explain culture (Nords in the cold; Bretons using spells; Imperials being diplomats/charmers, etc).<br /> .</li> <li><b>Non-human races serve as useful shorthand</b><br /> <br /> I've had couple (and thankfully no more) <i>unfortunate</i> Exalted games where - since &quot;we're all human, we're all Solars&quot; - we eventually concluded with some variant of the &quot;Lawful Stupid&quot; Zenith smites the morally dubious Night/Twilight/Eclipse Castemate. Heresy &quot;offends most&quot; when it resembles your own default faith/assumptions (in this case, the Zenith's player believed all Solars were virtuous heroes - so &quot;something was clearly wrong&quot; with characters who didn't honor that trope).<br /> <br /> <i>Conversely</i>, I've had these situations dodged in D&amp;D. You hear something like &quot;we don't allow Tieflings because....&quot; or &quot;my Paladin hates Tieflings&quot; (and then you can play something else - or explain why the Tiefling should be an exception because... yadda yadda).<br /> <br /> And if approved, it eliminates the presumption that &quot;we look alike, therefore we think alike&quot;.<br /> <br /> So my Tiefling was approved - another went Half-Orc - the rest either Human or Half-Elf? Great! <i>No one was ever upset OOC</i> when the Orc was spectacularly violent - nor surprised when I was scheming. Instead of being held to human-standards of behavior, we were eternally <i>the foreigners</i>, so they judged us as such (even embracing the Orc as someone to send to combat - as opposed to a &quot;maniac human&quot; who needs to be less aggressive).</li> </ul><b>RE: SERPENTMEN</b><br /> Yes, they're entirely Beastmen - just more humanoid than average. It was a pleasant find (I deeply loathe the Silver Pact / barbarian-savage cliche, so seeing Beastmen used as allusions to N\u00fcwa and/or n\u0101gas from which &quot;the Khmer people descend&quot; is dope).<br /> <br /> Maybe I could steal from Black Panther (5 tribes, each with a vague animal theme, but as &quot;toned down&quot; as the Serpentmen that they're not obviously <i>beastmen </i>- make the associations seem more abstract). Hmm.<br /> <br /> <b>DJALA </b><br /> Skin Color, Longevity, Small, Enlightened Essence - human - but really, <i>most of the Crafted Race descriptions</i> read like <i>Histories</i>. They're useful but feel dry. I want to know their culture, norms, gods - not their Usurpation-era legal status changes. I've never <b>felt</b> <i>how to use them.</i><br /> <br /> <b>HELL-FAUNA</b><br /> Good to know!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS:</b><br /> <b>Graceful Wicked Masques, pg 22 : </b><br /> For similar reasons and a host of others, none of the early sentient races of Creation appealed for very long to the raksha. The <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>alaun </b></span>were too devoted to their Primordial masters and too willing to sacrifice their desires in pursuit of their masters\u2019 favor. The <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>scathacs </b></span>intrigued the raksha, but only until the raksha revealed the false complexity of a scathac mind as just a morass of competing lesser desires deriving from each scathac\u2019s component selves. The appetites of the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>mazriki </b></span>seemed promising and taught the raksha much, but the mazriki\u2019s palates were too depressingly narrow to be worth the raksha\u2019s attention. The will of the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>t\u2019shay\u2019i </b></span>burned brightest of all, but the Dragon Kings all too rapidly hunted them to extinction. With each flare of interest and subsequent disappointment, the raksha turned away from Creation as best they could and returned their attention to their own desires. At least there, in the Wyld, their desires could not disappoint.<br /> <br /> So with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> The others seem to (mostly) be from the <b>Underworld </b>compass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 04-27-2018, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T00:56:41-07:00","id":1212169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212103#post1212103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, what we have on the last two and others does not paint a image much different from mutants or beastmen in play potential &amp; options. Though admitedly only so far and could certainly change if the right fancy or idea hit one of the devs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was tired last night and I didn't parse what I meant very well.<br /> <br /> I think it's very likely that if the Pelagials or Alaun were ever fleshed out to the degree that the Dragon Kings or Mountain Folk were let alone made playable they'd probably end up with a special class that served the overall function of Exalts. In the case of Pelagials I've previously speculated those might be their Dead Princes who could function a bit like the D&amp;D Demilich and potentially be pretty impressive enemies for embalmed corpses. Not particularly appealing to humans but that's not thinking like a Pelagial.<br /> <br /> As to the future, I know Lea is pretty against Star Trek style &quot;bumpy forehead aliens&quot; in Exalted and I believe that in the Ask The Developers thread the Lintha have been noted to be the result of a Primordial mingling her blood with humans rather than an entirely different species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-27-2018, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T01:29:36-07:00","id":1212175,"title":"","content":"Well I tried importing Thedas, the Dragon Age setting, into Exalted so it exists elsewhere on inverted cardinal directions to Creation (so secret paths say East in Creation will Bring you to the West of Thedas and the North of Creation could bring you to the South of Thedas) upon the back of a lost Primordial The Fade whose Fetiche Soul is the Golden City Turned Black. So I played with how to do them in the Exalted setting so Dwarves are a civilization descended from the Mountainfolk/Human Godblooded. Elves are descended from the Raksha/Gods, and the Qunari are Primordial Race tied to Dragons somehow, which there I have as corporeal forms of Devas.<br /> <br /> But I also include Moogles from Final Fantasy in the Form of the Kupo, mostly in the proportions you see in FF12. They are an extinct race that was pretty much genocided during the Primordial War, but some still exist as living dreams, or in stasis awakening in the Time of Tumult. I have it their souls naturally materialize into Magicite a rare magical material that is crystalline rather then the smelted soulsteel of men. They develop along a double job caste system where they develop a primary Career and a secondary Career which defines it more both broadening and narrowing their roles. They can develop Merits based on these, comparable to say the supernatural merits of Sorcerers or simple charms.<br /> <br /> I also have the Bangaa which which I have using an inverted soul structure to humans in their Po is the main soul and the Hun is the lesser one. I have the Nu Mou and Seeq also existing but haven't really got to introduce them and still working on their soul mechanics. Probably something simple for the Seeq,and mysterious for the Nu Mou. I also have the Shumi, from FF8, that are pacifist spiritualists who were made by the primordial to be constantly evolving and reincarnating. Basically their soul has the capacity to transform into the soul of another depending on their nature, so they could reincarnate as a human or even a Dragon King's immortal soul, or the innocent Godsouled Moomba.<br /> <br /> I also include the Krogan from Mass Effect, as basically having a redundant soul structure of two heart souls and four lower souls.<br /> <br /> I have other unique species I've made, like an Underdark race called the Arthax that evolved after some of the subcaste species died off other castes replaced it. Different castes have different souls based on Ren (True Name), Shadow, Heart, and Memory.<br /> <br /> I've played around with the idea of a Deviant civilization of Darkbrood that basically are an amalgamation of multiple extinct and mutated species that now result in each generation being a different species then their parents or siblings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:28:57-07:00","id":1212232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212169#post1212169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I was tired last night and I didn't parse what I meant very well.<br /> <br /> I think it's very likely that if the Pelagials or Alaun were ever fleshed out to the degree that the Dragon Kings or Mountain Folk were let alone made playable they'd probably end up with a special class that served the overall function of Exalts. In the case of Pelagials I've previously speculated those might be their Dead Princes who could function a bit like the D&amp;D Demilich and potentially be pretty impressive enemies for embalmed corpses. Not particularly appealing to humans but that's not thinking like a Pelagial.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dead Princes seemed far more like a kind of oracle/speaker for the Whispers type of thing in CotD: West to me, their main focus being minion cult-making through thaumaturgic weird science, but i do see how easily such a thing might be done in their case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212169#post1212169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the future, I know Lea is pretty against Star Trek style &quot;bumpy forehead aliens&quot; in Exalted and I believe that in the Ask The Developers thread the Lintha have been noted to be the result of a Primordial mingling her blood with humans rather than an entirely different species.</div> </div> </div> </div>More of a Howardian &quot;decadent dying race&quot; take, akin to Stygians, Zamorans, atlantean remnants or others than D&amp;D-esque &quot;race as bumpy forehead alien in fantasy&quot;? I can dig that for certain, it might even resonate better with some of the Blood &amp; Salt fluff, imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:01:32-07:00","id":1212280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212165#post1212165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy your response, Epee - even though I land on the opposite end of the spectrum! =)[LIST][*]<b>Non-human races side-step real-life baggage.</b><br /> <br /> I work with a director who <i>loathes</i> magical realism and fantasy - even if a film sells well, he can't grasp why. And I stress - over and over - that fantasy is good <b>because</b> it is divorced from real-life preconceptions. Do a realistic play with realistic people and viewers will insert their own real-life experiences into the story.<br /> <br /> But add Orcs or Gnomes or Golems? - <i>that's new</i>. Preconceptions and stereotypes <i>have</i> to go out the window. <b>And then</b> you can have a conversation about real-world social problems without the knee-jerk: &quot;you can't say that about Dwarves!&quot; or &quot;this is a negative stereotype about Goblins!&quot; or &quot;are you saying Elves don't have problems?&quot;\u200b Marvel uses Mutants as stand-ins for issues of race, gender, etc <i>and it works wonderfully</i> because it's unexpected when the fantasy-lessons line-up to real-life relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>To each their own, however I think Mutants are also...how shall I say...<i>terrrible</i> metaphors for real life racial concerns. I'm not saying fantasy can't preform this role, its just rarely done well. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212165#post1212165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.[*]<b>Non-human races <i>shouldn't</i> always be the centerpiece</b><br /> <br /> I get what you mean about differences among humans. I can discern a Cuban, Puerto Rican and Dominican <i>-</i> a Columbian vs Venezuelan - a Mexican vs Honduran - a Jamaican vs Haitian - a Lebanese vs Omani. I love my city even if most Americans see &quot;uh, Latino&quot; or &quot;White?&quot; or &quot;Black!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>But</b> the typical English-speaker <b>won't</b> see those differences - and it'll be difficult for the ST to portray it - let alone for players to then grasp it. So why deliberately avoid a useful tool?<br /> <br /> So Orcs serve a purpose in LOTR that Humans <b>never</b> could. Because as humans (in the theater) viewing the enemy from the perspective of humans (on the battlefield), <i>one glance at the Orcs</i> and you know they're <b>not-of-your-tribe</b>. Games like Warcraft have 8 Troll, 5 Elf and a half-dozen splinter variants - <b>all related</b> - but the typical lvl 15 Human will only see &quot;Trolls = Bad, Night Elves = Friend, Blood Elves = uh.... badish?&quot;. The cultural and biological evolution of the Troll-Elven species <b>is irrelevant</b> to a story about &quot;Warcraft&quot; or &quot;Battle for Azeroth&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> Have you played the Elder Scrolls? Humans have 4+ distinct races - elves have more,etc - and each <i>mechanical set</i> of racial bonuses helps explain culture (Nords in the cold; Bretons using spells; Imperials being diplomats/charmers, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in brief: I think if your going to do a non-human race in exalted they must, absolutely must have a purpose in the narrative.Giving mechanical stats to what are phenotypical differences, and making culture a part of character biology is irksome, and not well thought out, and IMHO rather dull. Elder Scrolls has fun races/species (give me my necromancer slug men damnit), and has some weird stuff going on with its elves(side note, I think someone in the headcanon thread has an origin of elves in exalted as Szorney imitating Autothcon, by using metal to bind fae? I think?Go check that out). But if I were porting it over Tameriel,I'd drop most of the racial bonuses. There's something deeply uncomfortable for me of having a culture that is baked into every character, in an irreversible way (why are all imperials silver tonuged? What does it mean to be an 'Imperial'? Do they have mandatory speech and debate classes in every imperial village? etc).<br /> <br /> Now, your talking more about Elves Dwarves Orcs tc. One sec.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212165#post1212165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.[*]<b>Non-human races serve as useful shorthand</b><br /> <br /> I've had couple (and thankfully no more) <i>unfortunate</i> Exalted games where - since &quot;we're all human, we're all Solars&quot; - we eventually concluded with some variant of the &quot;Lawful Stupid&quot; Zenith smites the morally dubious Night/Twilight/Eclipse Castemate. Heresy &quot;offends most&quot; when it resembles your own default faith/assumptions (in this case, the Zenith's player believed all Solars were virtuous heroes - so &quot;something was clearly wrong&quot; with characters who didn't honor that trope).<br /> <br /> <i>Conversely</i>, I've had these situations dodged in D&amp;D. You hear something like &quot;we don't allow Tieflings because....&quot; or &quot;my Paladin hates Tieflings&quot; (and then you can play something else - or explain why the Tiefling should be an exception because... yadda yadda).<br /> <br /> And if approved, it eliminates the presumption that &quot;we look alike, therefore we think alike&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zenith ...smite ...only works on CoD. I...I'm a bit confused here. Are you saying that a diversity of apperances helps avoid players assuming that other players work with you? I think prejudices against actual other ethnic groups might solve that(or hell, in the case of Tiefling, do demon blooded). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212165#post1212165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my Tiefling was approved - another went Half-Orc - the rest either Human or Half-Elf? Great! <i>No one was ever upset OOC</i> when the Orc was spectacularly violent - nor surprised when I was scheming. Instead of being held to human-standards of behavior, we were eternally <i>the foreigners</i>, so they judged us as such (even embracing the Orc as someone to send to combat - as opposed to a &quot;maniac human&quot; who needs to be less aggressive).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, now I get what you mean. I think to a degree that this short hand isn't entirely necessary (especially for the Orc version--Most people assume that the Viking Beserker is gonna be the same.) But I get what you mean. Fantasy races serve as a character trope marker, and thus signal what kind of character your going to play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212165#post1212165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>DJALA </b><br /> Skin Color, Longevity, Small, Enlightened Essence - human - but really, <i>most of the Crafted Race descriptions</i> read like <i>Histories</i>. They're useful but feel dry. I want to know their culture, norms, gods - not their Usurpation-era legal status changes. I've never <b>felt</b> <i>how to use them.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd need to check, but I'm pretty sure they are now <i>just</i> humans with an odd skin tone. Enlightend Essence definitly got cut.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212165#post1212165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>OTHERS:</b><br /> <b>Graceful Wicked Masques, pg 22 : </b><br /> For similar reasons and a host of others, none of the early sentient races of Creation appealed for very long to the raksha. The <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>alaun </b></span>were too devoted to their Primordial masters and too willing to sacrifice their desires in pursuit of their masters\u2019 favor. The <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>scathacs </b></span>intrigued the raksha, but only until the raksha revealed the false complexity of a scathac mind as just a morass of competing lesser desires deriving from each scathac\u2019s component selves. The appetites of the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>mazriki </b></span>seemed promising and taught the raksha much, but the mazriki\u2019s palates were too depressingly narrow to be worth the raksha\u2019s attention. The will of the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>t\u2019shay\u2019i </b></span>burned brightest of all, but the Dragon Kings all too rapidly hunted them to extinction. With each flare of interest and subsequent disappointment, the raksha turned away from Creation as best they could and returned their attention to their own desires. At least there, in the Wyld, their desires could not disappoint.<br /> <br /> So with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> The others seem to (mostly) be from the <b>Underworld </b>compass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhhh, I never touched Graceful Wicked Mask. Nice. Good to know.<br /> <br /> <br /> Allright, so instead of just critquing, I'm gonna talk about how Exalted uses pre-human races, its sources of inspiration, and how I use the few I have.<br /> <br /> Exaltd, as far as I can tell, uses non-humans that are distinctly...alien. In a lot of ways, non-human races(and most are prehuman), resemble demons. They're familair looking, but function completely differently, have unique anatomy, and senses/abillities. Your not going to mistake a non-human for a human(typically. The Lintha are...weird). So in general, other nonhumans are gonna be weird too. They are, fundamentally, alien. A dragon King has a life cycle that no human matches.<br /> <br /> Most nonhumans to me then work as communicating strange, alien worlds that are probably long gone or passing away (Oddly, Tolkien's idea of the elves fits here pretty well). Beastmen, no matter where they are, think like people. They are people. They work as people. Non-human groups are...not. They don't think about the world the same way, and never have.They can embody intreasting problems and philosphical thoughts (Dragon Kings, my faves still, have the intreasting notions of concrete memory of life times, with the result being that dying is less of a big deal to them).<br /> <br /> So when I say, a narrative purpose, I mean something where their activity couldn't just be done by humans. Why are the Giants of Dis giants and not people with the giant merit? If I wagered, its something to do with their cannibalistic tendencies and production of soul gems, tools unique to them. Mine were basically the Skesis.<br /> <br /> <br /> I had a group of vampiric hypno toads that fed people to a giant tree, in order for the people to become more toads, for instance. The party(or 1 memeber) convinced them to become more missonary/enlightment people then raiders, but that requiredlearning and understanding how the toads thought of themselves and the world in a way that just another human culture didn't. <br /> <br /> The other one I've touched on is ancient serpents, who were decadent and alchemically leaning rivals of the Dragon Kings, now long dead. I've not developed much past that for them.<br /> <br /> I'll also briefly say that Arms gave us a few more species if you have it (some six eyed sages, adn a race of subterranean worm people. Was that arms? Or am I thinking of another one?) <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:17:34-07:00","id":1212289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212280#post1212280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To each their own, however I think Mutants are also...how shall I say...<i>terrrible</i> metaphors for real life racial concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understatement! Marvel Mutants as metaphor for blacks/gays/other oppressed minority is <i>especially</i> shitty because, unlike in real life where these kinds of animosity are utterly irrational and unjustified, <i>I can't blame Marvel's humans for hating and fearing Marvel's mutants</i>. You don't go two weeks in the Marvel Universe without them blowing up a national monument or teleporting into the White House to threaten the President.<br /> <br /> If Marvel's humans are <i>half</i> as tired of mutant attacks as I am of school shootings, I pity them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-27-2018, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:36:57-07:00","id":1212299,"title":"","content":"Mutants are an <u><i><b>exceptionally shitty</b></i></u> stand-in for real-life minorities or other bigoted-people, because unlike mutants, homosexuals/blacks/insert minority here <u>can't</u> shoot lasers from their eyes, perfectly mimic the forms of other people, or whatever mutant-power you wish to show.<br /> <br /> People being afraid of mutants in that universe is <u>100% justified</u>. <br /> <br /> -deep breath-<br /> <br /> Sorry, people using that comparison is one of my berserk buttons. <br /> <br /> Back on topic:<br /> <br /> I'm not fond of trying to fit specific 'races' into specific holes. In fact, I usually go out of my way to disprove such racial &quot;stereotypes&quot;, both in my capacity as ST and when I played different races.<br /> <br /> Culture is just that, culture. A specific culture may be known for something, but take an individual (or even a group of people) outside of that culture, and you will realize that we are all just people. No more, no less.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:28:40-07:00","id":1212325,"title":"","content":"Should be noted that Lintha as they exist today are actually not anything to do wiht the Lintha of the past and their being non-human or not is implied as potentially propoganda in the <b>Blood &amp; Salt</b> depiction. A big thing I think with their &quot;not really human&quot; thing was that it was as I gather supposed to be an example of nationlaistic racism and how people in that mindset are very prone ot build up mythologies for themselves.<br /> <br /> 2e took a lot of the Lintha origin story they told themselves as fact, but seeing as Dukantha was an Exalt and they are human enough for most htings, I think what edition is being talked about and how much of htier origins are real or not should be kind of considered in a lot of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:00:58-07:00","id":1212340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212280#post1212280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are the Giants of Dis giants and not people with the giant merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHuh, I actually forgot about the Gigantes. I think there may be a few other instances of hinting at the presence of inhuman communities of intelligent beings.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, I'm also thinking that the conversation might be limiting itself byt hewing too closely to the vanilla Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bWho wants to try and talk through translating some of the principles of Gunstar Autochthonia and Heaven's Reach (as they pertain to this subject) into the basic setting of the dying world fantasy Creation governed by the Dragon Blooded and to which the Solars are returning?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:24:29-07:00","id":1212348,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll join those who are saying that Tolkien-esque elves and orcs and dwarves are ultimately just humans with mutations, no matter what unreasonable lifespans the elves are given.<br /> <br /> I like how Exalted is honest about it. <br /> <br /> Having different cultures, languages, and skin tones is enough to make a people alien. And the skin tones thing is optional: consider how other white people felt about the Vikings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-27-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:28:27-07:00","id":1212350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212340#post1212340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bHuh, I actually forgot about the Gigantes. I think there may be a few other instances of hinting at the presence of inhuman communities of intelligent beings.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, I'm also thinking that the conversation might be limiting itself byt hewing too closely to the vanilla Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bWho wants to try and talk through translating some of the principles of Gunstar Autochthonia and Heaven's Reach (as they pertain to this subject) into the basic setting of the dying world fantasy Creation governed by the Dragon Blooded and to which the Solars are returning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, I only remember the Soveriegns from Gunstar. Care to elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:35:51-07:00","id":1212352,"title":"","content":"I agree with many of the things others already wrote.<br /> <br /> I can understand &quot;race as a shorthand&quot;, &quot;race as a trope codifier&quot;, allowing everyone to be on the same page regarding what to expect from a character and their player.<br /> <br /> I'm still a little... unsure. Let me try to explain.<br /> <br /> The concept of race in fantasy was mainly born with Tolkien, and since he's so goddamn universal (you have to read it! It's incredible! Such mastery, such excellence, real literature etc) of course race has spread to all kinds of fantasy and even to science fiction and other creative writing/art/media/games... and so on.<br /> <br /> The problem of that concept is that Tolkien conflated race, culture, and ability. Hobbits are small and dexterous and have strong ties with the earth, and are thus naturally stealthy, and never study magic. Men are a race (I understand his need to avoid the term &quot;human&quot;, but I don't completely agree. <i>Menschen</i> would work, in German, but Modern English doesn't work like that). Elves are a race. Dwarves are a race. Orcs are a race. Some, like Aragorn, or the Uruk-Hai, have mixed ancestry. Unlike in real life, where race is a social construct, in Middle Earth race is an objective fact, an aspect of nature. Moreover, it dictates your culture, and your aptitudes. One could make the case that yes, they are races, since they can theoretically (and sometimes very practically) have offspring with one another. The reality is that Tolkien wrote in a very nasty historical period rife with misconceptions and terrible pseudoscience about race. And was inevitably (?) influenced by them. He wanted the elves and dwarves of Germanic tradition to interact with humans and his own hobbits, and the way he found to describe the differences between these creatures was to categorize them as different races. I'm quite sure he didn't really understood his mistake. In any case, the concept of race found in Tolkien is awfully flawed.<br /> <br /> But we worship him, so we create games meant to evoke his work. First of all Dungeons and Dragons. And since D&amp;D has enjoyed such an unprecedented success in fantasy and rpgs, the term race is still being used everywhere. D&amp;D itself, now in its 5th edition and with its popularity at stellar levels, still employs that term - race. Again, not to refer to its RL, social construct meaning, but to use it <i>exactly as Tolkien did</i> back in the day - an unscientific, clich\u00e9-ridden <i>mischung</i> of race (?), culture, and ability. Each &quot;race&quot; has certain physical features, <i>and</i> certain cultural traits, <i>and </i>certain aptitudes, quantified as modifiers to the base attributes and small laundry lists of special abilities. It doesn't matter if they derive from physiology, culture, education, habits - it's all the same. <i>Race</i>, as shorthand for... well, the <i>essence</i> of the character.<br /> <br /> I do understand it can be useful in a game, but it's still a contentious (and just plain wrong) definition. It breeds stereotypes. It teaches/reinforces gamers of all ages that different races have different abilities, <i>and even different moralities</i>. Orcs are evil. Of course orcs are also emphatically <i>not white</i>, savage, brutal, violent, and conventionally unattractive. While elves are most often white, conventionally attractive, cultured, magical, superior, good. But not the drow, they're evil. In fact they're black. But still conventionally attractive, unlike, it seems, <i>real Black people</i> - drow are black-skinned but with thin and delicate faces and bodies, slightly muscular but not musclebound, never even slightly chubby... I could go on but this is turning bitter, so let's not.<br /> <br /> Giving a fixed alignment to a fantasy race presents a world in which an entire culture/race/species can be monolithically good or evil, inherently. As what we play, watch, read, has a profound effect on our assumptions, that... is not a good thing. Not to add that imperialistic Europeans colonizing other continents often strived to portray the natives as not just <i>other</i>, not even just <i>subhuman</i>, but inherently <i>evil</i> (as great writer and racist Rudyard Kipling so famously wrote in &quot;The White Man's Burden&quot;: <i>half-devil and half-child</i>).<br /> <br /> This creates worlds structured along racial lines... not unlike Earth, and I don't need to specify how well that turned out for us. It's probably not intentional (although I know of many racist or sexist writers and designers, so... ?), but to constantly depict dark-skinned races as inherently evil only reinforces a narrative of white supremacy.<br /> <br /> But of course there's Drizzt do'Urden. Who, <i>despite</i> being <i>a dark elf, </i>has a conscience, and a sense of honor, and treats his friends well. Completely contrary to all expectations. Because by now you expect <i>all drow</i> to be rotten pieces of shit. He's an interesting character for a certain value of &quot;interesting&quot; - rogueish, nonconformist, sensitive, intelligent, eloquent, misunderstood, and above all, 1) a total badass, and 2) unerringly good. Drizzt is sometimes subjected to racism. But being racist against an Always Evil race of demon-worshipping slavers and murderers isn't exactly prejudice - even spells can reveal their evil, because it's <i>objective reality</i>. The one time you try a detect alignment on Drizzt (if you don't immediately charge him, because yo, dark elf), you'll think there's something wrong with the magic in this neck of the wood, or he's wearing an amulet hindering your efforts, or any of another dozen <i>justified</i> reactions. But no. Drizzt is <i>a credit to his race</i> - he rises above the many inherent flaws of the drow. How charming.<br /> <br /> It's not that Bob Salvatore didn't notice. He does, and tries to find ways to undermine the racist narrative of the D&amp;D worlds. He's just struggling with difficult odds. Some People of Color identify with a protagonist such as Drizzt and find that he helps them deal with the prejudice and abuse they suffer in meatspace. Others resent that drow in general and Drizzt in particular are always subjected to racism (no matter if justified by the warped narrative of these worlds), because it simply hits too close to home. Me, I think if elves naturally came in all skin colors and only some factions - political, criminal, religious or any other kind - engaged in demon-worshipping, enslavement or other traditionally villainous activities, not because of their skin color but because of their individual backgrounds, needs and propensities, then the worlds in question wouldn't be so jarring - they would be more similar to ours, in that even though people can have the stupidest preconceptions against a race, a gender, a sexuality, an age bracket, and so on, they are entirely unfounded. Things are never as simple as <i>that race is evil</i> (thank the gods).<br /> <br /> So... non-human races. What I'm advocating is: sure, why just humans? Creation is a world fashioned by beings we can scarcely imagine - who knows what wondrous alien life forms they've created? And there are beastfolks, who like standard humans come in a riot of different appearances and cultures - follow that example. There are Dragon Kings, who anatomically and psychologically are alien, but not so far removed from us as to not be understood, and through time have developed different societies in different places - some are sleeping down the ages in stasis chambers, some live with the gods in Yu-Shan. Maybe add more cultures, maybe don't make them all followers of the UCS, just to avoid generalizations, but the concept is good. There are the Air Folk, who were created with wings, but have different cultures and different races just like humans do, only their morphology allows them to fly, so they will by necessity differ from humans - but they'll still be, at heart, humans (or not?), and capable of all our fabled diversity (which is always the pitch when telling you about what makes humans special and different from other races... because they apparently have all been cloned from the same dna and brainwashed into the same homogenizing culture). Deconstruct the racist structures of traditional fantasy and bumpy-forehead-alien science fiction, embrace the new work being carried onward by new generations of writers and designers. Embrace the diversity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","user":"Roswynn","date":". 04-27-2018, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:37:14-07:00","id":1212353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212348#post1212348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll join those who are saying that Tolkien-esque elves and orcs and dwarves are ultimately just humans with mutations, no matter what unreasonable lifespans the elves are given.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMind, I'd say that works fairly well in the context of Tolkien's own cosmology, partially because those stories don't actually use the term &quot;human&quot; (which could really function as a stand-in for Children of Illuvatar in general more than Men specifically, even if Men were supposed to be the only form of human that &quot;still exist&quot;), and his priority was more on spiritual distinctions and how those affect their interactions with and experience of time and the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut hardly any of that can really be translated into the context of Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough, come to think of it... the Jadeborn are of course already an approximation of Tolkienesque elves and dwarves, appropriately translated to the setting's background. Depending on the kinds of rules that we ultimately get for them, one <i>could</i> conceivably alter their backstory and place in the setting so that they can have more prominent communities above ground, while retaining the distinctions of how they're born and how they experience the world.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how effectively they could be expected to transform the world if they were loose in it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:42:12-07:00","id":1212355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212350#post1212350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oooh, I only remember the Soveriegns from Gunstar. Care to elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSince both of those settings contained variations on space opera, they both involved humanity traversing the cosmos and encountering alien species. It was not a heavily elaborated upon element, with many only having names and others getting certain descriptions of how they looked, but they could be actively present in those settings because one was about the Realm being a spaceship convoy on the run from the Yozis through the infinite cosmos (and occasionally needing to engage in trade, diplomacy or conquest with encountered species for necessary resources), and the other was where humanity had spread across the cosmos in a vast star empire, encountering and incorporating various other species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:54:11-07:00","id":1212358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212352#post1212352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me, I think if elves naturally came in all skin colors and only some factions - political, criminal, religious or any other kind - engaged in demon-worshipping, enslavement or other traditionally villainous activities, not because of their skin color but because of their individual backgrounds, needs and propensities, then the worlds in question wouldn't be so jarring - they would be more similar to ours, in that even though people can have the stupidest preconceptions against a race, a gender, a sexuality, an age bracket, and so on, they are entirely unfounded. Things are never as simple as <i>that race is evil</i> (thank the gods).</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, there have been attempts in various works to rectify this.<br /> <br /> In the Realm there were sun elven kingdoms who feel to demon worship and breeding as part of a long period of geopolitical struggle with other elven nations.<br /> <br /> In Eberron the Drow are not evil and have multiple cultures with different magical and aesthetic traditions. The more traditional elves are split three ways between an island of necromancers, ancestor &quot;worshiping&quot; sort-of mongols, and old rich people integrated into the dominant human culture.<br /> <br /> Finally, in Pathfinder's Golarion there are dark skinned elves in the Mwangi Expanse where the dark skinned humans come from. The drow are mostly still evil though.<br /> (There are also &quot;barbarian&quot; tribes in Numeria who are more or less culturally identical kin-groups of orks or humans that get along with each other better than the civilized mostly human culture)<br /> <br /> These examples by no means undermine your point, only show that some people who work in development are aware of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:02:30-07:00","id":1212363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212355#post1212355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSince both of those settings contained variations on space opera, they both involved humanity traversing the cosmos and encountering alien species. It was not a heavily elaborated upon element, with many only having names and others getting certain descriptions of how they looked, but they could be actively present in those settings because one was about the Realm being a spaceship convoy on the run from the Yozis through the infinite cosmos (and occasionally needing to engage in trade, diplomacy or conquest with encountered species for necessary resources), and the other was where humanity had spread across the cosmos in a vast star empire, encountering and incorporating various other species.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant more what the races were...aw well, I'll dig up my shards book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:32:16-07:00","id":1212369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212358#post1212358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For what it's worth, there have been attempts in various works to rectify this.<br /> <br /> In the Realm there were sun elven kingdoms who feel to demon worship and breeding as part of a long period of geopolitical struggle with other elven nations.<br /> <br /> In Eberron the Drow are not evil and have multiple cultures with different magical and aesthetic traditions. The more traditional elves are split three ways between an island of necromancers, ancestor &quot;worshiping&quot; sort-of mongols, and old rich people integrated into the dominant human culture.<br /> <br /> Finally, in Pathfinder's Golarion there are dark skinned elves in the Mwangi Expanse where the dark skinned humans come from. The drow are mostly still evil though.<br /> (There are also &quot;barbarian&quot; tribes in Numeria who are more or less culturally identical kin-groups of orks or humans that get along with each other better than the civilized mostly human culture)<br /> <br /> These examples by no means undermine your point, only show that some people who work in development are aware of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know of them. Your first example are the Sun Elves (who are impossible elitist asses but somehow still count as good), they don't have a monolithic evil society though... still monolithic anyways.<br /> <br /> Your second example, sure, I like Eberron more than standard D&amp;D exactly because anyone could be of any alignment - good orcs, good red dragons, neutral drows... Again, they often have monolithic cultures (dwarves, halflings, gnomes, hobgoblins...) but the Aerenal and Valenar are very interesting cultures, I like them a lot. I just wish there were more material like that, even just in Eberron.<br /> <br /> As for Golarion, yes, there are <i>wild elves</i> (<i>rolls eyes</i>) in the Mwangi Expanse. I have different problems with Golarion (not just the mechanics, that's not what we're talking about) - they have whole human cultures based off of clich\u00e9s. The Varisians? Really, people, Roma are <i>not like that</i>. Sure, they have some divergent traditions of course, but they're mostly exactly like anyone else - I mean, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LPgvNlrBfb0&amp;list=PLuZfvuQUd_SYmtpy7MmXn1oD3_inkbJSS&amp;index=195&amp;t=0s\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is what a Roma looks like for chrissake. And D&amp;D's Vistani are even worse... Then we have the Keleshites, the Vudrani... stereotypical stand-ins for Arabs and Turks and for Indians, respectively. Why can't they accept every individual is different? Why are all Keleshites passionate and haughty? As for Africa - ahem, Garund, we have the Garundi (modernized Ancient Egyptians) and the Mwangi (all the Blacks of Garund in a single race with subraces for the roles of demon-worshipping slavers, sailors, almost-Egyptians-try-harder, and small shamanic tribalists... <i>sigh</i>).<br /> <br /> Oh and the art... can be good and diverse in both D&amp;D and Pathfinder, sure, but can also be full of white people, cheesecake girls, and so on. They're getting there. Slowly. It's not universally bad. But there's still a long road ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","user":"Roswynn","date":". 04-27-2018, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:28:31-07:00","id":1212386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212363#post1212363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I meant more what the races were...aw well, I'll dig up my shards book.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was at least one explicitly sapient kind of cephalopod. I think they were supposed to be capable of floating on air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:11:12-07:00","id":1212457,"title":"","content":"<b>So much to respond to! </b> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>re: Zenith Smite Solars</b><br /> I didn't mean the Zenith anima ability - but you basically hit it with the &quot;trope codifier&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Zenith thought <b>all Solars</b> adhered to the &quot;lawful, good, golden, nice&quot; trope - <b>therefore</b> he was upset at the non-lawful, non-good, non-golden, non-nine characters <i>existed</i>. He thought they were sabotaging the game - so in a fit of Limit Break, he bashed a circle-mates brains out.<br /> <br /> As you note, D&amp;D Races &amp; Classes are trope codifiers - so a zealous Paladin, a Tiefling Warlock and cuthroat Rogue might <i>dislike</i> each other IC, but OOC know what to accept (and give each other proper berth to avoid triggering each other).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>re: Species/Aliens vs Races vs Culture</b><br /> <br /> A huge issue seems to be the terminology.<br /> <br /> <b>A species</b> is what I think of sci-fi aliens and Exalted extinct &quot;races&quot; - biologically unrelated to one another. This is why &quot;aliens with funny foreheads&quot; fall flat - it breaks the immersion when most of us think alien-life will be utterly inhuman (which is why later sci-fi came up with the idea of progenitor-races &quot;seeding intelligent life&quot;, thus explaining us all as modified-animals)<br /> <br /> <b>A culture</b> is the pure fluff behavioral stuff. There is no &quot;American military race&quot;, but there <b>is </b>&quot;American military culture&quot;. There is &quot;gun culture&quot;, &quot;sub-cultures&quot;, etc. The cities of New York, Los Angeles and Miami all have different cultures.<br /> <br /> <b>A race</b> <b>is both</b>. It's not blood alone, it's not culture alone. <br /> <br /> And remember that the books used the Wyld to simulate evolution (ie, totem spirits of endangered animal species braving the Wyld hoping that their progeny might acquire a mutation or two that will allow them to adapt and survive).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> I see a lot of.... <i>American unease</i> with &quot;race&quot; in these posts - and I <i>understand</i> the unease if your conception of race is reduced to &quot;white, black&quot;, etc. But I disagree - and hope the convo remains healthy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Your skin color is not your race.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">It's impossible to &quot;embrace diversity&quot; by denying we are diverse.</span></b><br /> <br /> Turks don't confuse themselves with Armenians. The Japanese don't confuse themselves with Koreans or Chinese (and even Japanese-Americans are &quot;Gaijin&quot;). I can't imagine a Navajo, a Seminole and a Sioux think they're all &quot;the same&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Spain, Basques don't confuse themselves with Catalans, nor Madrile\u00f1os with Gallegos, nor Asturians with Canarians. (and these <b>aren't </b>just provincial names like &quot;New Yorker&quot; or &quot;Californian&quot; - there <b>are</b> physical and social traits associated with each). I have a friend whose family is <i>Canarian </i>- and I could tell <i>by the shape of his face</i>. My ethnonym (Gallego) <i>is used as a slur</i> by Madrile\u00f1os and yet <i>we take that as a point of pride</i> (and would view their ethnonym as the insult).<br /> <br /> Several of my friends took DNA tests (and the Spanish percentages were never &quot;generic Spanish&quot; nor &quot;generic European&quot; nor &quot;generic White&quot; - <b>you can see the region</b>). Same applies for our Latin American roots (you can't confuse a Puerto Rican, Mexican, Peruvian or Columbian &quot;native&quot; traces - they're distinct). We can <b>see</b> the differences even if Americans just see &quot;brown&quot;. <b>I certainly</b> don't need to worry about my gaming-group reducing the planet to 4-5 color-coded &quot;races&quot; (we're all migrants of mixed heritage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212280#post1212280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if I were porting it over Tameriel,I'd drop most of the racial bonuses. There's something deeply uncomfortable for me of having a culture that is baked into every character, in an irreversible way (why are all imperials silver tonuged? What does it mean to be an 'Imperial'? Do they have mandatory speech and debate classes in every imperial village? etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>You say &quot;speech and debate <b>classes</b>&quot; because that implies that these are <b>cultural</b> differences. They're not.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>(In ESO) Bretons</b> don't have mandatory &quot;magic classes&quot; - they're <i>part elven</i>. In Exalted terms, they're part God-Blooded. It doesn't matter if you want to be a farmer, a wizard, a bard or a warrior - these things have <b>nothing</b> to do with your heritage.<br /> <br /> <b>(In RL) the Bajau Laut</b> (Philipines, Malaysia, Indonesia) were part of articles that came out a week ago - <b>confirming</b> they are genetically adapted to the water (50% larger spleens vs their non-aquatic neighbors).<b> The Moken </b>(West Coast of Thailand) have swimmers who can <i>see twice as far</i> and <i>stay twice as long</i> underwater. The are <i>biologically and culturally</i> aquatic. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>This is awesome</i>. <i>This is a point of pride</i>. </span>In Exalted &amp; Real Life terms, they have a mutation and <i>no amount of swim classes</i> will enlarge your spleen to let you free dive 200ft like they do.<br /> <br /> <b>(In ESO)</b> <b>Nords</b> don't have &quot;nature survival &amp; combat classes&quot;. Their pre-history mentions Atmora <i>freezing over</i> (so they either had a mutation to thrive in the cold - <i>or died</i>). <b>Then</b> they had to fight the Falmer to live in Skyrim (so they either had another mutation that gave a bonus to combat - <i>or died</i>). &quot;Resist Frost&quot; and &quot;Battle Frenzy&quot; <b>aren't</b> cultural artifacts - they're natural selection killing off whoever doesn't breed true. Nature &amp; history don't care if you want to be a bard or a farmer - you are descended from frost-warriors - so you're a frost-warrior-turned-bard or a frost-warrior-turned-farmer, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>(In RL) the Inuit</b> have mutations (that 100% of their population has) that only 15% of Han Chinese and 2% of Europeans have - which help them thrive off their raw high-meat, high-fat diets. Conversely, the <b>Havasupai </b>(in Arizona) <i>grew sick from European foods. </i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Denying biological differences resulted in suffering</span> - as the Havasupai <i>lost teeth, became diabetic and a half-dozen other diseases</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bantu &amp; Benin</b> (sickle-cell anemia to resist Malaria); <b>the Kalenjin</b> &amp; other Nilotic peoples are runners (people have copied their diets, altitude &amp; other practices - but you can't copy biomechanics); even <b>Europeans</b> (digesting milk &amp; alcohol - and 1% being HIV immune due to plagues). <br /> <br /> <b>All of these are awesome - and none of them &quot;cultural&quot;. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I understand American concerns (I think) - </span></b>but none of these differences claim &quot;superiority&quot;. Twenty different LATAM countries can see the differences in one another (and have rivalries) without anyone claiming to be a master race. <br /> <br /> In Spain, the same applies to regions - the Catalans are industrious/dour economical/stingy; the Gallegos are blunt/curt dumb/honest brutes/strong (Orcs!); the Madrile\u00f1os think they brought &quot;civilization&quot; unto everyone else (snooty/high-class, manipulative/leaders); etc - <b><i>everyone</i></b> likes to pretend they're better, but it's on part with a Dwarf, an Orc and a High Elf forming a group (they're still a group - Galician-Orcs aren't trying to wage genocide on High-Elven-Madrile\u00f1os, nor are Catalan-Dwarves trying to replace Basque-Druids).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212280#post1212280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are all imperials silver tonuged? What does it mean to be an 'Imperial'? Do they have mandatory speech and debate classes in every imperial village? etc).</div> </div> </div> </div><b>(In ESO) Imperials</b> I'd liken to <b>Roman</b> or <b>Latin</b> people (their obvious inspiration). There are 20~ Spanish countries, a few other Latin-cousins (Italians, Portuguese, etc), and I mentioned our Jamaican, Haitian, Middle-Eastern populations (and the ever-so-exotic &quot;Americans&quot;). The Romans <i>were great</i> at assimilating &quot;European barbarians&quot; and the Spanish strove to emulate the model (intermixing and creating a dozen syncretic cultures).<br /> <br /> I never took &quot;speech classes&quot; to learn the differences - I'm <b>not</b> especially social - but <i>I'd slap myself</i> if I ever committed some of the faux pas I've seen Anglo-American tourists commit. You grow up surrounded by different peoples and <b>need</b> to learn the nuances. Meeting &quot;Middle Easterners&quot; was <i>new</i> for me in College, but they have a lot of similarities (even our mother tongues share links in syntax and vocabulary).<br /> <br /> And English-speakers find <b><i>words</i></b> offensive - Spanish-speakers listen to <b><i>tone</i></b>. You might not understand Japanese or Arabic <b>words</b> but you can always pick up <b>tone</b>.<br /> <br /> It does <b>not</b> stretch my imagination that a race (<b>the Imperials</b>) living in a central-location surrounded by multiple races will <b>naturally</b> have more nuance for cultural differences - that the more isolated or war-like Nords, Reguards and Bretons don't. Imperials aren't &quot;silver tongued&quot; because they took classes - they're &quot;silver tongued&quot; <i>because everyone else talks like an idiot</i> with foreigners. The Altmer don't seem to notice their eugenicism terrifies others - the Bosmer come across like cannibals - the Dunmer religion shocks tourists - Redguards &amp; Nords are too busy picking fights to learn social charms. <b>The Imperial gift</b> is being less assholes than the isolated bumpkins that surround them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <hr /><br /> <b>re: Race as Trope Markers</b><br /> <br /> I really like the 3E Lintha clarification you folks point to - and by extension, all this mulling on Elder Scrolls races. I'm liking this &quot;nationalistic racism&quot; and &quot;propaganda&quot; angle a lot. Less mechanical difference (except maybe a few mutations). No need for &quot;Orcs, Dwarves, Elves&quot; with unique origin stories - when &quot;humans adapted to different environments&quot; are fitting (and they don't need to live in the far-flung corners of the Bordermarches for this benefit). <br /> <br /> The Snake People in An-Teng <b>are a race</b>. No one thinks of them as &quot;Beastmen&quot; - they're seen a distinct local race.<br /> <br /> The Lintha <b>are a race</b>. No one thinks about magic-mechanics of being altered-humans or not. A couple aquatic mutations could suffice for humans to make up completely fictitious histories for this &quot;magical&quot; race.<br /> <br /> The Sijanese? <b>Are a race</b>. Without making them all ghost-blooded, it'd suffice to give 1-2 mutations or merits that might be shadowland related (representing a <i>lifetime</i> among the dead that no mere tourist or migrant will acquire overnight).<br /> <br /> The people of Great Forks? <b>Are a race</b>. Without making them all god-blooded, it'd suffice to give 1-2 mutations or merits in the vein of Bretons (from Elder Scrolls). <br /> <br /> <b>They're all human</b>.<br /> <br /> But one could easily &quot;build racial tropes&quot; (the way Orcs, Dwarves, Elves, etc have them) representing stereotypes (that have grains of truth in them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T22:22:11-07:00","id":1212536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212175#post1212175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I tried importing Thedas, the Dragon Age setting, into Exalted so it exists elsewhere on inverted cardinal directions to Creation (so secret paths say East in Creation will Bring you to the West of Thedas and the North of Creation could bring you to the South of Thedas) upon the back of a lost Primordial The Fade whose Fetiche Soul is the Golden City Turned Black. So I played with how to do them in the Exalted setting so Dwarves are a civilization descended from the Mountainfolk/Human Godblooded. Elves are descended from the Raksha/Gods, and the Qunari are Primordial Race tied to Dragons somehow, which there I have as corporeal forms of Devas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this &quot;adding into Exalted's Creation&quot; <b>or </b>&quot;playing the Dragon Age setting but using Exalted mechanics and terms&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212175#post1212175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I also include Moogles from Final Fantasy in the Form of the Kupo, mostly in the proportions you see in FF12. They are an extinct race that was pretty much genocided during the Primordial War, but some still exist as living dreams, or in stasis awakening in the Time of Tumult. I have it their souls naturally materialize into Magicite a rare magical material that is crystalline rather then the smelted soulsteel of men. They develop along a double job caste system where they develop a primary Career and a secondary Career which defines it more both broadening and narrowing their roles. They can develop Merits based on these, comparable to say the supernatural merits of Sorcerers or simple charms.<br /> <br /> I have the Nu Mou and Seeq also existing but haven't really got to introduce them and still working on their soul mechanics. Probably something simple for the Seeq,and mysterious for the Nu Mou. I also have the Shumi, from FF8, that are pacifist spiritualists who were made by the primordial to be constantly evolving and reincarnating. Basically their soul has the capacity to transform into the soul of another depending on their nature, so they could reincarnate as a human or even a Dragon King's immortal soul, or the innocent Godsouled Moomba.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, I hate cute shit, lol. But I can think of a player who would revel in that.<br /> <br /> How did they.... fit in? Intelligent pets? Could they speak a tongue and communicate with humans? What was their purpose for existing? Were they just a fun Easter Egg or Expy - or did you work them in to contribute something grander?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212175#post1212175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have the Bangaa which which I have using an inverted soul structure to humans in their Po is the main soul and the Hun is the lesser one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So.... feral, human-shaped animals that turn into intelligent zombies? How'd they work? What was their purpose?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212175#post1212175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also include the Krogan from Mass Effect, as basically having a redundant soul structure of two heart souls and four lower souls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212175#post1212175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have other unique species I've made, like an Underdark race called the Arthax that evolved after some of the subcaste species died off other castes replaced it. Different castes have different souls based on Ren (True Name), Shadow, Heart, and Memory.<br /> <br /> I've played around with the idea of a Deviant civilization of Darkbrood that basically are an amalgamation of multiple extinct and mutated species that now result in each generation being a different species then their parents or siblings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely feel I saw something like this in Marvel comics - perhaps pre-Inhumans? Or hell, the Zerg from Starcraft assimilating other races.<br /> <br /> <b>But my chief question to all of these are - </b>what did you get out of them?<br /> <br /> Did players catch the references? Did they need to? Was their existence a part of the setting (or something thrown in later for fun)?<br /> <br /> Were these playable? Antagonists? Allies?<br /> <br /> How did human NPCs interact? The players? <br /> <br /> I'm intrigued that you went with non-D&amp;Dish tropes - so what do you think worked (or didn't work)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T22:34:19-07:00","id":1212540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>A race</b> <b>is both</b>. It's not blood alone, it's not culture alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be pedantic, but I'm probably going to come off as pedantic - sociologically speaking, the concept you're talking about is more ethnicity than race. Ethnicity is shared ancestry identified by cultural markers. Race is harder to define specifically because the concept is based on debunked pseudo-science (while physical common traits can be generalized to ancestry from different regions of the world, we know now there is greater biological difference between two different tribal communities in subsaharan Africa than between Europeans and Aboriginal Australians - racial categories are complete social constructs that were defined in order to justify imperialism) - but as a social construct it still majorly impacts people's lives and thus can not be ignored by anyone engaged with reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T22:48:45-07:00","id":1212543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212352#post1212352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... non-human races. What I'm advocating is: sure, why just humans? Creation is a world fashioned by beings we can scarcely imagine - who knows what wondrous alien life forms they've created? And there are beastfolks, who like standard humans come in a riot of different appearances and cultures - follow that example. There are Dragon Kings, who anatomically and psychologically are alien, but not so far removed from us as to not be understood, and through time have developed different societies in different places - some are sleeping down the ages in stasis chambers, some live with the gods in Yu-Shan. Maybe add more cultures, maybe don't make them all followers of the UCS, just to avoid generalizations, but the concept is good. There are the Air Folk, who were created with wings, but have different cultures and different races just like humans do, only their morphology allows them to fly, so they will by necessity differ from humans - but they'll still be, at heart, humans (or not?), and capable of all our fabled diversity (which is always the pitch when telling you about what makes humans special and different from other races... because they apparently have all been cloned from the same dna and brainwashed into the same homogenizing culture). Deconstruct the racist structures of traditional fantasy and bumpy-forehead-alien science fiction, embrace the new work being carried onward by new generations of writers and designers. Embrace the diversity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agreed with all of your post deconstructing Tolkien's impact on the genre, but I disagree here, because I think the better path for Exalted to deconstruct the Tolkien/D&amp;D tropes around race is embracing endless morphological diversity of humanity in the setting, rather than treating &quot;humans&quot; as a distinct race among others. Sure there are exceptions like the Dragon Kings, but they're by design a fringe element, relics of a lost past before the human era. Air Folk are just human beings with wings, with all the diversity being human implies, not a separate species. Making Air Folk a different species would just be a more extreme case of &quot;bumpy forehead alien&quot;. To justify not being human, a type of being would have to be far more different from human than can be reflected by mutations, merits &amp; flaws, as Air Folk, Pelagrothopes, all Beastmen, Arczekhi, Djala, etc etc can.<br /> <br /> A being entirely made out of a hive-mind insect swarm, with the ability to co-locate, and a fluid self-identity allowing it to merge with/consume/be consumed by other colony entities of its kind... that justifies a different species from human. A human-sized mortal being morphologically different from humans of our world so it can climb walls and spin webs... that's just a Beastman or Mutant (mechanically speaking, in-setting it could just be thought of as another &quot;people&quot;, without the origin of their morphology ever needing to be nailed down), and has a human soul fully capable of Exalting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-28-2018, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T23:08:26-07:00","id":1212544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was this &quot;adding into Exalted's Creation&quot; <b>or </b>&quot;playing the Dragon Age setting but using Exalted mechanics and terms&quot;? </div> </div> </div><br /> Thedas was a place that could be reached via mysterious means, they never got around to going to it, but one of the players made a character from it that Exalted when in Creation. It was mainly a method to help someone who didn't know the setting to create someone from a fictional culture they knew of.<br /> <br /> It was a fun fictional set of cultures I thought was done well so I could mine their setting if they go there, and they can experience what it would be like to be Exalted against some setting they know of, to help show power levels and what not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ugh, I hate cute shit, lol. But I can think of a player who would revel in that.<br /> <br /> How did they.... fit in? Intelligent pets? Could they speak a tongue and communicate with humans? What was their purpose for existing? Were they just a fun Easter Egg or Expy - or did you work them in to contribute something grander? </div> </div> </div>They didn't get to experience them thoroughly but by the next storyline before Hiatus I was going to have a Kupo join as an NPC<br /> <br /> Most have either a native Major language group, multiple 1/4th dialects, or both, but they also usually had Old Realm since they were from the Time of Glory.<br /> <br /> They were a fun NPC, were pretty tiny so they were like an intelligent 3 Footish species and had better technology then most humans now. They are to show inhuman civilizations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So.... feral, human-shaped animals that turn into intelligent zombies? How'd they work? What was their purpose? </div> </div> </div>They were a prehuman civilization that showed how many civilizations are degenerate or extinct now. They were Warriors and more inclined to being Berserkers or martial artists. And showing how hidden corners of Creations, and otherworlds adrift in the Wyld have multiple prehuman relics. They also showed like many of the ones I created that not everyone has human style souls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ha! </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I vaguely feel I saw something like this in Marvel comics - perhaps pre-Inhumans? Or hell, the Zerg from Starcraft assimilating other races. </div> </div> </div>Yeah they were a wink to the Deviants from Marvels, the foes of the Eternals and Creations of the Celestials. I liked the idea of an unstable civilizations that horribly mutated and how they adapt, and how they can be covetous of wanting the Surface, or even exist under the Earth without war with Mountain Folk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><b>But my chief question to all of these are - </b>what did you get out of them?<br /> <br /> Did players catch the references? Did they need to? Was their existence a part of the setting (or something thrown in later for fun)?<br /> <br /> Were these playable? Antagonists? Allies?<br /> <br /> How did human NPCs interact? The players? <br /> <br /> I'm intrigued that you went with non-D&amp;Dish tropes - so what do you think worked (or didn't work)?</span><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was satisfying if they caught the reference, even if they didn't catch em immediately, it then became a geek touchstone. But I try to have everything part of the Setting, nothing exists in a Vacuum what what.<br /> <br /> They were often allies, but could be antagonists.<br /> <br /> <br /> How did human NPCs interact? You mean with the Primordial Races? Well humans were often superstitious and ignorant. If they were scary looking species they would view them as monsters. If they were things you could easily underestimate they would. Some would figure they would make great trade connections. Players are fickle, often depending on how they stumble upon them. They often couldn't tell what was a god or a monster or whatever unless they discovered enough info. One of the Players wants to probably steal a Kupos skyship if they can find and repair it.<br /> <br /> It was fun, I'm more of a Final Fantasy and what not fella rather then the DnD guy. I felt DnD were forced stereotypes and often when interacting with DnD forums they often seem upset that I call into question why we need both Halflings, Dwarves, and Gnomes... Or why you can't just play Orcs rather then Half Orcs. I just find it fun to make different cultures, and many of the inhumany things are often just humans anyways like Beastman or a culture of Godblooded of somekind.<br /> <br /> Like I had a miniture Heaven of Godblooded that live atop a giant mountain with their God Parents. They didn't view themselves as humans, more like lesser gods, and their Heaven didn't reveal to the region that they are not the real heaven, and most never heard of Yu-Shan. They were mostly spoiled cultured people with skin the color of the sky and clouds and had a tendancy for little blessings like the ability to speak to birds, or their feet never touched the ground, and they lived like twice as long as most humans.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T23:25:24-07:00","id":1212547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212540#post1212540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to be pedantic, but I'm probably going to come off as pedantic - sociologically speaking, the concept you're talking about is more ethnicity than race. Ethnicity is shared ancestry identified by cultural markers. Race is harder to define specifically because the concept is based on debunked pseudo-science (while physical common traits can be generalized to ancestry from different regions of the world, we know now there is greater biological difference between two different tribal communities in subsaharan Africa than between Europeans and Aboriginal Australians - racial categories are complete social constructs that were defined in order to justify imperialism) - but as a social construct it still majorly impacts people's lives and thus can not be ignored by anyone engaged with reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><i>I love pendantic! </i></b><br /> <br /> And English isn't my primary tongue - so I love nuance!<br /> <br /> I always thought the dichotomy was <b>race-as-color</b> vs <b>race-as-culture</b>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><b>Race-as-Color :</b> Northern Europeans (usually). The whole &quot;sons of Noah&quot; schtick (Whites descend from Japheth ; Blacks from Ham ; Reds from Shem). <b>Then</b> as the world-map grew, Red was shuffled around, Yellow added in and Brown most recently. It's pure phenotype.</li> <li><b>Race-as-Culture : </b>Southern Europeans (usually). Emulating the Romans (and their assimilation of non-Roman barbarians) - language, culture, clothing, etc was prioritized. So we had &quot;black&quot; conquistadors - <i>by the thousands</i> - who got rich raiding the Incas or assaulting French incursions. If they <i>spoke Spanish</i> and <i>dressed Spanish</i> then they were <i>Spanish </i>(a thousand times more than an English or French or German could ever be). LATAM even had laws aimed at alienating/disgusting English/French.<br /> .<ul><li>This is further strengthened by how mixed our families are. I have a &quot;white, blond, blue-eyed&quot; aunt who gave birth to a &quot;black&quot; female - and in turn, my cousin then birthed a &quot;white, dirty-blond, green-eyed&quot; - by American standards, my cousin is a different race than her own mother and child? Americans tend to think we all &quot;brown out to an average&quot; instead of &quot;reshuffled and roll the genetic dice&quot;. Or that somehow a &quot;black&quot; Cuban has more connection to Black-American culture than (any other color) Hispanics? Mind boggling.</li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Anyways.<b> I appreciate the difference! </b><br /> <br /> Maybe both ideas are useful?<br /> <br /> <b>Ethnicity</b> to make paragraph-sized regional blurbs (with a couple merits/mutations) befitting the unusual conditions they live in.<br /> <br /> And then a separate section of <b>Races</b> (which are just ethnicities disguised as magical &quot;others&quot; if we need to &quot;foreignize&quot; groups like the Lintha or Snakemen as neither common nor accepted). Or maybe a couple legitimately inhuman ones (although I struggle to think of a useful purpose for them, the more I mull it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 04-28-2018, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T04:01:14-07:00","id":1212590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212543#post1212543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agreed with all of your post deconstructing Tolkien's impact on the genre, but I disagree here, because I think the better path for Exalted to deconstruct the Tolkien/D&amp;D tropes around race is embracing endless morphological diversity of humanity in the setting, rather than treating &quot;humans&quot; as a distinct race among others. Sure there are exceptions like the Dragon Kings, but they're by design a fringe element, relics of a lost past before the human era. Air Folk are just human beings with wings, with all the diversity being human implies, not a separate species. Making Air Folk a different species would just be a more extreme case of &quot;bumpy forehead alien&quot;. To justify not being human, a type of being would have to be far more different from human than can be reflected by mutations, merits &amp; flaws, as Air Folk, Pelagrothopes, all Beastmen, Arczekhi, Djala, etc etc can.<br /> <br /> A being entirely made out of a hive-mind insect swarm, with the ability to co-locate, and a fluid self-identity allowing it to merge with/consume/be consumed by other colony entities of its kind... that justifies a different species from human. A human-sized mortal being morphologically different from humans of our world so it can climb walls and spin webs... that's just a Beastman or Mutant (mechanically speaking, in-setting it could just be thought of as another &quot;people&quot;, without the origin of their morphology ever needing to be nailed down), and has a human soul fully capable of Exalting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embracing endless morphological diversity in humanity sounds great! And you're right, Air Folk are human - artificially mutated humans. They could be thought of as <i>transhuman</i> - human baseline with genetic engineering - but then, are for instance the Bajai Laut and Moken that Salagimsim mentions transhuman too, because of their useful mutations? Let's just agree that &quot;human&quot; is a much bigger, varied category than traditionally assumed. It does work for Exalted, with its beastfolk, created races and so on.<br /> <br /> I'm not advocating treating humans as a different race among others! If that's what you took away from my post, then I definitely didn't explain myself well enough. At most, humans would be a different <i>species</i>, and I'm <i>not sure</i> I want a lot of other species in Creation. As you say, the Dragon Kings work because they're so fringe, a lost civilization from before humanity. The Raksha and other Fair Folk, like hobgoblins, are totally alien creatures - they're still people, but they're definitely not just &quot;bumpy-forehead aliens&quot; - they're <i>truly, frighteningly </i>alien. Sure, they share superficial traits with humans, but they're still really <i>other</i>. And that of course doesn't bring with it a moral judgment (no alignment in Exalted, thank the gods).<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of diversity in Exalted - in the more typical human cultures and ethnicities, as well as in the more fantastically mutated varieties - be it because of the influence of the Wyld, of First Age genetic engineering, or something else entirely. I love it, it's wonderful.<br /> <br /> Then again your co-locating, fluid-identity, hive-minded insect swarms are <i>fascinating</i>. I'm not saying, let's have tons of alien species fill the setting and work, fight, pray and love together with humans. It's much more impactful if really <i>different</i> beings (your swarms, Mountain Folk, Dragon Kings, Fair Folk, Darkbrood, Primordial... &quot;races&quot; - heh, can't have it all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) have their personal niches. Precise brush strokes to highlight contrast. Mind-blowing new ideas. If these alien beings came <i>in as much variety as humans,</i> well then I'd be on Cloud 9. But I'm totally fine already.<br /> <br /> The <i>least </i>thing I want is for <i>all of Creation</i> to turn into generic human/elf/dwarf fantasy setting #821 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","user":"Roswynn","date":". 04-28-2018, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T09:20:09-07:00","id":1212695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>So much to respond to! </b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You stirred the hornets' nest! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>re: Zenith Smite Solars</b><br /> I didn't mean the Zenith anima ability - but you basically hit it with the &quot;trope codifier&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Zenith thought <b>all Solars</b> adhered to the &quot;lawful, good, golden, nice&quot; trope - <b>therefore</b> he was upset at the non-lawful, non-good, non-golden, non-nine characters <i>existed</i>. He thought they were sabotaging the game - so in a fit of Limit Break, he bashed a circle-mates brains out.<br /> <br /> As you note, D&amp;D Races &amp; Classes are trope codifiers - so a zealous Paladin, a Tiefling Warlock and cuthroat Rogue might <i>dislike</i> each other IC, but OOC know what to accept (and give each other proper berth to avoid triggering each other).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well the reaction of the Zenith's player wasn't very mature, nor very genre-savvy. Even though it's not obvious for many new players, it's better to talk out problems with your group than go berserk and attack them. I wonder if there is some value in D&amp;D's trope-codifying categorization. As you previously said, you can have a glance at the main Ixalan playable races/main characters and decide if that's the game for you. I really appreciate the direction MtG is going towards, all this explicitly non-white, non-eurocentric, beautiful settings, but... don't we already have that in Exalted? Excluding the different exaltations and the fact they become super-tropes overlayed on your cultural, racial, personal tropes, there are a lot of different cultures and races. Harborhead has 5 ethnicities of Black people (some of which in 2e had their skin color described in terms of food... <i>sigh</i>), and they have different cultures that still are very influenced by the national character. An-Teng, which you mentioned, has a lot of cultural diversity too. Greyfalls has many ethnicities, mostly slightly mutated by the Wyld iirc, and the DBs are playing one against the others. This is <i>interesting, cool</i> stuff. <i>Diverse</i> stuff. All these different cultures are small trope codifiers too and there's a lot of them, all over Creation - and they're still all humans.<br /> <br /> I think stereotypes tend to be harmful in discussing race (I might be wrong, I can see how they might also be useful... perhaps), but when you play Exalted you do retain some trope-codifiers. My Haslanti fights with a crossbow, because they have such an important place in Haslanti martial culture and bows are just too difficult and cumbersome for her. She hates slavery though, which distinguishes her from most other Haslanti. Her mother is an Icewalker godblooded shaman, but she's not godblooded and her father's work with technology and wonders extricated from the ruins of Bagrash Kol's realm has always been her main fascination. And so on - essentially, being from the Haslanti League gives you a culture, a trope-codifier. Then you customize your character from there, deciding exactly what matters to them, what they like, what they dislike, how they see other cultures, etc. I think it's useful and gives you a very good substitute for D&amp;D's class/race/background. I love that they added backgrounds in this edition, it allows a lot of flavorful customization - there was something similar in 4e too, although not right from the start - but I still see class as too limiting and artificial (in 2e heroic mortals could belong to archetypes and professions related to the main 5 almost-universal castes, but that didn't limit you, it gave you bonuses if you qualified)... and race, well. We'll talk about it later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><hr /><br /> <b>re: Species/Aliens vs Races vs Culture</b><br /> <br /> A huge issue seems to be the terminology.<br /> <br /> <b>A species</b> is what I think of sci-fi aliens and Exalted extinct &quot;races&quot; - biologically unrelated to one another. This is why &quot;aliens with funny foreheads&quot; fall flat - it breaks the immersion when most of us think alien-life will be utterly inhuman (which is why later sci-fi came up with the idea of progenitor-races &quot;seeding intelligent life&quot;, thus explaining us all as modified-animals)<br /> <br /> <b>A culture</b> is the pure fluff behavioral stuff. There is no &quot;American military race&quot;, but there <b>is </b>&quot;American military culture&quot;. There is &quot;gun culture&quot;, &quot;sub-cultures&quot;, etc. The cities of New York, Los Angeles and Miami all have different cultures.<br /> <br /> <b>A race</b> <b>is both</b>. It's not blood alone, it's not culture alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I know I should just shut up, because as a Person of Color you evidently can talk circles around me about race, but since I'm impossibly anal retentive... No? <i>Race is a social construct</i>. It's an <i>informal</i> taxonomic rank below subspecies. It <i>can </i>be useful, but is often incongrous and leading to biological essentialism, which is scientifically untenable (and disgusting). Among human beings, race has no scientific value - we're all <i>homo sapiens</i>. As glamourweavers says, what you're talking about is probably ethnicity - a category of people identifying with each other on the bases of shared language, culture, ancestry, society or nation. Other possibly useful classifications are populations (inhabitants of a specific place), peoples (the Frisian people, the Danish people, the Semitic people), or communities (social groups with something in common).<br /> <br /> Of course if you want to refer to something using the term <i>race</i> it's not anyone's business to tell you <i>naaah, wrong!! - </i>it's just that D&amp;D and other games are guilty of exactly the main problem with the term - <i>biological essentialism</i>. You're an orc, hence you're strong, tough, prone to rage, and evil. Thx no thx!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And remember that the books used the Wyld to simulate evolution (ie, totem spirits of endangered animal species braving the Wyld hoping that their progeny might acquire a mutation or two that will allow them to adapt and survive).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is interesting, although I don't know whether the devs will reiterate the point in 3e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see a lot of.... <i>American unease</i> with &quot;race&quot; in these posts - and I <i>understand</i> the unease if your conception of race is reduced to &quot;white, black&quot;, etc. But I disagree - and hope the convo remains healthy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I totally agree, I've always thought one of the great virtues of these forums is that they're almost always a safe space where people are decent and ethical. It's not all rainbows and unicorns (we're all human beings) but that's the trend I've spotted.<br /> <br /> And can I say how right you are? About American unease with race? Like totally. Actually, since I'm European, let's call it differently - <i>white unease</i>. We whites know we've messed up something awful in the past (and we still do, like a lot) and we're enormously uneasy with our treatment of PoC, native peoples and foreign sovereign nations. We can get downright irrational about it. White guilt. It's not a good thing, we should resign ourselves to the fact many of us were and are more rotten shits than the drow will ever be and at least learn something from that, like, trying to be less racist ourselves. But it's not easy. You see our oh-so-good intentions peeking through. We'd shut up people of color to have a chance to express how <i>deeply non-racist</i> we are... oh, and it's always about us of course, how ashamed we are of our colonialist/imperialist past, how sorry we are for various PoC... okay, you already know all this, I'll shut up now - for now the discussion seems to be quite healthy as you were saying, so as long as you and other people of color here are alright, it's all good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your skin color is not your race.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well... the two are related though?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">It's impossible to &quot;embrace diversity&quot; by denying we are diverse.</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, by the gods, that's not what I meant! Jesus, I really dropped the ball in the last part of my post there - sorry!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turks don't confuse themselves with Armenians. The Japanese don't confuse themselves with Koreans or Chinese (and even Japanese-Americans are &quot;Gaijin&quot;). I can't imagine a Navajo, a Seminole and a Sioux think they're all &quot;the same&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Spain, Basques don't confuse themselves with Catalans, nor Madrile\u00f1os with Gallegos, nor Asturians with Canarians. (and these <b>aren't </b>just provincial names like &quot;New Yorker&quot; or &quot;Californian&quot; - there <b>are</b> physical and social traits associated with each). I have a friend whose family is <i>Canarian </i>- and I could tell <i>by the shape of his face</i>. My ethnonym (Gallego) <i>is used as a slur</i> by Madrile\u00f1os and yet <i>we take that as a point of pride</i> (and would view their ethnonym as the insult).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But... that's not race? Turkey is a nation, Armenia is a nation, Japan is a nation... Navajo are a people (divided in tribes), Seminole are a people divided in tribes and informal groups, Sioux are a nation of various ethnic groups... I'm Italian, but that's not my race - if I had to tell you what my race is I'd probably say white caucasian? And still nations are very interesting, they're trope-codifiers all by themselves, it's cool stuff! It's part of your identity (whether I like it or not... meep!) and there are a lot of traits that depend on your nationality. Peoples and tribes and ethnic groups are even cooler, lots of trope-codifiers, lots of cultural differences, lots of different phenotypes... okay I've just loved foreign cultures since I was a little girl (and even distinct regional cultures within Italy!) but that's not here nor there, so I'll stop gushing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several of my friends took DNA tests (and the Spanish percentages were never &quot;generic Spanish&quot; nor &quot;generic European&quot; nor &quot;generic White&quot; - <b>you can see the region</b>). Same applies for our Latin American roots (you can't confuse a Puerto Rican, Mexican, Peruvian or Columbian &quot;native&quot; traces - they're distinct). We can <b>see</b> the differences even if Americans just see &quot;brown&quot;. <b>I certainly</b> don't need to worry about my gaming-group reducing the planet to 4-5 color-coded &quot;races&quot; (we're all migrants of mixed heritage).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Again, thank the gods. Although, the DNA differences between even a Swede and a Congolese are <i>superficial</i>, mostly - something about melanin, absorption rates of vitamin D, hair texture, bone structure, fat deposits... but on average we all have 99.9% of the same DNA as anybody else. So yeah, diversity - and also, equality. That tiny bit of DNA variance counts for all the diversity in ethnicity and heritage, but as for the rest we're also strikingly similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say &quot;speech and debate <b>classes</b>&quot; because that implies that these are <b>cultural</b> differences. They're not.<br /> <br /> <b>(In ESO) Bretons</b> don't have mandatory &quot;magic classes&quot; - they're <i>part elven</i>. In Exalted terms, they're part God-Blooded. It doesn't matter if you want to be a farmer, a wizard, a bard or a warrior - these things have <b>nothing</b> to do with your heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's absolutely true. I have a Breton character and even though she looks for all intents and purposes fully human she has a tiny sliver of elven blood in there. But should such a remote ancestral variation play such a big part in what she's capable of? I guess it comes down to preferences - if elven magic is a <i>big deal</i>, well, then probably yes, you might want to starkly differentiate a Breton from a Nord. Beware essentialism though... it would be nice if, say, Bretons had a slight affinity for magic on average, but that wasn't restricted to them, and any &quot;race&quot; could potentially produce the most powerful archmage possible (and iirc in the lore it's quite like that, as Shalidor was a Nord, which is totally playing against type).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(In RL) the Bajau Laut</b> (Philipines, Malaysia, Indonesia) were part of articles that came out a week ago - <b>confirming</b> they are genetically adapted to the water (50% larger spleens vs their non-aquatic neighbors).<b> The Moken </b>(West Coast of Thailand) have swimmers who can <i>see twice as far</i> and <i>stay twice as long</i> underwater. The are <i>biologically and culturally</i> aquatic. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i>This is awesome</i>. <i>This is a point of pride</i>. </span>In Exalted &amp; Real Life terms, they have a mutation and <i>no amount of swim classes</i> will enlarge your spleen to let you free dive 200ft like they do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is totally awesome and very eye-opening. I say in Exalted we could have some ethnicities with this kind of genetic adaptations too. After all, even just dark or light skin are genetic adaptations - more melanin protects your skin from the sun's UV radiations (a small bonus to Survival in savannas and hot deserts?), lighter skin lets more vitamin D pass through (ah, this would be more difficult to model - how do you treat &quot;hey I'm less predisposed to rickets and osteoporosis!&quot; as a game trait?... But you'd totally burn more easily under stronger sunlight, so maybe we might give also flaws?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(In ESO)</b> <b>Nords</b> don't have &quot;nature survival &amp; combat classes&quot;. Their pre-history mentions Atmora <i>freezing over</i> (so they either had a mutation to thrive in the cold - <i>or died</i>). <b>Then</b> they had to fight the Falmer to live in Skyrim (so they either had another mutation that gave a bonus to combat - <i>or died</i>). &quot;Resist Frost&quot; and &quot;Battle Frenzy&quot; <b>aren't</b> cultural artifacts - they're natural selection killing off whoever doesn't breed true. Nature &amp; history don't care if you want to be a bard or a farmer - you are descended from frost-warriors - so you're a frost-warrior-turned-bard or a frost-warrior-turned-farmer, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is very interesting and I can agree with you... on some levels. It's fascinating, and has a basis in the lore. I don't want it to become biological essentialism though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(In RL) the Inuit</b> have mutations (that 100% of their population has) that only 15% of Han Chinese and 2% of Europeans have - which help them thrive off their raw high-meat, high-fat diets. Conversely, the <b>Havasupai </b>(in Arizona) <i>grew sick from European foods. </i><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Denying biological differences resulted in suffering</span> - as the Havasupai <i>lost teeth, became diabetic and a half-dozen other diseases</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bantu &amp; Benin</b> (sickle-cell anemia to resist Malaria); <b>the Kalenjin</b> &amp; other Nilotic peoples are runners (people have copied their diets, altitude &amp; other practices - but you can't copy biomechanics); even <b>Europeans</b> (digesting milk &amp; alcohol - and 1% being HIV immune due to plagues).<br /> <br /> <b>All of these are awesome - and none of them &quot;cultural&quot;.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yep, more awesome facts. I'm really liking this post! (It also reminds me that, iirc, most East Asians have a harder time with alcohol and get drunk more easily than whites, true? Although most whites stop being able to digest milk with puberty, and that's where lactose intolerance comes in, but children are almost always totally fine).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I understand American concerns (I think) - </span>but none of these differences claim &quot;superiority&quot;. Twenty different LATAM countries can see the differences in one another (and have rivalries) without anyone claiming to be a master race.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You're right, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Spain, the same applies to regions - the Catalans are industrious/dour economical/stingy; the Gallegos are blunt/curt dumb/honest brutes/strong (Orcs!); the Madrile\u00f1os think they brought &quot;civilization&quot; unto everyone else (snooty/high-class, manipulative/leaders); etc - <b><i>everyone</i></b> likes to pretend they're better, but it's on part with a Dwarf, an Orc and a High Elf forming a group (they're still a group - Galician-Orcs aren't trying to wage genocide on High-Elven-Madrile\u00f1os, nor are Catalan-Dwarves trying to replace Basque-Druids).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hah, but those are stereotypes! You can have very similar people think of each other in those terms too - but okay, sure, there are many complex factors at play, and what we perceive as stereotypes can have their roots in culture and background and even geographical region... I'm not sure though whether I would want to introduce regional stereotypes as hard and fast racial traits - and I know Spanish are very into their regional identity and learn both Castillan and the dialect of their region, and I appreciate it. In Italy there's a strong cultural divide between North and South - Northerners see themselves as more hardworking, serious and honest, Southerners usually think of themselves as friendlier, more gregarious, more cunning and adaptable, and more passionate. It's not complete bullshit - every city has a different culture, and many cities close to each other share similar cultural aspect, so there is a form of conditioning, of nurture above nature if you will. It's all interesting stuff - that too often leads to hate in Italy, because of course - but I think it's more fluff than crunch... nope?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>(In ESO) Imperials</b> I'd liken to <b>Roman</b> or <b>Latin</b> people (their obvious inspiration). There are 20~ Spanish countries, a few other Latin-cousins (Italians, Portuguese, etc), and I mentioned our Jamaican, Haitian, Middle-Eastern populations (and the ever-so-exotic &quot;Americans&quot;). The Romans <i>were great</i> at assimilating &quot;European barbarians&quot; and the Spanish strove to emulate the model (intermixing and creating a dozen syncretic cultures).<br /> <br /> I never took &quot;speech classes&quot; to learn the differences - I'm <b>not</b> especially social - but <i>I'd slap myself</i> if I ever committed some of the faux pas I've seen Anglo-American tourists commit. You grow up surrounded by different peoples and <b>need</b> to learn the nuances. Meeting &quot;Middle Easterners&quot; was <i>new</i> for me in College, but they have a lot of similarities (even our mother tongues share links in syntax and vocabulary).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It makes a lot of sense, and yes, when the Umayyad Caliphate conquered the Iberic Peninsula the Muslims' Arabic mingled with the local Latin, so you share a lot of fascinating words, phonemes and grammar, it's really beautiful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And English-speakers find <b><i>words</i></b> offensive - Spanish-speakers listen to <b><i>tone</i></b>. You might not understand Japanese or Arabic <b>words</b> but you can always pick up <b>tone</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That is rather interesting, and probably a cultural-lingustic phenomenon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does <b>not</b> stretch my imagination that a race (<b>the Imperials</b>) living in a central-location surrounded by multiple races will <b>naturally</b> have more nuance for cultural differences - that the more isolated or war-like Nords, Reguards and Bretons don't. Imperials aren't &quot;silver tongued&quot; because they took classes - they're &quot;silver tongued&quot; <i>because everyone else talks like an idiot</i> with foreigners. The Altmer don't seem to notice their eugenicism terrifies others - the Bosmer come across like cannibals - the Dunmer religion shocks tourists - Redguards &amp; Nords are too busy picking fights to learn social charms. <b>The Imperial gift</b> is being less assholes than the isolated bumpkins that surround them.[/spoiler]<br /> <hr /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This had <i>never occurred to me</i> (nor did the fact that the Nord are good at fighting and resisting cold because of mutations) - I think it's an especially brilliant explanation. I have a &quot;but&quot; though! Bretons have a mostly mercantile economy... why not something similar? Oh and we also, apparently, are used to intrigues and plots - should we have a trait for that too? I'm teasing you of course. Btw I think it's very interesting that even Breton culture is so varied according to where exactly in High Rock you are, and the same holds true for most &quot;races&quot; in TES - but then should we try and replicate all cultural variations? And I'm only half-teasing now. Should we have cultures that give us small benefits and flaws in Exalted as well? It's undeniable that the Delzahn and the Marukani could qualify for some Riding bonus I think - if that were the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>re: Race as Trope Markers</b><br /> <br /> I really like the 3E Lintha clarification you folks point to - and by extension, all this mulling on Elder Scrolls races. I'm liking this &quot;nationalistic racism&quot; and &quot;propaganda&quot; angle a lot. Less mechanical difference (except maybe a few mutations). No need for &quot;Orcs, Dwarves, Elves&quot; with unique origin stories - when &quot;humans adapted to different environments&quot; are fitting (and they don't need to live in the far-flung corners of the Bordermarches for this benefit).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Agreed!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212457#post1212457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Snake People in An-Teng <b>are a race</b>. No one thinks of them as &quot;Beastmen&quot; - they're seen a distinct local race.<br /> <br /> The Lintha <b>are a race</b>. No one thinks about magic-mechanics of being altered-humans or not. A couple aquatic mutations could suffice for humans to make up completely fictitious histories for this &quot;magical&quot; race.<br /> <br /> The Sijanese? <b>Are a race</b>. Without making them all ghost-blooded, it'd suffice to give 1-2 mutations or merits that might be shadowland related (representing a <i>lifetime</i> among the dead that no mere tourist or migrant will acquire overnight).<br /> <br /> The people of Great Forks? <b>Are a race</b>. Without making them all god-blooded, it'd suffice to give 1-2 mutations or merits in the vein of Bretons (from Elder Scrolls).<br /> <br /> <b>They're all human</b>.<br /> <br /> But one could easily &quot;build racial tropes&quot; (the way Orcs, Dwarves, Elves, etc have them) representing stereotypes (that have grains of truth in them).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very thought-provoking conclusion to a very thought-provoking post, and I really love all the points you're making, because you're so passionate about them and you make them so crystal clear.<br /> <br /> But of course I have to play Devil's advocate (sometimes it feels like it's... genetic) - &quot;race&quot; is a concept that came up with colonialism. Not that nobody else before ever had that thought, actually, of course human beings have always identified themselves as distinct from neighboring groups - but these differences usually haven't been seen as natural/immutable/global - the way race is traditionally thought of by cis white male pseudointellectuals and scared white SJW like Yours Truly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - these populations, these ethnicities, thought in terms of &quot;peoples&quot; and &quot;folks&quot; much more often than &quot;race&quot;. Beast<i>folk</i> is, I think, an especially apt nomenclature, in game - &quot;the serpentfolk of Ixcoatli&quot; is something people in Creation could actually say. &quot;The Dragon Kings are a dying race&quot;... ? ... Would they use that term? I wonder. Maybe a dying people? A dying civilization? A dying culture? Or maybe, yes, a dying race. Need more data - I should check how scholars and storytellers from the Roman Empire, Classical Greece, various Chinese dynasties, the Muslim expansion, the Aztec empire, the Maya empire, the Mongol empire, Songhai, Ghana, Ethiopia... referred to other people, and various animals, and how they subdivided them, what taxonomy they used... Nice, I have my work cut out for me... and I did it to myself!<br /> <br /> You do make your point though regarding the Sijanese. They might very well have developed a shadowland-related mutation. And maybe all the gods and elementals in Great Forks did rub off some of their magic onto the humans.<br /> <br /> It's interesting! And even while they're still all humans, they could have cultural assets and flaws and physical differences...<br /> <br /> It is certainly a valid point of view, and well worth bearing in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T20:37:21-07:00","id":1212911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know I should just shut up, because as a Person of Color you evidently can talk circles around me about race, but since I'm impossibly anal retentive... No? <i>Race is a social construct</i>. It's an <i>informal</i> taxonomic rank below subspecies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it more or less maps onto and rides an archaic attempt to define subspecies of humans, since the categories were derived from Carolus Linnaeus's early and extremely wayward work on the subject. I call it wayward because the groups were based on the fluids of humorism; it turns out, trying to delineate groups of humans by way of magical thinking yields results that don't reflect reality in any way, shape, or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:00:57-07:00","id":1212921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212911#post1212911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it more or less maps onto and rides an archaic attempt to define subspecies of humans, since the categories were derived from Carolus Linnaeus's early and extremely wayward work on the subject. I call it wayward because the groups were based on the fluids of humorism; it turns out, trying to delineate groups of humans by way of magical thinking yields results that don't reflect reality in any way, shape, or form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A good proof of 'race as social construct' is that literally no one could agree on who was what, anywhere(Hell, the US can't agree from Census to Census what 'races' exist, how to divide them up, and on what grounds. Legal systems are the most common way to 'define' the terms and <i>wow</i> do those not agree with each other. If you have a tolerance for pseudo-science, dig around colonial works of French, German, and British race scientests and wowee, they get weird. And that's even before getting into what defined the term: French colonies operated on the notion that different groups/nationals had inherently different tempermants that shaped their bodies, where as the Brits thought the differences were fundamentally biological, and then there were the adaptives who thought culture was written into the body of people.) Anthropology/history of science is fun!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I think another word your using is 'natural', which...I disagree with. Or rather, I think your blending with cultural in an odd way. We could say that Nords had mutations that grant them cold resistance--that's an inheritable trait, such that if I stole a Nord baby and dropped them in Morrowind, it'd be there. The Imperial gift with words can't come about that--tempermant isn't inherited. Now, it might be that then this trait is reflective of the resutl of Imperial upbrinigng...but its put on the same level as biological phenomona.<br /> <br /> Also, for those who want to non-humans, I think aliens are pretty good inspiration(especialyl pulpy ones). I've considered adapting Namekians to Exalted as prehumans(or at least their merging/splitting thing).<br /> <br /> The Lintha are especially intreasting in that regard...Has Moorcook ever said they were a direct jab at elves? They feel like that, including the weird internal differences in thought with humans.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm...iffy about giving every culture group 1 or 2 mutations to repersent the local enviroment, since that seems to turn what is mostly social into biological. Merits, yeah, sure. But mutations? Exalted's source of mutations and biological changes are pretty clearly...unsubtle, and not something that just happen from being somewhere a long time(mostly. Wyld, Ysyr, and Shadowlands and such, but tbh I don't think the shadowlands would be much more then cosmetics.)<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: And if their mutations to repersent a sort of natural selection adaptivity...uh...very few people in exalted have lived in a place long enough for that to take affect.<br /> <br /> EDIT 3: Sleeping on it, I want to be clear that Social Construct =/= not real. Just not based on a meaningful, non-cultural basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 04-29-2018, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:22:16-07:00","id":1212926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212911#post1212911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it more or less maps onto and rides an archaic attempt to define subspecies of humans, since the categories were derived from Carolus Linnaeus's early and extremely wayward work on the subject. I call it wayward because the groups were based on the fluids of humorism; it turns out, trying to delineate groups of humans by way of magical thinking yields results that don't reflect reality in any way, shape, or form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Linnaeus was the first to sciencify race, but there were some attempts to classify human races a little before him (with similar &quot;Oh shit, there's way more vareity in people than we thought&quot; going on). But yeah, he had this weird fivefold thing up and down his original taxonomy which was <i>weird</i> when you sit and read what the hell he was doing back in the day.<br /> <br /> Modern genetic studies shows human race is pretty neglible as a species. Like, humans are notable for as big a population we have but low genetic diversity, indicating a pretty recent bottle neck event. Recent studies tracking human migraiton patterns and such kind of show this gets even more distinct, with most human populations being a kind of Matroshka doll of genetic diversity starting in African populations and getting thinner as you get further away from it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T04:11:33-07:00","id":1212996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212921#post1212921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm...iffy about giving every culture group 1 or 2 mutations to repersent the local enviroment, since that seems to turn what is mostly social into biological. Merits, yeah, sure. But mutations? Exalted's source of mutations and biological changes are pretty clearly...unsubtle</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that in this Edition, the only thing that we've got so far distinctly referring to &quot;mutations&quot; is going to be Hybrid Body Transformation, and Vance has stated that the mutations you can gain from that include virtually all physical Merits. And not just the Supernatural ones.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink about it; we've got Innate physical Merits for things like being able to control your capacity to conceive children, or a version of Ambidextrous that gives one prehensile feet (which is said to be common among the population of Halta). How are those not mutations?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:05:22-07:00","id":1213057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212996#post1212996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that in this Edition, the only thing that we've got so far distinctly referring to &quot;mutations&quot; is going to be Hybrid Body Transformation, and Vance has stated that the mutations you can gain from that include virtually all physical Merits. And not just the Supernatural ones.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink about it; we've got Innate physical Merits for things like being able to control your capacity to conceive children, or a version of Ambidextrous that gives one prehensile feet (which is said to be common among the population of Halta). How are those not mutations?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh. I've been thinking exclusively of Supernatural merits as mutations. Good call. I'd still be antsy on making innate physical merits for the majority of creation's human populace, but to each their own on that front.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T09:17:28-07:00","id":1213087,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the majority, and there are a number of purchasable Merits that can also fit the bill, but in cases where one wishes to depict a locally adapted or otherwise distinct population, Merits are there as a means of representing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T09:19:12-07:00","id":1213089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213087#post1213087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about the majority, and there are a number of purchasable Merits that can also fit the bill, but in cases where one wishes to depict a locally adapted or otherwise distinct population, Merits are there as a means of representing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to dig for it, but my understanding is there will be a definitive list in Lunars as what is a mutation or not for purposes of their Charms and that htere will probably be some new ones too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T09:21:49-07:00","id":1213091,"title":"","content":"I should clarify that when I'm suggesting that the two-dot version of Ambidextrous constitutes a mutation, I'm thinking more in an evolutionary biology sense rather than a magically altered morphology one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:33:58-07:00","id":1213202,"title":"","content":"While on the subject of non-human species there are the other members of the genus homo. A few of them were contemporary with sapiens and interbred with them. It is (or was) a bit of a thing that Mountainfolk warriors were Neanderthals in power armor, but if extinct megafauna is still around I suppose there is room for other upright apes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T16:43:54-07:00","id":1213222,"title":"","content":"I set out to make a collection of races lost during the primordial war. Some harken to themes and abilities lost with the three sphere cataclysm and the death of pluto but I hope they can spark ideas at least.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15meFxtC1n-pEa68usLTLsIX-nMuj81MYJTORetZyEhA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15meFxtC1n-pEa68usLTLsIX-nMuj81MYJTORetZyEhA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15meFxtC1n-pEa68usLTLsIX-nMuj81MYJTORetZyEhA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/15meFxtC1n-pEa68usLTLsIX-nMuj81MYJTORetZyEhA/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:38:11-07:00","id":1213625,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#0000ff\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Sorry</b></span></span> for the delayed response! I wanted to give each point thorough thought (with dates or links to show I wasn't talking madness). I hope this finds you well. (and that it's mildly entertaining to anyone else).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I should just shut up, because as a Person of Color you evidently can talk circles around me about race, but since I'm impossibly anal retentive... No? (<b>snip</b>) so as long as you and other people of color here are alright, it's all good.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Thank you for not shutting up!</span> </span></span><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The only thing that ever makes me uncomfortable - are the pro-censorship &quot;white knights&quot; who think minorities &quot;need saving&quot; - as if we're too intellectually stunted or fragile to enjoy these conversations. No one's skin color gives anyone a right to silence others.<br /> <br /> If I mention the Hispanic thing during race topics, it's to preempt the occasional &quot;white knight&quot; trying to frame me as anything else.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And can I say how right you are? About American unease with race? Like totally. Actually, since I'm European, let's call it differently - white unease. We whites know we've messed up something awful in the past (and we still do, like a lot) and we're enormously uneasy with our treatment of PoC, native peoples and foreign sovereign nations. We can get downright irrational about it. White guilt.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Please don't kick yourself! </b></span></span><br /> <br /> \u200bYou (or any other &quot;white&quot; person) are <b>not responsible </b>for what your ancestors may-or-may-not have done half-a-thousand years ago.<br /> <br /> <b>And if you are</b>, then we need to <b>also blame</b> the Berbers, the Moors, the Ottomans and other groups who invaded Europe<i> in the first place</i>.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Dates become <b>very</b> important.<br /> <br /> <b>711</b> is when the Umayyad conquest of Hispania began - <i>three centuries</i> before the Crusades started (<b>1095-1291</b>), long before the First Inquisition (<b>1231</b>), long before the Spanish Inquisitoin (<b>1478</b>). The full Reconquista (<b>718-1492</b>) took <u><i>more than seven centuries</i></u>.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;But what does that have to do with slavery?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Etymologically, <i>slave</i> comes from <i>Slav</i> - Eastern Europeans. The Ottoman Sultan <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mehmed_the_Conqueror\" target=\"_blank\">Mehmed</a> II conquered (Byzantine/Constantinople/Istanbul) in <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">1453 </span>- </b>and went on to claim Constantinople &amp; Morea (Greece), Wallachia &amp; Moldavia (Romania), Serbia &amp; Bosnia (Slavs), the Black Sea Coast <b>and</b> attack Venice, Genoa and coasts of Italy.<ul><li>For reference, Vlad the Impaler was from this time period - a hostage of the Ottomans - with much of his fame <i>a reaction</i> to them. Sultan Mehmed II eventually had Vlad <i>dismembered</i> and his <i>decapitated head</i> delivered to him as a trophy. If you think Vampires and Dracula are bad, <i>this is the guy who killed Dracula</i>.</li> <li>For reference, Mehmed was the guy who demanded that Notaras - the Byzantine Megas Doux - give up his 14 y/o son &quot;for the Sultan's pleasure&quot;. When Notaras refused, the Sultan had him, his son and his son-in-law decapitated (their heads decorating his banquet table).</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">The Pope asked all Christian nations to send aid to Constantinople.</span><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;So a bunch of Crusaders went for war and glory!?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Nope. Europe was fractured beyond belief.<ul><li><b>England &amp; France</b> were weakened from the Hundred Years War (1337 to 1453).</li> <li><b>Spain didn't exist. </b>Ancestral distrust was strong and it took <i>centuries</i> for Kingdoms to conglomerate into larger alliances. The Umayyads, the Almoravids and others <b>all</b> took Iberian slaves too. By the 1400s, the 4 major alliances were the Kingdoms of Portugal, Castille, Aragon and Granada.</li> <li><b>Italy didn't exist</b>. It was fragmented into the Kingdoms of Sicily and Naples - the Republics of Siena, Lucca, , Genoa, Florence and Venice - the Duchy of Modena, Ferrara, Milan and Savoy - and the Papal States. Mehmed attacked Venice (1463-1479) and Italian coasts (1480). For comparison, Machiavelli wasn't born until 1469 - so he grew up among all this warfare - with The Prince being written in 1513.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">The only ones who came were soldiers from the Kingdom of Portugal (far Western Europe) who sailed the entire Mediterranean to try helping the Greeks in Constantinople (far Eastern Europe). It was too late to save the city - but the Pope <b>noticed</b>.</span><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Why does any of this matter? How's it relate to slavery?&quot;</b><ul><li>By <b>1415</b>, the Kingdom of Portugal felt the need to debate &quot;the wisdom and justice&quot; of an attack on Morocco (in order to cut off the Moors at the root). Religious and ethical limitations were a serious concern.</li> <li>But in <b>1432, </b>Prince Afonso V was born. His father died, so he became a 6 y/o King in <b>1438</b> - came to full power at 16 y/o in <b>1448</b> (and enjoyed his first war against his uncle) - and by <b>1452</b> (he was 20) the Pope issued the Papal Bull -<b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dum_Diversas\" target=\"_blank\">Dum Diversas</a></b> - giving the Iberian kingdoms religious leeway to go <i>buckwild</i> on the invaders - and by <b>1458</b>, Portugal was claiming territory Morocco (26 y/o King).</li> </ul>In other words, the Church had <i>forbidden slavery</i> for nearly a thousand years - but that became irrelevant if the Moors, the Barbary States and the Ottoman's are invading Christian lands to take slaves. <b>Therefore</b>, Dum Diversas authorized Iberians to go &quot;an eye for an eye&quot; and seek to conquer and convert the Maghreb (because then, as Christians, they'd stop trying to enslave other Christians). <b>And for comparison</b>, there are <b>still modern slave practices </b>- in Morocco and Mauritania (the Moors), in Libya (the Barbary / Berber), etc.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And then there's the issue of this radical, one-sided, good/evil, black/white, yes/no dichotomy for colonialism?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yes, the British were assholes - but their Imperialism also <b>ended widow-burnings</b> in India. Before the British, the Mughals had marched into India and razed Delhi <b>eight times in eight centuries. </b>The British knocked out local rulers - and the democratic institutions remained long after. Roughly 106 countries have English as a business-tongue, eliminating the &quot;Tower of Babel&quot; scenario where people can't communicate to negotiate peace. Oh and the modern Criminal Justice system is also British - replacing centuries (in most places) of mob violence or blood feuds (the system helped other Europeans too).<br /> <br /> Yes, the Spanish were assholes - but how far can you condemn them?<ul><li><b>Diseases:</b><br /> Spaniards wanted converts and citizens they could tax - not massacres. Most of the violence was pathogenic - not physical - as the Spanish unwittingly carried diseases the Natives had never encountered. There was no &quot;Trail of Tears&quot;. Even then, Spain wanted <b>Criollos </b>to interbreed with <b>Indios</b> to create <b>Mestizos </b>who could serve as in-betweens and survive the illnesses.<ul><li>And at first, Mestizos weren't categorized by color - they were either treated as Spanish or Native based on which culture they were raised in. The category arose later when some were clearly half-and-half..</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Aztecs:</b><br /> Or do you condemn Cort\u00e9s for sending 600 men against the Aztecs? Then you need to condemn the indigenous peoples from Tlaxcala who contributed 6,000 soldiers <i>and pointed the way to them</i>. People seem to forget that Cort\u00e9s was guilty of <b>mutiny</b> - he was going to be recalled back to Spain, so he misled a garrison of soldiers in the middle of the night - stole a ship - and sailed West in pursuit of his own wealth. <b>Then he burnt the ships</b> (Arthas style). So do you blame 600 lost Conquistadors or the 6,000 natives who were tired of the Aztecs <i>decorating their temples with skulls?</i></li> <li><b>Famine:</b><br /> Famines killed millions every decade - until the Spanish conquistadors discovered potatoes in Peru and exported them back to Europe. <b>Suddenly</b> crops no longer failed en masse, starvation rates plummeted and less people died.</li> <li><b>Black Legend:</b><br /> Much of Spanish infamy was from the Dominican friar Bartolom\u00e9 de las Casas - whose polemics inspired the <i>Black Legend</i> Anglo-Protestants loved to spread. He made the argument for the humanity of the native people (due the protections of the Spanish Crown).<ul><li>And is this not progress in itself? The Bible has examples of <i>celebrated</i> genocides. The Aztecs had no problem torturing sacrifices. <b>Less than 20 years</b> after the Spanish touched soil, people like Bartolom\u00e9 were advocating <b>for</b> the conquered peoples. Does anyone believe the Aztecs would have returned the favor?</li> </ul></li> </ul>Yes, the French were assholes. Mostly assholes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No defense.<br /> <br /> Colonialism had lots of negatives - but it also spread <b>infrastructure</b>, spread <b>democracy</b>, created modern <b>medicine </b>(all those foreign bugs &amp; diseases killing everyone).<br /> <br /> The world now speaks English in 106 countries, Arabic in 58, French in 53, Spanish in 31 - plus Russian and Mandarin more localized - world languages that <b>make trade and diplomacy more feasible.</b> ALL of those languages are colonial ones (not only did Arabic speakers have their own empires - but French policies inadvertently helped spread and cement Arabic).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> TLDR - Don't drink the kool-aid that you have to loathe your ancestors (and anyone who looks remotely like them). The world was always full of shitty people, Europe was invaded for almost a thousand years - and then they got lucky on a coin toss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on average we all have 99.9% of the same DNA as anybody else. So yeah, diversity - and also, equality.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>And that 0.1% of DNA </b>decides who dies of malaria, who drowns first, who outruns a predator and who doesn't get HIV.<br /> <br /> Your intentions are good - but we don't need to diminish science for &quot;equality&quot;. Everyone is special in different ways - but that difference is <b>why</b> diversity is good (if it was something insignificant, like hair-color, then diversity would be worthless).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>biological essentialism</i>. You're an orc, hence you're strong, tough, prone to rage, and evil. Thx no thx!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>re: Biological Essentialism </b><br /> I wasn't familiar with this term - but I don't see the problem with it?<br /> <br /> Are you religious? Do you believe our bodies are just dolls that our souls marionette? Because I don't think our brains are divorced from our bodies - therefore, hormones, drugs and genetics certainly affect how we think. And there's something <b>more hopeful</b> about bio-essentialism (because instead of throwing our arms in the air and saying &quot;people are randomly evil&quot;, we can go &quot;oh, if this behavior is malevolent, we can cure it by....&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Psychopaths:</b><br /> Ever see the story about the <a href=\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/science-nature/the-neuroscientist-who-discovered-he-was-a-psychopath-180947814/\" target=\"_blank\">Neuroscientist who discovered he was a psyhopath</a> - &quot;<b>nurture</b>&quot; made him a doctor instead of a criminal, but his <b>nature</b> was still the same.<ul><li>After a series of genetic tests, \u201cI had all these high-risk alleles for aggression, violence and low empathy,\u201d he says, such as a variant of the MAO-A gene that has been linked with aggressive behavior. Additionally, his family line included seven alleged murderers.</li> </ul><b>IQ Scores:</b><br /> Have you ever read about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashkenazi_Jewish_intelligence\" target=\"_blank\">Ashkenazi IQ scores</a>? Less that 0<b>.</b>2% of the global population - and they are 25% of Nobel Prize winners, 37% of National Medal of Science winners, 42% of Nobel laureates in medicine - and in 1954, out of all New York children with an IQ over 170, 85% were Jewish.<br /> <br /> <b>Testosterone vs Cortisol in Sex Offenders:</b><br /> There was another study I read a while back surveying hormones in inmate populations - that found that rapists had <b>the lowest</b> levels of Cortisol (stress hormone). Testosterone and Cortisol clash - too much cortisol can even kill an erection - ergo, having a &quot;healthy balance&quot; was good, since it encouraged males to slow down and ensure their partner was comfortable and consenting. <b>With rapists</b>, however, lack of cortisol meant testosterone was unbound - rapists had less empathy than <i>murderers</i>.<br /> <br /> There's also other things like high-Testosterone making you more interested in &quot;things&quot; rather than &quot;people&quot; - and 4/5ths of Autism and Asperger's patients being male. That's pretty biological.<br /> <br /> <b>Ethnonym:</b><br /> Or when I compared my ethnonym to Orcs - did you think it was arbitrary?<ul><li><b>Pre-Roman</b>, Galicians were described as &quot;head-hunters whose wise-men divine fate in entrails&quot; who valued &quot;heads more than gold&quot;</li> <li><b>Post-Roman, </b>the region (which was 5% of Iberia) produced 33% of all Roman recruits</li> <li><b>Christians</b> had such headaches converting the region, they gave Galicia a <a href=\"http://www.ancient-origins.net/history-famous-people/saint-witch-or-both-strange-case-st-columba-sens-006735\" target=\"_blank\">Patron Saint of Witchcraft </a>(midway down the article)</li> <li><b>The Umayyads </b>abandoned the region, claiming &quot;their only sport is <i>violence&quot; </i>(not good as slaves), they valued &quot;neither art nor gold&quot; (nothing to tax) and the woods were &quot;haunted by pagan monsters&quot;.</li> <li><b>The Kingdom of Castille</b> famously &quot;tamed&quot; the region by offering local leaders military support - and watching them kill each other off - with the survivors swearing fealty in gratitude. <i>This is one of the reasons </i>Madrid stereotypes them as &quot;dumb brutes&quot; and Galicia stereotypes them as &quot;conniving snakes&quot;.</li> </ul>That's 2,000 years with changes to the language, the religion and culture - <b>but every</b> foreign power sees the same stereotype. And DNA tests confirm Galicia is more closely related to the Basque and Irish (meaning that in 20 centuries, they didn't even intermix much with their neighbors).<br /> <br /> This is not to say every Galician is a raving barbarian - but &quot;all the above&quot; colors the regional personalities, even in the <i>kindest</i> of them. Even my American-raised kin (far removed from the above) all showed strong stereotypes (despite being unaware of them).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's absolutely true. I have a Breton character and even though she looks for all intents and purposes fully human she has a tiny sliver of elven blood in there. But should such a remote ancestral variation play such a big part in what she's capable of? I guess it comes down to preferences - if elven magic is a <i>big deal</i>, well, then probably yes, you might want to starkly differentiate a Breton from a Nord. Beware essentialism though... it would be nice if, say, Bretons had a slight affinity for magic on average, but that wasn't restricted to them, and any &quot;race&quot; could potentially produce the most powerful archmage possible (and iirc in the lore it's quite like that, as Shalidor was a Nord, which is totally playing against type).<br /> <b>(snip)</b><br /> Bretons have a mostly mercantile economy... why not something similar?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>re: Bretons, Shalidor &amp; Racial Mutations</b><br /> Always ask &quot;would lacking this mutation <b>kill you</b>&quot;?<br /> <br /> <b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Bretons </div></div> </div> </div></b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>don't </b>get bonuses to mercantile - because such bonuses are <i>irrelevant</i> to whether they live or die. If an Altmer can cast Illusion spells to mind-control you, such a bonus instantly becomes irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <b>Bretons do </b>get (in Skyrim) a 25% Magic Resist and 50% Magic Absorption. Not only do they have Elven blood - but these traits <b>definitely</b> let you survive Altmer mind-control and fireballs (which they had to do at some point when they broke free). And there is <b>no guarantee</b> the Bretons would have survived otherwise - mother nature wouldn't care if an entire race went extinct. Any bloodlines that lacked these resistances/absorption were obviously exterminated.<br /> <br /> <b>Shalidor</b> is actually <i>a great example of why Essentialism is great</i>. Altmer and Bretons have better magic skills - but Shalidor defied natural predispositions <b>and</b> culture to be amazing. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Essentialism</b> thus rebuffs them all, showcasing how those with privilege (the Altmer &amp; Breton) <i>take it for granted</i> - whereas someone without those gifts (Shalidor) strives harder.</span><br /> <br /> Or to borrow from <b>Bajau Laut</b> again - <i>essentially</i>, they have a mutation that makes them better divers - but it was someone <b>without those gifts</b> who invented Scuba Gear. Essentialism doesn't prohibit cleverness from circumventing restrictions.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... the two (race &amp; color) are related though?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>re: Race vs Color</b><br /> No necessarily?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">If we took a vacation to India, I would <b>not</b> expect the Shudras to identify with Jamaicans or watch BET - <b>nor</b> would I think the Brahmins find kinship with the Irish or Greek. Different skin tones don't make the Hindi people less &quot;a people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise with Spanish. If I mention Celia Cruz and Willy Chirino, most of us would know them as <b>Cubans</b>, not &quot;black female, white male&quot;. They made <i>Cuban</i> music. Haitians don't have any special &quot;dibs&quot; on Celia - nor do Romanians get &quot;dibs&quot; on Willy.<br /> <br /> My aunt is &quot;white&quot; - her daughter is &quot;black&quot; - the grandson is &quot;white&quot;. What good is a &quot;race&quot; definition if mother-and-child aren't even in the same categories?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... that's not race? Turkey is a nation, Armenia is a nation, Japan is a nation... I'm Italian, but that's not my race - if I had to tell you what my race is I'd probably say white caucasian? And still nations are very interesting, they're trope-codifiers all by themselves, it's cool stuff! It's part of your identity (whether I like it or not... meep!)</div> </div> </div> </div>You say you're &quot;white&quot; - but...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I've never heard a Korean or Thai or Japanese call themselves &quot;yellow&quot;. I dated a Jamaican whose parents were from Ghana - and they referred to themselves as either &quot;Jamaican&quot; or &quot;Ghanaian&quot; (never &quot;black&quot;). And could you imagine any Native Americans referring to themselves as &quot;reds&quot;?<br /> <br /> The Japanese Emperors are descended from Amaterasu Omikami, the sun goddess. No elections nor politics will ever make a Korean a descendant of Amaterasu. If I lived 40 years in Japan, I would never be truly <i>Japanese</i> (even if they quite graciously let me enjoy the culture, the language, etc).<br /> <br /> The Turks are descended from the Ottoman's, who are descended ultimately from the Hittites, a warrior-race that threatened even ancient Egypt. If I moved to Turkey next week and lived there for a three decades, I would <b>not</b> be confused for one of them.<br /> <br /> What <b>good</b> is &quot;white&quot;? The only people I know who say &quot;white&quot; (in the US) are Anglo-Saxons and the like who long ago forgot their ancestry (but they still think of their ancestry as the &quot;default&quot; - so &quot;whiteness&quot; is either &quot;English-ness&quot; or &quot;German-ness&quot;).<br /> <br /> <b>But go with Italian</b> <b>and <i>that's a people</i>.</b> Language, culture, history, art - you can't confuse an Italian with a Swede or a Serb. I have an Italian friend and there is <b>too much overlap</b> to not consider them cousins. And I doubt taking a couple Italian classes would suffice for an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=krtnt191Drg\" target=\"_blank\">Anglo-American to pass for Italian</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>At this point</b>, I think we're swapping &quot;race&quot; for &quot;ethnicity&quot; - but it remains that most people <b>don't</b> change ethnicities just by moving to a new country and learning another tongue</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is rather interesting, and probably a cultural-lingustic phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>re: Words vs Tone</b><br /> English colonies started a century after the rest - with a heavy eye aimed at dealing with overpopulation and crime (which is why they made strides in their criminal justice system). Ergo, they have nuance in words. They needed to <i>write down</i> exactly who-did-what and why-they-go-to-jail.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I can use 1-2 words for a 'murderer' in Spanish - but then I need to translate for family members the difference between an Assassin (political) vs Hitman (business); a Mass Murderer (lots of victims), a Spree Shooter (lots of victims at 2 or more locations) and a Serial Killer (lots of victims but carefully selected over time and place); a Killer (takes a life) vs a Murderer (takes a life without legal sanction) vs an Executioner (etc, etc, etc). There are <b>so many</b> crime &amp; law TV shows in English, it's mind-boggling.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212695#post1212695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>biological essentialism</i>. You're an orc, hence you're strong, tough, prone to rage, and evil. Thx no thx!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>re: Orcs &amp; Green Face</b><br /> I'll revisit this with a counter-poke - as a proud lover of Orcs, I think you're an Elf asking for permission to engage in Green-Face!<br /> Just a bit of paint and a couple tusks and you think that's all an Orc <b>is</b>. =P lol<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I used to hate Orc cliches.</span><br /> <br /> But then I was playing Skyrim - in the College of Mages - when the elitism of certain Mage NPCs <i>infuriated me</i> (and that was inspiration). And then the racism of the Thalmor <i>infuriated me</i> (and that was inspiration). And then one day I paid attention to the Orc Librarian and realized &quot;wow, if I'm angry, I can only imagine a character like him!&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">So I re-rolled an Orc mage (who was deliberately incompetent with spells).</span><br /> <br /> And while everyone ran around with a multitude of cool spells, I focused on my racial talents - smithing and enchanting. <i>People don't choose their talents</i> in real-life, right? And still being infuriated (with elitists and racists), I spent hours improving my craft and collecting soul gems. <b>And I crafted</b> a set of magic-resist armor. <b>And I enchanted</b> my blacksmithing hammer with &quot;Soul Trap&quot;. And I realized my Orc was <i>really good at</i> killing rogue mages (bashing their brains out and using their souls to enchant <i>better</i> armor).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">And then I revisited Orcish law and custom and asked - <i>was my character self-loathing? </i><i>No!</i></span><br /> <br /> And as I read the Monomyth, I began to see how to reiterpret it.<ul><li>Orc oaths &quot;end in death&quot;? <b>Of course they do</b> - Trinimac's duties to Auri-el ended when he died and was reborn as Malacath.</li> <li>Orcs admire a glorious death? <b>Of course they do</b> - through death, Trinimac was reborn as something greater. He was no longer an Aedra (doomed to mortality) but now a Daedra (immortal and unharmed by Creation).</li> <li>Orcs replace unfit rulers by violence? <b>Of course they do</b> - had Trinimac not been <i>too loyal</i> to Auri-el (who was clearly a failed leader), the doom of the Mer might have been averted.</li> <li>Orcs shun weakness, thieves and kin-slayers? <b>Of course they do - </b>Lorkhan was the &quot;weakest&quot; of the et'Ada and thus schemed to steal power (and kill) many of his peers via Creation. Malacath isn't <i>heartless</i> (or he wouldn't favor the Orsimer) - he had <i>learned harsh lessons</i>.</li> <li>Orcs demand a blood-price? <b>Of course they do</b> - when Lorkhan's deception was discovered, it was Trinimac who ripped his heart out (literally the first Blood Price in Creation, the Cain and Abel moment).</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Instead of &quot;Orcs are barbarians&quot;, it became &quot;Orcs have the purist religion and connection to their god-ancestor&quot;. <b>Every</b> Orcish custom seemed to have some direct parallel to Trinimac's legendary feats (such that we were in a way <i>the most <b>divinely</b> civilized</i>).</span><br /> <br /> <b>And then I played Elder Scrolls online</b> with a similar character - and it was <i>fun</i>. <b>Yes, </b>my <i>character</i> hated Orc stereotypes - but I <i>loved them</i>.<ul><li><b>Of course</b> my Orc was stereotypically angry - my character hated the stereotypes (even as she embodied them).</li> <li><b>Of course</b> my Orc was stereotypically a good crafter - if I wanted to break stereotypes, I needed to woo my peers into not dressing like savages - and eventually we had an all-Orc guild in <i>sweet </i>uniforms (free, fully enchanted and enhanced) and it was stunning in large RP and PVP events.</li> <li><b>Of course</b> my Orc was stereotypically strong - she wasn't a warrior, she merely was tough from working the forge (and a lifetime of being given menial tasks, for being underestimated).</li> <li><b>And if they thought</b> Orcs were stupid? <b>Great!</b> <i>It stings that much worse</i> when the &quot;stupid&quot; Orc scalds you with a quip that makes paint peel off the walls.</li> <li><b>And if they thought </b>Orcs were part of the &quot;House of Troubles&quot;? <b>Great!</b> Your religion has given me a &quot;space&quot; to exist within - and I could discuss with Dunmeri theologians after their sermons, building comraderie over our shared loathing of other races (like Nords and Altmer).</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>My point is</b> - <b>even characters who <u>hate</u> the bioessentialist stereotypes</b> can end up embodying (and playing off them). </span> And if it offends you deeply, then perhaps you <i>lack the mindset</i> to play an Orc. (for comparison, you'll never see me RP a pacifist for instance, since it'd be a dumb caricature at best - I don't think I'm capable of <i>not enjoying</i> a conflict)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  formatting 04-30-2018, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:32:06-07:00","id":1213644,"title":"","content":"As a note, your writing style could probably do some pruning, as it actually doe smake it hard to engage/respond. It's why I've been quie tin this thread, but I kind of feel that some of the way you are approaching some fo these things has less a racial tinge, but a Euro-Centric (I gathered that's where you are?). Lemme explain how and where I can on this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that ever makes me uncomfortable - are the pro-censorship &quot;white knights&quot; who think minorities &quot;need saving&quot; - as if we're too intellectually stunted or fragile to enjoy these conversations. No one's skin color gives anyone a right to silence others.<br /> <br /> If I mention the Hispanic thing during race topics, it's to preempt the occasional &quot;white knight&quot; trying to frame me as anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something you kind of have to be careful about. You are in effect casting any criticism of some of your stuff as white-knighting. While this is something that I have seen white folk do (I'm a PoC for record here), there are times where people are I think overly dismissive of the way that race plays into societal issues, politics, and descriptions of population. I just want you to keep tha tin mind before some other stuff gets talked on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Please don't kick yourself!</div> </div> </div> </div>White people don't need PoC to make them feel good. Remember that the way you put this, it kind of has this sense of belittlement to me. This is mostly because I think most white folk are actually able to handle criticisms bettter, and I think that it is playing into the &quot;white grievance&quot; narrative that is often used in the Americas to try and dismiss claims and issues made by PoC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[\u200bYou (or any other &quot;white&quot; person) are <b>not responsible </b>for what your ancestors may-or-may-not have done half-a-thousand years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>White supremacy as an overt force was in full affect in parts of the world until the 1990s (South Africa). It has left lingering effects throughout the African continent and the Americas. It is still in effect institutionally thorughout the Western world today. Mind, this doesn't mean that every indivdual white person is a white supremacist. What I mean is that there are instituitonal forces around the world which <i>do</i> cause problems for People of Color, which were often founded with an express purpose of enforcing white supremacy through either segregation and apartheid (as in the case of the US, South Africa, Rhodisa, or the Domincan Republic), or colonialism designed with the benefit of foreign, usually white, nations in mind (this is a large factor of various conflicts throughout the world).<br /> <br /> Again, I might have missed your background in this some, but there is a segment who believes that no, the world isn't all better now. And the causes for what made the world not so good are not very old.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<b>And if you are</b>, then we need to <b>also blame</b> the Berbers, the Moors, the Ottomans and other groups who invaded Europe<i> in the first place</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>My ancestors were taken from West Africa and sold into markets in Colombia probably by the English, Portugese, or Dutch. There's all sorts of tit-for-tat, but that doesn't excuse the fact that while there were other invasion sor slave trades, the people who enslaved people I claim descent from were Europeans, not Berbers or Ottomans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Etymologically, <i>slave</i> comes from <i>Slav</i> - Eastern Europeans....</div> </div> </div> </div> This is actually up to debate, as a note.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... (Euroepan timeilnie stuff)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what this does save trying to rehabilitate folks like Vlad who yeah, he was held captive by Turks but he was still an asshole. Two wrongs don't make a right and Europe was to my understanding an economic crator and clump of failed states after the fall of Rome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>(Reconquista stuff</i><i>)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a &quot;two wrongs made a right&quot; argument and ultimately fails. This is literaly &quot;They did it, so I can.&quot; and that they did it somehow absolves the Portugese from particpating in slavery. There are also arguments, such as those presented by Daved Graeber in <b>Debt: the First 5,000 Years</b> that arguably while the Church was a stopgap of slavery in the Medeival period, it's worth remebmering that serfdom was slavery of another kind by some definitions, and that many of the forces to encourage slavery in the Atlantic were likely less religious justificaiton and more economic incentives. Graeber argued pretty ehavily that <i>merchants</i> pushed for slavery, and in this case, it kind of undermiens a lot since it was done mostly for raw capital gain, not some view that somehow the Ottomans had authority. (Because let's be clear, most Catholics at the time could give zero fucks what Berbers, Arabs or Turks thought.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then there's the issue of this radical, one-sided, good/evil, black/white, yes/no dichotomy for colonialism?<br /> <br /> Yes, the British were assholes - but their Imperialism also <b>ended widow-burnings</b> in India. Before the British, the Mughals had marched into India and razed Delhi <b>eight times in eight centuries. </b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>There is debate as a note as to how often cities and temples were razed, as there is some hints that while the Mughals did raise temples, many mosques were also razed by Hindus. How often things were destroyed are muddled especially post-1940s by nationalists. And while wife burning was yes, terrible, it is patriarchal to think that the British ahd to Come In to Save Folks from Native Savagery. THey kicked the Mughals out and replaced it with their Raj. Women weren't burned at weddings, but folks starved in Benghal to feed Britsih soldiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... The British knocked out local rulers - and the democratic institutions remained long after. Roughly 106 countries have English as a business-tongue, eliminating the &quot;Tower of Babel&quot; scenario where people can't communicate to negotiate peace. Oh and the modern Criminal Justice system is also British - replacing centuries (in most places) of mob violence or blood feuds (the system helped other Europeans too).</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Latin America doesn't run on British Common Law, nor do most folks in the world in Asia. There's actually a good deal fo Dutch, French, Chinese, and Arab law in things about. Additionally, the use of some world langauge to conduct business likely is inevitable given the way economies operate. The subjugation of the plaent to European colonialism doesn't make up for that.<br /> <br /> My personal view: Everyone speaking English doesn't justify the famines in Bengal, the Opium Wars, African colonialism, or King Leopold being let near anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Spanish were assholes - but how far can you condemn them?Spaniards wanted converts and citizens they could tax - not massacres. Most of the violence was pathogenic - not physical - as the Spanish unwittingly carried diseases the Natives had never encountered. There was no &quot;Trail of Tears&quot;. Even then, Spain wanted <b>Criollos </b>to interbreed with <b>Indios</b> to create <b>Mestizos </b>who could serve as in-betweens and survive the illnesses.</div> </div> </div> </div>9/10s of the population was wiped out from the Americas dude. And the Spanish purposefully gave blankets and left sick people amongst populations. Columbus conducted systematic enslavement and genocide of the natives of Hispaniola, and the Spanish probably are responsible for the collapse of teh Miississippi civilization because they rampaged about, spread disease and left pigs. In the Amazon there is evidence that there might have been complex socieites which were driven to near extinction due to disease and later Spanish ensalvement.<br /> <br /> Theer was no Trail of Tears in the Spanish Americas because the Spanish were more interested in enslavement of locals. They introduced a casta system, which put natives only slightly above black slaves, and forbade local religions. They killed htier kings and burned their libraries. And after the Latin American Revolutions, many of the new nations introduced various laws around race, marginalized native population.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I call bullshit on this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And at first, Mestizos weren't categorized by color - they were either treated as Spanish or Native based on which culture they were raised in. The category arose later when some were clearly half-and-half..</div> </div> </div> </div>And they were always second-class to Penninsulares or Creoles one they were established in teh casta system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aztecs: ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Cortes was a liar, thief, gambler, and kind of a monster. That he was also good at playing local politics doesn't suddenly excuse him or make him good. The Spanish destroyed the Aztec and Incan civilizations for silver, slaves and plunder. Maybe they were on their own courses, but the continents were depopulated and their land stolen and cultures destroyed to enrich some folks back in Lisbon and Madrid. That's Empire to a T and pretty assholish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Famine: ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This didn't require the destruction of the Incas, yet Pizarro still well, did. Nor did they need slaves in Colombia to cultivate sugar and coffee, yet they did. The Columbian Exchange doesn't jusitfy European New World Imperialism, and I am confused as to how you think potatos solve the destroying of Cusco.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Legend: ...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is again, post-hoc. By twenty years, most of the population was subjugatd, the civilizations destroyed and in some cases, the people effectivley extinct. &quot;That folks felt bad&quot; again, seems to be looking for silver lining here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Colonialism had lots of negatives - but it also spread <b>infrastructure</b>, spread <b>democracy</b>, created modern <b>medicine </b>(all those foreign bugs &amp; diseases killing everyone).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nine tenths of two continents peoples died. Most of the post-colonial states have become single-party dictatorships or anarchies since a lot of the infrastructure was for the benefit of colonial interests, not for the people living in those places. Many of the democracies that do flourish didso <i>to resist</i> foreign rule, as in the case of India. Many 19th Century and early 20th Century imperialists were in fact, pretty explictly anti-democratic. Modern medicine doens't require fammines in Bengal, genocides in Armenia, or CIA-backed coups in Iran.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>(Language stuff.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The world will always have trade langauges. I fail to see how &quot;we can now all talk to eachother&quot; holds when well, we don't (you just listed eight langaueges there) and folks seemed to be able to conduct complex international trade without such langauges. And likely the world tends to lingua francas anyhow, so I don't see how colonialism justifies any of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TLDR - Don't drink the kool-aid that you have to loathe your ancestors (and anyone who looks remotely like them). The world was always full of shitty people, Europe was invaded for almost a thousand years - and then they got lucky on a coin toss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Europe got beat up thousans of years ago doesn't justify Europe and its favorite colonies fucking up a lot of other places of the globe in the last two centuries. Folks don't have to hate their ancestors or themselves. Folks like me also don't want folks to pretend that racism doesn't exist or that it all is justified in the end, which you seem fine with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your intentions are good - but we don't need to diminish science for &quot;equality&quot;. Everyone is special in different ways - but that difference is <b>why</b> diversity is good (if it was something insignificant, like hair-color, then diversity would be worthless).</div> </div> </div> </div>The big thing to remember is that while the small amount determines a lot, it is also worth noting that what that is doesn't map onto clear racial divisonis. Humans are not just not very diverse, we have always had lots of high admixture in the grand scale of things. Humans as a population are not isolated long enough for the diversity to be more than just subsequent sampling and slight gene-flow events. It's not about equality. It's about why race as a genetic construct is pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biological Essentialism [/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>Bio-essentialism's sin isn't that it assumes our behavior has some genetic or physical cause. It's that it assumes that cause is entirely genetic. Environment plays enormous factors in the development, and potential success of indivdiuals. Bio-essentialism is often a way to do what you just say: It's genetic, so nothing can be done. It's more an excuse, often, to justify not doing policies which help the needy or disadvantaged by blaming them for their failings, rather than enviornment, opportunity, or institutions. Genetics means nothing without an enviornment to perate in.<br /> <br /> That and well, as I have said, there's no races genetically. Humans have had too mcuh gene flow for races to mean much as a genetic category, again, save as a series of subsets of populations in the human speices htat sitll have mixing with other groups over the centuries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...<br /> Likewise with Spanish. If I mention Celia Cruz and Willy Chirino, most of us would know them as <b>Cubans</b>, not &quot;black female, white male&quot;. They made <i>Cuban</i> music. Haitians don't have any special &quot;dibs&quot; on Celia - nor do Romanians get &quot;dibs&quot; on Willy.<br /> <br /> My aunt is &quot;white&quot; - her daughter is &quot;black&quot; - the grandson is &quot;white&quot;. What good is a &quot;race&quot; definition if mother-and-child aren't even in the same categories?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because while they are not real biological constructs, they are realized societally and people will be treated differently for it. I am not treated like my brother who looks blacker is treated, and his son will not be treated like him growing up because he looks more East Asian. Just saying they don't exist doesn't make them not exist culturally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213625#post1213625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>(Whiteness stuff)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So the thing to remember with whiteness, at least as I perceive it as a non-white American, is that it's not actually a race, per se, like it is often used for other categories. It is a lack of race for a lot of socieites, and very distinct extra layer of status and power perpetuated with European colonialsm. That it in itself doesn't t advantage white folk in the world today doesn't mean it doesn't exist. And note, that white people decided the terms of who was what, and that many racial categories in the world are thsoe defined by white people in teh 17th through 19th Centuries. It was the Spanish who introduced the casta system to the Phillipines and Latin America, based on race. You were black even if you were Bantu, Koi, Pygmy, or Zulu, not according ot them, but according to the Europeans. Folks were Asian because that's what the Europeans called folks with a certain set of ethnic traits. And folks could stop being white as needed, as the Irish for the English, Turks for Germans today, or many Latinos in the United States.<br /> <br /> &quot;They don't call themselves that&quot; is a canard. That folks are that and that it is a thing at all was because white people came in and said that was the case. It is a label given to many fo the world, adn it is something that was used to build institutions that still affect the world. You are again going a bit in the solipsistic &quot;I don't see what you're talking about so it's not real&quot; bullshit that is often used to claim &quot;race blind&quot; policy or what have you. Again, these people didn't define the terms. But the world has been affected and as a result, has to navigate them.<br /> <br /> I frankly have no clue wha thte hell is up on the ork stuff. But I will conclude that while you think folks like might be white knighting, I think you are coming from a position that if anything, seems to me Euro-centric, colonial-apologetic and pretentiously race-blind. It affects a lot of how your post read to me here, and so drew my want to respond. Just because you don't understand a thing doesn't mean that folks might not be talking about it right. You might just not know what you mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T23:19:21-07:00","id":1213681,"title":"","content":"(doublepost?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 05-02-2018, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T23:21:38-07:00","id":1213682,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar353_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"353\" data-vbnamecard=\"353\">Blaque</a> I sincerely <i>adore</i> your response - it's precisely the kind of criticism I like. <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>re: White Knighting &amp; Criticism</b><br /> I agree with you - and I'm 100% happy with criticism - so long as it isn't <b>censorship</b>. Right? My <i>cringe</i> are people who want to silence all taboo topics (instead of giving everyone the benefit of the doubt, let someone trip over their words without devouring them, etc).<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Back-and-Forth on Colonialism</b><br /> <br /> <b>re: Guilt</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">You're right - two wrongs don't make a right. But if you see a domestic abuse victim punched for 7 years - and then she <i>snaps </i>and stabs her spouse - you generally don't go &quot;it was all her fault obviously, she's truly the scum of the earth.&quot; <br /> <br /> My point is not to absolve any population of innocence - so much as to make clear that <i>everyone was a bastard</i> - so these discussions shouldn't be framed as &quot;good vs evil&quot; or &quot;innocent vs guilt&quot; but as &quot;winners vs losers&quot;. Because I <b>have</b> dealt with people who <i>legitimately</i> believe whites &quot;have no soul&quot; and are all monsters incarnate.<br /> <br /> Europe happened to get it's ass kicked for a few centuries - and then turned around to repay the favor. Had the Maghreb <b>not invaded</b>, the prohibitions against slavery would have likely <i>stayed in effect</i> (as they did for the 700 years that preceded) and the provinces <i>would have probably</i> remained fractured (<b>even today</b> Spain is full of separatist movements). This isn't a moral judgment - it's a cause-and-effect observation.<br /> <br /> Or at the least, when describing &quot;guilt&quot;, people need to divide by country. Should a Romanian or Czech feel responsibility for what the Dutch did? Should the Spanish (who intermarried) be on par with the English (who had miscegeneration laws until the mid 1990s)? Should the French (who <i>were the worst</i>) be compared to anyone else? Specificity is important.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>re: West Africa</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Horn of Africa got a raw deal - <b>and it still does</b>. But it's not Europeans hanging out in 2018.<ul><li><b>The Moors?</b> That's Morocco and Mauritania today. Mauritania claimed to have abolished slavery in 1905, 1961, 1981.... but Arab Muslims (the bidanes) still own slaves (the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haratin\" target=\"_blank\">haratines</a>). As recently as 2015 they were still <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/the_slatest/2015/01/15/biram_dah_abeid_mauritanian_anti_slavery_activist_sentenced_to_two_years.html\" target=\"_blank\">arresting anti-slavery activists</a>. They &quot;outlawed&quot; slavery but opt not to inform the slaves, instead letting some believe they will &quot;<a href=\"https://www.timesofmalta.com/articles/view/20070921/opinion/a-view-from-the-edge.4427\" target=\"_blank\">not go to paradise if they disobey</a>&quot;.</li> <li><b>The Barbary?</b> That's Libya, which was all over the news <a href=\"http://time.com/5042560/libya-slave-trade/\" target=\"_blank\">last year</a>. There are a lot of parallels with Central American &quot;coyotes&quot; (human smugglers) - <b>except</b> that the Berber Libyans don't consider people south of the Sahara kin (so the abuse is more horrific).</li> <li><b>Sudan </b>also has problems - with <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20080923220548/http://archives.cnn.com/2000/US/09/05/state.dept.religion/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">government-sponsored conversion to Islam</a>. Northern Sudanese Arabs enslaving their &quot;African&quot; neighbors. And we're talking the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slavery_in_Sudan#Modern-day_slavery\" target=\"_blank\">1990s</a> - when the UN criticized the situation, the slavers claimed the UN was &quot;persecuting their religion&quot;.</li> <li><b>Saudi Arabia &amp; the Persion Gulf? </b><i>Do I have to link</i> the video of the &quot;migrant worker&quot; hanging from the balcony?</li> </ul>So this is where I approach these topics. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Who needs the lesson in anti-slavery?</b> </span> Is it the self-avowed SJW from Italy who admits to feeling terrible about everything (and very politely tries to dodge a risque topic for fear of eugenics)? <b>Or is it</b> the half-dozen countries who <b>still</b> engage in slavery, like Libyans selling Africans off for organ-harvesting?<br /> <br /> Because <b>being practical</b> - when North Sudan claims &quot;the UN is a bunch of white people persecuting our religion&quot; - just because they want <b>to end slavery</b>..... yeah, I rather those &quot;white people&quot; feel firm and empowered enough to call <i>bullshit</i>, as opposed to shriveling up due to colonial guilt.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of Latin America doesn't run on British Common Law, nor do most folks in the world in Asia. </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on this - <b>but we wish</b>. The majority of my family &amp; friends have all fled Latin America <i>because of the lawlessness</i>. It's not just the enforcement, it's the conception. Cronyism (which is a vice in English) doesn't even have a proper translation in Spanish (because it's almost a virtue - <i>of course you'll hire friends and family</i>). The pro-family, pro-community stuff also easily leads to pro-communism. I love my culture except for the legal systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 9/10s of the population was wiped out from the Americas dude. And the Spanish purposefully gave blankets and left sick people amongst populations. Columbus conducted systematic enslavement and genocide of the natives of Hispaniola, and the Spanish probably are responsible for the collapse of teh Miississippi civilization because they rampaged about, spread disease and left pigs. In the Amazon there is evidence that there might have been complex socieites which were driven to near extinction due to disease and later Spanish ensalvement.<br /> <br /> Theer was no Trail of Tears in the Spanish Americas because the Spanish were more interested in enslavement of locals. They introduced a casta system, which put natives only slightly above black slaves, and forbade local religions. They killed htier kings and burned their libraries. And after the Latin American Revolutions, many of the new nations introduced various laws around race, marginalized native population.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I call bullshit on this one. </div> </div> </div>Multiple points here, but lets give it a go.<br /> <br /> <b>re: 9/10ths &amp; Disease<br /> </b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Intent matters. The Spanish didn't shoot natives for giggles, they were <i>ignorant</i> vectors for death. You can't attribute <i>volition</i> when <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germ_theory_of_disease\" target=\"_blank\">germ theory wasn't proposed until 1546 and then expanded upon in 1762</a>. The Spanish were in the Americas 50-150 years before anyone had a clue.<br /> <br /> I've heard the &quot;small pox blanket&quot; story - but you have the wrong time and place. It was North America, not South - <a href=\"http://www.historynet.com/smallpox-in-the-blankets.htm\" target=\"_blank\">English, French &amp; Swiss</a>, not Spaniards - and 1700-1800s (<b>after</b> germ theory). And it makes no sense to infest your own &quot;potential slave population&quot; - so Spain &amp; Portugal had no desire to start-from-scratch (whereas the North Americans were eager to claim new territory).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>re: Columbus &amp; Slaves vs Encomiendas</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Columbus was a wanker 100% - and when word had spread by his 3rd voyage, he was transported to Spain in chains in 1500. Then imprisoned. Him and his men were eventually freed, but he was stripped of the position of &quot;governor&quot; and the crown refused to give him a percent of any profits thereafter. <br /> <br /> All in all, I agree he got off easy - but Spain didn't approve of him terrorizing his citizens either.<br /> <br /> So we agree there, right?<br /> <br /> The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Encomienda\" target=\"_blank\">encomienda system</a> was more complex than mere slavery. It had antecedents in the tribute systems that Inca and Aztecs demanded from their neighbors - which is why Tlaxcala claimed they couldn't recognize Cortes until the Aztecs were gone. (Tangent: Cortes actually promised Tlaxcala independence from it - so despite him being off-orders, the Spanish Crown still honored his promises to them - skipping the tribute so long as they permitted a priest to teach the language and religion. The deal was honored until Mexico claimed independence altogether.)<br /> <br /> <b>But again - perspective - the alternative was human sacrifice and <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/article/us-mexico-archaeology-skulls-idUSKBN19M3Q6\" target=\"_blank\">temples covered in skulls</a>. </b>The indigenous people <i>allied with Spain</i> for a reason and it's complete fantasy to think everyone <i>misses</i> the Aztecs.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>re: Kings? Religion? Caste?</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Caste system <b>needs nuance. </b>For example, this Casta painting of a &quot;<a href=\"https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-pkqMtGWNNYo/Vr2qaYaNkRI/AAAAAAAAI4Y/NNTJDkC3DXY/s640/castas.png\" target=\"_blank\">black man with a white woman</a>&quot;.<ul><li><b>First</b>, note it says Espa\u00f1ola (meaning &quot;Spaniard&quot;) not Blanca (&quot;White&quot;). The Casta system favored <b>Spanish-ness</b>, not White-ness (and I can show you laws designed to keep French and English away if needed). A Spanish &quot;mulatto&quot; was valued more than a Frenchman.</li> <li><b>Second</b>, note the Black man - and ask how he'd fare in the US even 300 years later? He's not in rags - he's not being lynched - their child is not in chains. The painting depicts him as <b>Spanish</b> by culture and norms. This aligns with the fact that there were <a href=\"http://www.blackpast.org/gah/garcia-juan-1495\" target=\"_blank\">Black Conquistadors</a>.</li> </ul>So yes, the Casta paintings favor Spanish-ness at the top and non-Spanish-ness at the bottom. <b>This is why</b> an African + Native combo was devalued - the &quot;citizen&quot; would not speak the language nor adopt the culture nor know the laws. <b>But you can't</b> compare this with the French (who had laws to re-enslave any black man without a master for 3 years) or the Anglo-Americans (who would be lynching for 400 years more).<br /> <br /> <b>Plus</b> the Caste system had other issues. I'm glad you mention the difference between Peninsulares and Criollos - so you know Criollos were 2nd class citizens compared to Peninsulares. And while the Peninsulares wanted Criollos to intermix with Indios (to create Mestizos) -- the Criollos were fighting alongside Africanos to survive against Indios (making Mulattos a likely mix). <b>It wasn't a ladder</b>, it was a jumble (which is why Bolivar abolished slavery <b>with</b> the Independence Wars). He was a wealthy Criollo raised by an African slave. And he recategorized the &quot;races&quot; as &quot;all Criollos&quot; (regardless of color) vs &quot;all Peninsulares&quot; (who claim fealty to the Crown).<ul><li>Was everything this ideal? Of course not. But this is all <b>leagues</b> ahead of the North American experience with a Civil War, Jim Crow, Miscegenation laws, etc. We have to judge societies by the times they lived in (not modern values).</li> </ul>I can agree that the destruction of religion &amp; kings might suck - <i>but that was kind of the point</i>. Although I find the religion part a little.... nebulous. The entire premise was they were &quot;conquering foreign lands for Christendom&quot; - and some locals (like the Aztecs) I can hardly <i>defend</i> preserving. <b>But what about all the sycnretic religions?</b> The North Americans didn't permit any of that - but in Cuba we still have Santeria; Candomble in Brazil; Hispaniola has Vudu/Vodou; Mexico has Santa Muerte. <b>It must say something</b> that North Americans have <b><i>zero</i></b>such faiths but South America embraced a little paganism (which is why Catholics usually get flack from Protestants).</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All in all, I think we can <b>both agree</b> that life was unpleasant for many.<br /> <br /> I think our main difference is that I'm only interested in cause-and-effect or comparisons - not in passing ethnical judgment. <b>Everyone</b> was shitty, and Aztec human-sacrifice doesn't become a &quot;lost noble tradition&quot; just because they were on the losing side of a conflict.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Folks like me also don't want folks to pretend that racism doesn't exist or that it all is justified in the end, which you seem fine with. </div> </div> </div>Except, I never said anything of the sort? Perhaps you're conflating me with someone?<br /> <br /> If I want to battle racism - I just don't see wisdom in alienating &quot;whites&quot; by saying &quot;you're all somehow benefiting from racism&quot;. Better to double-down harsh on the <i>actually racist</i> and not grief the friendly, awkward ones who are mortified by the idea. This weird &quot;reverse-racism&quot; that some Europeans lash themselves with doesn't accomplish anything except tell well-intentioned people to not speak up. <br /> <br /> I point back to Sudan, Libya, Mauritania, Saudi Arabia, etc - <b>all of which </b>are guilty - but Europeans don't feel they can say anything. <br /> <br /> At one point <b>Libya blamed European self-loathing</b> for their slave markets - arguing that European pro-migrant groups (who don't differentiate between economic migrants and war refugees) were <b>empowering</b> human traffickers by making smuggling easier. (And the problem was that Libya's police couldn't handle such an influx of new gangs). <b>I mean, think on that</b>. They were <i>so worried about doing the right thing</i> - without questioning it - that pro-migrant groups were <b>enabling more human suffering</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's about why race as a genetic construct is pointless. </div> </div> </div>If by &quot;race&quot; you mean the white/black/red/yellow categories - I agree with you 100%.<br /> <br /> But if by &quot;race&quot; you mean &quot;West Africans being susceptible to sickle cell anemia&quot; - eh, no? It's <b>very</b> worthwhile to know what advantages or disadvantages populations deal with, so they can be better treated by the medical establishment. But this is not what you meant? Because this is what <b>I </b>meant. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's that it assumes that cause is entirely genetic. </div> </div> </div>I didn't see that in the definition - but I can see where that is a concern. Thank you!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because while they are not real biological constructs, </div> </div> </div>My point being that the way (culture A) views people <b>isn't</b> uniform throughout the world. <br /> <br /> So yes, Celia and Willy are &quot;black female, white male&quot; in America. But in Cuba, <i>they're Cubans</i>. An American who expects Cuban society to work the way American society does will be disappointed. &quot;Social constructs&quot; exist within very specific societies. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You were black even if you were Bantu, Koi, Pygmy, or Zulu, </div> </div> </div>Agreed - although again, Casta paintings looked at the world as Spanish vs non-Spanish.<br /> <br /> Take Paraguay for example - they made &quot;same race&quot; marriage illegal in <a href=\"http://www.tierraviva.org.py/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Digesto_Normativo_sobre_Pueblos_Indigenas_en_el_Paraguay_1811-20031.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">1814</a> for Europeans in order to get rid of the English and French (knowing they shunned intermarriage). Paraguay sought to create a &quot;new Paraguayan race&quot;. These laws had <b><i>no reason to interest</i> </b>a Bantu or a Brit, an Inca or an Italian - it was purely Spanish-centric. And they were willing to shed their own &quot;whiteness&quot; if it created a more purely &quot;Spanish&quot; mix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I frankly have no clue what the hell is up on the ork stuff. </div> </div> </div>The thread is about <b>fantasy races</b> - and while real-life races are useful, Roswynn and I flipped back-and-forth a lot (including Orcs).<br /> <br /> <b>The point I struggled to make is that </b>even if I dislike Orc stereotypes - and want to play against Orc tropes - the existence of those tropes <b>enriched</b> the character. Playing a stubborn Orc mage investing in a very niche form of magic <b>was way more fun</b> than playing my 235th elven mage (or whatever).<br /> <br /> Kind of how &quot;restrictions inspire art&quot; (easy example: Islamic prohibitions against illustration and statues inspiring amazing calligraphy and mosaic work) - negative stereotypes can inspire more complex characters. I was surprised at how much I enjoyed playing an Orc (who hates Orcish stereotypes).<br /> <br /> <br /> <hr /> <br /> <br /> All in all, thank you for the reply! It was an enjoyable read. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:26:15-07:00","id":1213736,"title":"","content":"I don't have any &quot;nonhuman&quot; peoples in my games. I -do- have peoples that roughly map to D&amp;D elves, orcs and dwarfs.... But they are all human where it counts, since they can interbreed with &quot;standard&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, if examined from a biological perspective, most of the playable humanoid D&amp;D races are, in fact, human, because they can produce fertile offspring with baseline humanity. If two species can produce fertile offspring, then they are close enough to be subspecies of each other.<br /> <br /> Homo sapiens sapiens and homo sapiens neanderthalis, for example. Neanderthals were -not- a different species, as popularly envisioned, but a subspecies of the greater human population. Most Europeans and Asians have some Neanderthal mitochondrial DNA, so interbreeding most definitely took place.<br /> <br /> The &quot;demihuman&quot; peoples are denigrated against by the Immaculate Faith, since physical purity is viewed as being related to spiritual purity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:15:26-07:00","id":1213743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213736#post1213736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any &quot;nonhuman&quot; peoples in my games. I -do- have peoples that roughly map to D&amp;D elves, orcs and dwarfs.... But they are all human where it counts, since they can interbreed with &quot;standard&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, if examined from a biological perspective, most of the playable humanoid D&amp;D races are, in fact, human, because they can produce fertile offspring with baseline humanity. If two species can produce fertile offspring, then they are close enough to be subspecies of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but then the matter of what constitutes a species or subspecies can be confusing to specialists themselves, as shown by the cases of coyotes in North America and golden jackals in Southeast Europe &amp; Asia or african golden wolves (previously jackals) x grey (aka &quot;common&quot;) wolves, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213736#post1213736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Homo sapiens sapiens and homo sapiens neanderthalis, for example. Neanderthals were -not- a different species, as popularly envisioned, but a subspecies of the greater human population. Most Europeans and Asians have some Neanderthal mitochondrial DNA, so interbreeding most definitely took place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last time i checked it seemed there was some division on the issue of sapiens sapiens &amp; neanderthalensis interbreeding. Good to see the matter of evidence reliability has been solved and the doubts are mostly cleared it seems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213736#post1213736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;demihuman&quot; peoples are denigrated against by the Immaculate Faith, since physical purity is viewed as being related to spiritual purity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be, could be not, that argument makes more sense with <b>mutated </b>individuals per se, who deviated from their rightful forms.<br /> <br /> Different places/roles in the cycle could be a different but convenient interpretation for &quot;demihuman&quot;, from the standpoint of the Immaculate Faith, on either the Realm's caste-based society or other nations influenced by alternate takes on the religion like Lookshy, Prasad and others. Mostly depends on what a ST wants to tinker with in a game, i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-09-2020, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T08:38:33-07:00","id":1213802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213736#post1213736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any &quot;nonhuman&quot; peoples in my games. I -do- have peoples that roughly map to D&amp;D elves, orcs and dwarfs.... But they are all human where it counts, since they can interbreed with &quot;standard&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, if examined from a biological perspective, most of the playable humanoid D&amp;D races are, in fact, human, because they can produce fertile offspring with baseline humanity. If two species can produce fertile offspring, then they are close enough to be subspecies of each other.<br /> <br /> Homo sapiens sapiens and homo sapiens neanderthalis, for example. Neanderthals were -not- a different species, as popularly envisioned, but a subspecies of the greater human population. Most Europeans and Asians have some Neanderthal mitochondrial DNA, so interbreeding most definitely took place.<br /> <br /> The &quot;demihuman&quot; peoples are denigrated against by the Immaculate Faith, since physical purity is viewed as being related to spiritual purity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This far along, I think you hit it on the head - and the thread was simply named wrong (partly due to lack-of-vocabulary on my part - partly due to fantasy conventions).<br /> <br /> It seems the best &quot;races&quot; are human-enough to interbreed and relate to - there's little utility in exotic origin stories (unless maybe the Raksha - who aren't actually mortal and only look the part to prey on us). Races like the Dragonborn or Dragon-Kings feel odd to use. Exalted has a few really obscure non-human races, but most exist only as fodder (to explain a ruin here or some underworld monster there).<br /> <br /> The term ethnicity is probably most accurate <b>OOC</b> - while 'race' still works <b>IC</b>. Just because the players/ST know they're all human - doesn't mean that characters should know/believe that as well. And thus &quot;races&quot; like Orcs, Elves, Dwarves, etc are &quot;human&quot; (in so far as they can interbreed, eat the same things, etc etc) - and racial abilities are just ethnic trope short-hand. <br /> <br /> <b>In Exalted terms</b>, instead of telling players &quot;People from Lookshy need War 2 ; the Marukani need Ride 2 ; the Sijanese need Occult 2; people from Nexus need Larceny or Bureaucracy 2&quot; (and thus there's a risk that people overlook ethnicities - because &quot;anyone can have the same stats depending on where you invest them&quot;....<br /> <br /> ...D&amp;D races <b>bake-it-in. </b>A Half-Orc with a +2 to Intimidation isn't merely &quot;just another intimidating human&quot; - he's <i>an ethnic group</i> that is easy to identify, and <b>independent</b> of their individual personality, other groups simply give them wide berth. You could be the sweetest, kindest Orc in D&amp;D - but Elves and Gnomes will still fear you somewhat. <b>And good</b>. If all races are essentially &quot;human&quot;, then you <i>must have</i> chosen an Orc <i>because</i> you want to engage with the trope (and not merely put on green face paint and tusks).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T11:38:39-07:00","id":1213836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were <i>so worried about doing the right thing</i> - without questioning it - that pro-migrant groups were <b>enabling more human suffering</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div> As someone whose worked on the financial side of organisations like that. You're way off on how charities actually work, nobody gets money for anything without completing a project proposal which outlines basic objectives, demand for the project, the kind of budget you're expecting and importantly risks where you need to explore the potential harm of your project.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, human trafficking is the stuff of sensationalist news stories and people of a certain mindset like to see do-gooders fall flat on their face, so they pretend they actually care about this problem. It really needs to be stressed that these gangs existed before they just operated somewhere else that the media didn't care about. People didn't just meet up and go &quot;Europeans are really lax on immigration so I've got a great idea to make money from that... the slave trade!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T14:12:22-07:00","id":1213881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213836#post1213836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As someone whose worked on the financial side of organisations like that. You're way off on how charities actually work, nobody gets money for anything without completing a project proposal which outlines basic objectives, demand for the project, the kind of budget you're expecting and importantly risks where you need to explore the potential harm of your project.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, human trafficking is the stuff of sensationalist news stories and people of a certain mindset like to see do-gooders fall flat on their face, so they pretend they actually care about this problem. It really needs to be stressed that these gangs existed before they just operated somewhere else that the media didn't care about. People didn't just meet up and go &quot;Europeans are really lax on immigration so I've got a great idea to make money from that... the slave trade!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like you're pitching theory against practice. No one is saying that &quot;these gangs came out from no where&quot;. One (of many) articles:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/sep/03/libyan-naval-attack-on-charity-ship-adds-new-danger-to-migrant-rescue\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/8af82ab43e8b82c9f208221605c982b821d61cac/0_133_4000_2399/4000.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdG8tYWdlLTIwMTYucG5n&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=8ac32868e03c0ba418826197eea0f78a\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/sep/03/libyan-naval-attack-on-charity-ship-adds-new-danger-to-migrant-rescue\" target=\"_blank\"> Libyan naval attack on charity ship adds new danger to migrant rescue </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/sep/03/libyan-naval-attack-on-charity-ship-adds-new-danger-to-migrant-rescue\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/sep/03/libyan-naval-attack-on-charity-ship-adds-new-danger-to-migrant-rescue </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Crews fear armed violence as a Libyan naval vessel opens fire in Mediterranean and EU sends in protective seapower </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And I quote:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;A deal cut in the spring between the EU and Turkey has blocked the route to Europe used by 900,000 migrants last year. As a result, smuggling gangs have switched gear, channelling Middle Eastern migrants through </span></span><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/libya\" target=\"_blank\">Libya</a><span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> to join the growing number of Africans making the same journey.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> And thus:<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Libya\u2019s UN-backed government has no security force of its own or the means to police the militias, for whom migrant smuggling is big business. </span></span>&quot;<br /> <br /> Because<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#121212\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The growth of the flotilla of rescue ships from charities across Europe has seen tens of thousands saved from drowning&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> You're saying &quot;no one gets money&quot; for such projects without potential harm assessment - and yet there Libya was saying &quot;you guys are so busy trying to do 'the right thing' in the short-term, you're destabilizing us in the long term&quot;. They want <b>zero</b> ships in their territorial waters so that there is <b>zero</b> encouragement for flotillas. It won't stop migrants - but it could discourage them - and maybe nudge them into going to other countries.<br /> <br /> And by the way, <b>the have the sovereign right to make such declarations</b>. African countries don't lose their sovereignty just because some &quot;well-intentioned&quot; Europeans think they know better about how to help them.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>And similar situation </b>occurred at the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calais_Jungle\" target=\"_blank\">Calais Jungle Camp</a> - off the top of my head:<ul><li><b>Charities weren't local:</b><br /> Locals were infuriated with charities trying to help migrants - because those charities <i>weren't local</i> - and thus those charities had no interest in whether there was a danger to citizens or not. They send aid and help but it was the local towns whose police and hospitals were overworked (because migrants from rival ethnic groups had no qualms about fighting).</li> <li><b>Migrants didn't want asylum:</b><br /> The French offered to help migrants with asylum - <i>and they refused</i> - because the Calais Camp was formed of people who wanted to go to the UK for economic prospects. <b>If you're fleeing a war torn country</b>, you don't usually pick-and-choose when (a) your current host is inviting you to stay and (b) your desired host ditched the EU to keep you out.</li> </ul>So <b>no </b>- I don't believe &quot;charities&quot; are omniscient and benign. Plenty are satisfied to &quot;achieve their mission&quot; and anyone who criticizes them is called &quot;a bigot obviously&quot;. <br /> <hr /><br /> Please feel free to rebut as you wish! I enjoy the feedback. The thread was intended for fantasy-races, but a lot of real-world inspiration has certainly surfaced with the back-and-forth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T14:20:17-07:00","id":1213886,"title":"","content":"In light of so much information being available nowadays, it is not only normal, but advisable, to be very skeptic about charities.<br /> <br /> And the comment about caring about human trafficking somehow has to do with wanting to see do gooders fall on their face is just weird.<br /> <br /> Its like saying that people only care about child rape when churches are involved, and that the child rapists were always here, so we shouldn't care about how the church rules might or might not facilitate this horrible behavior.<br /> <br /> Plain wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:11:24-07:00","id":1213912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213886#post1213886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In light of so much information being available nowadays, it is not only normal, but advisable, to be very skeptic about charities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh <b>absolutely</b>, be sceptical about charitable organisations.<br /> But they tend to be geared up more towards eating up your donation money on administration costs while talking a good game than spending a ridiculous amount of aid money in a foreign country without doing their homework.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the comment about caring about human trafficking somehow has to do with wanting to see do gooders fall on their face is just weird.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you don't believe there's people who wish to see aid initiatives, specifically ones concerning refugees fail because of their personal politics I really do envy you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its like saying that people only care about child rape when churches are involved, and that the child rapists were always here, so we shouldn't care about how the church rules might or might not facilitate this horrible behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except we know how less restrictions on migration aids human traffic. Restrictions on migration wouldn't break up those smuggling rings, it would tell them to go elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:29:02-07:00","id":1213919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213912#post1213912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't believe there's people who wish to see aid initiatives, specifically ones concerning refugees fail because of their personal politics I really do envy you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I know that.<br /> <br /> What is weird is that you say these people would otherwise not care about human trafficking. That is just dehumanizing people with different politics. I could be opposed to free migration and still care very much that people do not suffer human trafficking. It is even worst that a thing I abhor is facilitated by a thing I'm opposed to. It makes it easier for me to be even more forceful against it. Doesn't mean I would otherwise not care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213912#post1213912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except we know how less restrictions on migration aids human traffic. Restrictions on migration wouldn't break up those smuggling rings, it would tell them to go elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how about we get together and make it so there is nowhere they can go, rather just let them operate right here?<br /> <br /> Do you just let pests live in your home because if you treat your house they might go to a neighbor's? What kind of logic is that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:38:32-07:00","id":1213925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213736#post1213736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have any &quot;nonhuman&quot; peoples in my games. I -do- have peoples that roughly map to D&amp;D elves, orcs and dwarfs.... But they are all human where it counts, since they can interbreed with &quot;standard&quot; humans.<br /> <br /> Amusingly, if examined from a biological perspective, most of the playable humanoid D&amp;D races are, in fact, human, because they can produce fertile offspring with baseline humanity. If two species can produce fertile offspring, then they are close enough to be subspecies of each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>One species concept of many. I doubt you'd get much useful reflection out of D&amp;D's contemplation on genetics, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Homo sapiens sapiens and homo sapiens neanderthalis, for example. Neanderthals were -not- a different species, as popularly envisioned, but a subspecies of the greater human population. Most Europeans and Asians have some Neanderthal mitochondrial DNA, so interbreeding most definitely took place.<br /> <br /> The &quot;demihuman&quot; peoples are denigrated against by the Immaculate Faith, since physical purity is viewed as being related to spiritual purity. </div> </div> </div>There were also Denisovians in that archaic hominin mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:58:22-07:00","id":1213935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213912#post1213912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh <b>absolutely</b>, be sceptical about charitable organisations. But they tend to be geared up more towards eating up your donation money on administration costs while talking a good game than spending a ridiculous amount of aid money in a foreign country without doing their homework.</div> </div> </div> </div>You accuse charities of malfeasance - trying to gobble up money for themselves - but then presume that <b>when they do</b> &quot;do something&quot;, it's well-researched and well-planned? That doesn't feel right.<br /> <br /> The Calais Jungle Camp was closed in 2016.<br /> <br /> Here's an article (from 2017) on one of the charities delivering &quot;a third of a ton&quot; of food daily (so despite France <b>closing</b> it, charities <b>continued</b> to flout the law).. <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.express.co.uk/news/world/840130/British-charity-Calais-migrants-David-Davies-UK-France-Germany-Macron\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.images.express.co.uk/img/dynamic/78/750x445/840130.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.express.co.uk/news/world/840130/British-charity-Calais-migrants-David-Davies-UK-France-Germany-Macron\" target=\"_blank\"> Despair as British charity hand out rice for migrants in Calais </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.express.co.uk/news/world/840130/British-charity-Calais-migrants-David-Davies-UK-France-Germany-Macron\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.express.co.uk/news/world/840130/British-charity-Calais-migrants-David-Davies-UK-France-Germany-Macron </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> BRITISH charity workers are handing out more than a third of a ton of rice every day to feed the growing numbers of migrants arriving on the outskirts of Calais. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Even Macron (in 2018) accuses charities of helping migrants avoid police.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2018/01/16/will-no-return-jungle-camp-calais-macron-vows/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/201...s-macron-vows/</a><br /> <br /> <b>So I politely disagree</b>. &quot;Giving out cheap food&quot; - and then leaving the locals to deal with emergency room visits, policing, cleaning up trash, ensuring the local town doesn't have problems - <b>is precisely</b> the kind of mess I expect half-hearteded &quot;do gooders&quot; to create. Locals were afraid to let their daughters walk to school (after a bunch of <i>other incidents</i>). <br /> <br /> These charities are not local - and they have <b>no</b> compassion for the locals. Their self-loathing is &quot;so real&quot;, they'll support <i>clear economic migrants</i> even if it <i>hurts</i> the local population who was previously minding it's own business. I cannot fathom this short-term &quot;feel good&quot; mentality - because in the long term it only increases hostilities to migrants. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213912#post1213912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't believe there's people who wish to see aid initiatives, specifically ones concerning refugees fail because of their personal politics I really do envy you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's &quot;people want aid initiatives to fail&quot; so much as &quot;they got called bigots for years - and now they're vindicated - so yes, relief&quot;.<br /> <br /> Again - Calais. It was <b>years</b> that the locals had to deal with the problem (they bulldozed it in 2009 and had to keep re-clearing it) - <b>so of course</b> they're happy when charities get caught <i>breaking the law</i> - because they've known it for years and were ignored. <br /> <br /> I'm in the US and I saw a lot of friends (<b>all </b>immigrants) <i>switch sides</i> politically because they got <i>tired</i> of every taboo-topic resulting in you being called (some variation of bigot) for deviating from &quot;party dogma&quot;. The worst offense being the &quot;do-gooders&quot; who <b>think </b>they know what you want - and then push for the opposite - because the sensible position has already been claimed by a faction they demonize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213925#post1213925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One species concept of many. I doubt you'd get much useful reflection out of D&amp;D's contemplation on genetics, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the interbreeding point went far enough.<br /> <br /> Ditching all the exotic origin stories - the fact that they can interbreed suggests genetic similarity? The origin stories might just be regional religious tales.<br /> <br /> IE, for an Exalted-version, the lesson would be that <b>out-of-character</b>, all playable characters are humans with some odd regional mutations (based on exposure to manses, the shadowlands, to whatever). But <b>in-character</b>, play up fantastic stories. Revisiting An-Teng (where the snakemen are OOC beastmen - but IC seen as a half-divine race - really cemented the idea home).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:48:37-07:00","id":1213963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213919#post1213919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is weird is that you say these people would otherwise not care about human trafficking. That is just dehumanizing people with different politics. I could be opposed to free migration and still care very much that people do not suffer human trafficking. It is even worst that a thing I abhor is facilitated by a thing I'm opposed to. It makes it easier for me to be even more forceful against it. Doesn't mean I would otherwise not care.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is this hypothetical person skeptical of aid agencies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then how about we get together and make it so there is nowhere they can go, rather just let them operate right here?</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you elabourate on this? What you appear to be proposing doesn't seem that far away from world peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you just let pests live in your home because if you treat your house they might go to a neighbor's? What kind of logic is that?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe that European law enforcement agencies are (generally speaking) better equipped to handle human trafficking rings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T17:26:53-07:00","id":1213977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213935#post1213935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the interbreeding point went far enough.<br /> <br /> Ditching all the exotic origin stories - the fact that they can interbreed suggests genetic similarity? The origin stories might just be regional religious tales.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's D&amp;D. Its brand of fantasy involves lots of boring monocultures and often shoves literal divine origins into the setting, such as the reasoning for the elf vs. orc conflict, or really pretty much any demihuman vs. its &quot;evil counterpart&quot; conflicts - it writes it off as the gods doing it. If you're looking for something that relates to real life, you're probably better off looking for another setting cluster and system, because D&amp;D is thoroughly its own genre, and it only simulates and games for said genre<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IE, for an Exalted-version, the lesson would be that <b>out-of-character</b>, all playable characters are humans with some odd regional mutations (based on exposure to manses, the shadowlands, to whatever). But <b>in-character</b>, play up fantastic stories. Revisiting An-Teng (where the snakemen are OOC beastmen - but IC seen as a half-divine race - really cemented the idea home). </div> </div> </div>What's perhaps far more important about how the Serpents Who Walk As Men are perceived is that they don't have vital mining or farmland operations that would be more profitable for outsiders, so they get written off as god-blooded (with a lower class who have kinship ties to surrounding communities and fewer ophidian traits). Rest assured that if they had jade mines, the Realm probably would have swooped in and declared them Anathema-spawn or illegal children of the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T18:13:59-07:00","id":1213989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213963#post1213963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is this hypothetical person skeptical of aid agencies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would this matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213963#post1213963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you elabourate on this? What you appear to be proposing doesn't seem that far away from world peace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Create laws that would make people not want to be trafficked to get to Europe and only go where they are lawfully allowed to? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213963#post1213963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that European law enforcement agencies are (generally speaking) better equipped to handle human trafficking rings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah, create a problem and let it keep existing because I am the one who can handle it best. makes total sense.<br /> <br /> Let me guess, European Law will handle it by making every trafficked person a well adjusted citizen with every right and duty that that entails right? <br /> <br /> What was it that caused all this trafficking again? People wanting to get to a better place to live a better life, breaking any laws they have to and feeling entitled to it? Was that it?<br /> <br /> What is the solution here? No borders? No property? Talk about rainbows and world peace, will ya?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T18:29:39-07:00","id":1214861,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You guys are getting way off topic with the human trafficking discussion. It's gone in a rather distasteful direction so it either stops or the mods will take whatever we feel to be appropriate action.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:16:23-07:00","id":1215822,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I stay away for a couple days and you folks manage to have some great debate about race, colonialism, imperialism, slavery... and also get a mod to almost shut the thread down. I'm almost envious.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I would've liked being here and discussing these things, but I was damn busy. AFAIK this coming week will be more of the same.<br /> <br /> Let's see whether I can give you my opinions on a couple points you make...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>re: White Knighting &amp; Criticism</b><br /> I agree with you - and I'm 100% happy with criticism - so long as it isn't <b>censorship</b>. Right? My <i>cringe</i> are people who want to silence all taboo topics (instead of giving everyone the benefit of the doubt, let someone trip over their words without devouring them, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I usually hear the term &quot;White Knight&quot; from alt-reich jerks who want to shut up a feminist ally by saying he's defending feminism only to appear attractive to us women, but if this is another definition, honestly, fuck taboo topics. Let's hash things out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>re: Guilt</b><br /> [spoiler]You're right - two wrongs don't make a right. But if you see a domestic abuse victim punched for 7 years - and then she <i>snaps </i>and stabs her spouse - you generally don't go &quot;it was all her fault obviously, she's truly the scum of the earth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But that's not the case for Europe. We weren't punched for 7 years, and we didn't just stab our spouse. Our societies evolved in a very stimulating, dog-eat-dog environment with lots of advantages (horses, rich food, easily domesticable vegetable fare, a sort of balkanization encouraging everyone to develop better and better weapons, a hot mix of deadly diseases we were among the very few people resistant to, the list goes on forever but it's all a string of coincidences). People from Europe weren't enslaved en masse and deported across the ocean. People from Europe weren't destroyed by foreign diseases, or opium, or alcoholics. It's not like our racist and white supremacist elements arose because of a series of crimes committed towards us by People of Color. It's actually like this: at a certain point in history - and we're still going strong - we wanted to expand our empires. So we started planting our nice banners all around the world. Of course people didn't want to be conquered, but we were totally fine, because we <i>invented that they were not people</i>. They were subhumans, &quot;half devil, half child&quot;, savages, needing Christianity, and civilization, etc. We did that to: all of America; a huge part of Africa (all of it?); China; India; South-East Asia; Australia and Oceania.<br /> <br /> They hadn't punched us for 7 years. Most of them we didn't even know existed. We just saw a way to enrich ourselves and started spinning our narrative, stamping out religions, paying bounties for scalps, giving away opium and alcoholics, stealing away whole generations, confining tribes and nations to reserves...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is not to absolve any population of innocence - so much as to make clear that <i>everyone was a bastard</i> - so these discussions shouldn't be framed as &quot;good vs evil&quot; or &quot;innocent vs guilt&quot; but as &quot;winners vs losers&quot;. Because I <b>have</b> dealt with people who <i>legitimately</i> believe whites &quot;have no soul&quot; and are all monsters incarnate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes, okay, blanket statements... are blanket statements. Check <a href=\"https://it.pinterest.com/pin/427067977159198379/\" target=\"_blank\">this video by Rachel Bloom</a>. Okay, sure, there are people who think all whites have no souls. There are also people who think all Muslims have no souls. Or that races shouldn't interbreed (a woman in my art class: &quot;God made us different for a reason&quot;... ugh). Also true we whites have not exactly engendered a lot of good will through the years, I mean, it's not like exaggerated reactions to our colonialism, imperialism, racism, supremacism, oh shit the list goes on and on, see?<br /> <br /> As for &quot;everyone was a bastard&quot;... see above - how many races do you know that have perpetrated crimes against humanity on our scale? I mean sure, many people are bastards (mostly people in positions of power... b/c it invariably corrupts), but there's bastard and <b>BASTARD</b>. You dig?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Europe happened to get it's ass kicked for a few centuries - and then turned around to repay the favor. Had the Maghreb <b>not invaded</b>, the prohibitions against slavery would have likely <i>stayed in effect</i> (as they did for the 700 years that preceded) and the provinces <i>would have probably</i> remained fractured (<b>even today</b> Spain is full of separatist movements). This isn't a moral judgment - it's a cause-and-effect observation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Again, not really. They never kicked our ass. Sure, the Muslims took Spain and Southern Italy, the Mongols took a huge swathe of Russia... compared to our treatment of other people they treated us like delicate flowers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at the least, when describing &quot;guilt&quot;, people need to divide by country. Should a Romanian or Czech feel responsibility for what the Dutch did? Should the Spanish (who intermarried) be on par with the English (who had miscegeneration laws until the mid 1990s)? Should the French (who <i>were the worst</i>) be compared to anyone else? Specificity is important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Depends on the individual. My country has a small history of colonialism and imperialism in Africa (Benito Mussolini, that charming gentleman - hey, do you know a lot of Italians still pine for him? Like a lot! Those were good times!) and we went there with gas and flamethrowers to kill soldiers and civilians while faking that we were bringing Italian Civilization. So nice of us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Who needs the lesson in anti-slavery?</b> </span> Is it the self-avowed SJW from Italy who admits to feeling terrible about everything (and very politely tries to dodge a risque topic for fear of eugenics)? <b>Or is it</b> the half-dozen countries who <b>still</b> engage in slavery, like Libyans selling Africans off for organ-harvesting?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Look, there are peoples everywhere in the world who do ugly, ugly things. There's also a lot of peoples who were ruined by European capitalism and colonialism. And the West still manipulates many countries. Or we have treaties with the fabulously rich sheiks who have all the oil and employ their people in rather inhumane ways. Point is, the world was probably a bit better before we decided to colonize it. Powerful people are almost always dicks, but we shat a big pile of poop on everyone and said it was good for your complexion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because <b>being practical</b> - when North Sudan claims &quot;the UN is a bunch of white people persecuting our religion&quot; - just because they want <b>to end slavery</b>..... yeah, I rather those &quot;white people&quot; feel firm and empowered enough to call <i>bullshit</i>, as opposed to shriveling up due to colonial guilt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pot calling the kettle black and vice versa?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>re: 9/10ths &amp; Disease<br /> [spoiler]</b>Intent matters. The Spanish didn't shoot natives for giggles, they were <i>ignorant</i> vectors for death. You can't attribute <i>volition</i> when <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germ_theory_of_disease\" target=\"_blank\">germ theory wasn't proposed until 1546 and then expanded upon in 1762</a>. The Spanish were in the Americas 50-150 years before anyone had a clue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, wait, germ theory wasn't absolutely needed by anyone with half a brain to know how diseases spread. Long before germ theory if you had the plague they nailed your door and burned your house with you and your family in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard the &quot;small pox blanket&quot; story - but you have the wrong time and place. It was North America, not South - <a href=\"http://www.historynet.com/smallpox-in-the-blankets.htm\" target=\"_blank\">English, French &amp; Swiss</a>, not Spaniards - and 1700-1800s (<b>after</b> germ theory). And it makes no sense to infest your own &quot;potential slave population&quot; - so Spain &amp; Portugal had no desire to start-from-scratch (whereas the North Americans were eager to claim new territory).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well that's not actually nicer. Considering the horrible conditions Native Americans still live in today...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want to battle racism - I just don't see wisdom in alienating &quot;whites&quot; by saying &quot;you're all somehow benefiting from racism&quot;. Better to double-down harsh on the <i>actually racist</i> and not grief the friendly, awkward ones who are mortified by the idea. This weird &quot;reverse-racism&quot; that some Europeans lash themselves with doesn't accomplish anything except tell well-intentioned people to not speak up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But we do benefit from racism. Sure, don't be too harsh on me, I try not to be racist, and to check my privilege, and so on, and there's a lot of people much better than me, but we do benefit from racism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If by &quot;race&quot; you mean the white/black/red/yellow categories - I agree with you 100%.<br /> <br /> But if by &quot;race&quot; you mean &quot;West Africans being susceptible to sickle cell anemia&quot; - eh, no? It's <b>very</b> worthwhile to know what advantages or disadvantages populations deal with, so they can be better treated by the medical establishment. But this is not what you meant? Because this is what <b>I </b>meant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Race usually refers to Black, white, Latino, Native American, Middle Eastern, South Asian, East Asian, South East Asian, Pacific Islander, Semite... stuff like that. I'm quite sure when people talk about race they're not talking about a given ethnicity's adaptations and biological quirks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1213682#post1213682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thread is about <b>fantasy races</b> - and while real-life races are useful, Roswynn and I flipped back-and-forth a lot (including Orcs).<br /> <br /> <b>The point I struggled to make is that </b>even if I dislike Orc stereotypes - and want to play against Orc tropes - the existence of those tropes <b>enriched</b> the character. Playing a stubborn Orc mage investing in a very niche form of magic <b>was way more fun</b> than playing my 235th elven mage (or whatever).<br /> <br /> Kind of how &quot;restrictions inspire art&quot; (easy example: Islamic prohibitions against illustration and statues inspiring amazing calligraphy and mosaic work) - negative stereotypes can inspire more complex characters. I was surprised at how much I enjoyed playing an Orc (who hates Orcish stereotypes)</div> </div> </div> </div>Aniconism. Same principle in the Immaculate Faith, you just don't depict real life figures. Indeed it can have beautiful results - I remember an old arabic signature that looked a lot like a tiger, but no one could say anything because it was just calligraphy.<br /> <br /> I'm digging how orcs give you inspiration (in TES they're certainly a lot more interesting than in D&amp;D). We also already have some stereotypes in Exalted. Like, if you're a Sesus everyone will think you're a thug and a murderer. If you're a Cynis you'll be seen as an hedonist and slaver. If you're a Marukani they'll say you love horses more than your spouse. I mean you don't need baked in modifiers. And I don't think the devs will add them, unless we're talking Dragon Kings, Mountain Folk, Air People... I agree that most ethnicity might do with a couple tiny merits, but I don't really feel the need, in all honesty, and I doubt it will happen. That said you could start homebrewing something, posting it around here and where other Exalted players congregate, and see what people think.<br /> <br /> Harder restrictions... perhaps it's just because I'm not used to them in Exalted, but it's a little hard to imagine, for humans I mean. Isn't the way their cultures are characterized usually enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T09:12:11-07:00","id":1216163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so I stay away for a couple days and you folks manage to have some great debate about race, colonialism, imperialism, slavery... and also get a mod to almost shut the thread down. I'm almost envious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reason #359 this place beats Reddit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually hear the term &quot;White Knight&quot; from alt-reich jerks who want to shut up a feminist ally by saying he's defending feminism only to appear attractive to us women, but if this is another definition, honestly, fuck taboo topics. Let's hash things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I first - and most frequently - heard it used for when &quot;a guy gives a girl preferential treatment&quot; (especially online, where the only thing that should matter are our ideas, not our genitals). If we believe in gender-equality, then girls don't need special coddling or protection in online debates. <br /> <br /> Then, by extension, it began to apply to all &quot;white knights&quot; who feel a need to &quot;defend&quot; women, minorities, etc - to the point that they think we can't participate in such discussions. In divine irony, it's the 2018 version of &quot;white man's burden&quot;, except it's the far-Left who feel this &quot;duty&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm fond of the term because I give my male friends grief over this all the time. I've literally &quot;hung out with the girls&quot; to grab cocktails and we talk about BJs and politics - but if my friends / their boyfriends show up, the guys self-censor as if their significant others are these dainty, fragile little angels. It makes my eyes want to roll into the back of my skull, lol.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not the case for Europe. We weren't punched for 7 years, and we didn't just stab our spouse. Our societies evolved in a very stimulating, dog-eat-dog environment with lots of advantages (horses, rich food, easily domesticable vegetable fare, a sort of balkanization encouraging everyone to develop better and better weapons, a hot mix of deadly diseases we were among the very few people resistant to, the list goes on forever but it's all a string of coincidences). People from Europe weren't enslaved en masse and deported across the ocean. People from Europe weren't destroyed by foreign diseases, or opium, or alcoholics. It's not like our racist and white supremacist elements arose because of a series of crimes committed towards us by People of Color. It's actually like this: at a certain point in history - and we're still going strong - we wanted to expand our empires. So we started planting our nice banners all around the world. Of course people didn't want to be conquered, but we were totally fine, because we <i>invented that they were not people</i>. They were subhumans, &quot;half devil, half child&quot;, savages, needing Christianity, and civilization, etc. We did that to: all of America; a huge part of Africa (all of it?); China; India; South-East Asia; Australia and Oceania.<br /> <br /> They hadn't punched us for 7 years. Most of them we didn't even know existed. We just saw a way to enrich ourselves and started spinning our narrative, stamping out religions, paying bounties for scalps, giving away opium and alcoholics, stealing away whole generations, confining tribes and nations to reserves...</div> </div> </div> </div>You're only talking 500 years ago (when the New World period started).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dum_Diversas\" target=\"_blank\">Dum Diversas</a> was a <b>reaction</b> to the Eastern invasion of Europe (by the Ottomans) and the Western invasion of Europe (by the various Caliphates for 700 years). <i>The founding document that re-authorized slavery was a response</i>. There are books on <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=zsQ2DwAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PT164&amp;lpg=PT164&amp;dq=basque+slaves&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=ohmWZ7slA0&amp;sig=tkqedkbs9jEFSUOG4ABFoto8Mqw&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjv46n-5vPaAhUjwlkKHaoTAykQ6AEIYTAI#v=onepage&amp;q=basque%20slaves&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">Female Slaves in Islamic History</a> - and yes, from Andalusia to the Basque, they took Europeans as slaves. This isn't some obscure fact either - my friend and I (both Hispanic, both Arabic-studying) have looked at it (I hadn't realized how prevalent Basque slaves were until he explained how it resulted in the &quot;whitening&quot; of the Berber leadership to the point that over centuries they began looking more Spanish than North African). <br /> <br /> <b>The problem is</b> that every culture likes to focus on their glories - not on their losses. It's more flattering to say &quot;Spain kicked ass for 2-3 centuries&quot; than &quot;Spain was preyed upon for 7 centuries&quot;. So people forget <b>where</b> the ass-kicking originated from.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to talk about the British or French or whoever? Go for it. But I sustain:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>the religious re-authorization of slavery <b>originated</b> as a reaction to invasions</li> <li>I can't condemn the initial &quot;victor&quot; countries who had been &quot;victims&quot; for the better half of a millennia</li> <li>I can't blame &quot;all Europeans&quot; (including those without colonies) for the handful of major empires</li> </ol><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for &quot;everyone was a bastard&quot;... see above - how many races do you know that have perpetrated crimes against humanity on our scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mongols? Entire nations eradicated. Exterminated the half the Mongol tribes, genocide in Afghanistan - in Assyria, killed all the Christians, tons of Muslims &amp; Jews.<br /> <br /> The Chinese General Ran Min exterminated the Wu Hu for having &quot;high bridged noses and bushy beards&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Armenian Genocide was Turkish; the Rape of Nanking was Japanese; the Rwandan genocide was Hutu vs Tutsi. <br /> <br /> Lack of power does not denote a lack of will. <br /> <br /> The rest of the world isn't &quot;less murderous&quot; than Europe - the only difference is <i>reach</i>. There are plenty of modern atrocities going on, unrelated to Europe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">compared to our treatment of other people they treated us like delicate flowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a grotesque &quot;white-washing&quot; of history. They took <a href=\"http://Trade and traders in Muslim Spain, Fourth Series, Cambridge University Press, 1996.\" target=\"_blank\">slaves in Spain</a> half-a-thousand years before Columbus was ever born. They took women as sex slaves to the point that they <i>recolored their own bloodlines</i>. <br /> <br /> They were bad enough that - 2,000 years after the Romans &quot;unified&quot; the Iberian peninsula - regional rivalries and separatist movements remain strong...... yet 500 years ago, they were willing to put those aside just to get rid of the invaders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the individual. My country has a small history of colonialism and imperialism in Africa (Benito Mussolini, that charming gentleman - hey, do you know a lot of Italians still pine for him? Like a lot! Those were good times!) and we went there with gas and flamethrowers to kill soldiers and civilians while faking that we were bringing Italian Civilization. So nice of us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> You use &quot;us&quot; loosely - I don't see how Roswynn in 2018 is guilty of Mussolini or whoever else.<br /> <br /> And I disagree <b>even more</b> at the idea that a Bosnian is held responsible for Italy - or that a Ukrainian is responsible for France - or that (any country) is guilty for what (another country) has done. Should we blame the Chinese for Japan's behavior in Nanking? Are the Azerbaijani guilty of the Armenian genocide? Do we blame Egypt for Rwanda just because they're on the same continent?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><i><b>Who needs the lesson in anti-slavery?</b> </i></span><i>Is it the self-avowed SJW from Italy who admits to feeling terrible about everything (and very politely tries to dodge a risque topic for fear of eugenics)? </i><b>Or is it</b><i> the half-dozen countries who </i><b>still</b><i> engage in slavery, like Libyans selling Africans off for organ-harvesting?</i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, there are peoples everywhere in the world who do ugly, ugly things. There's also a lot of peoples who were ruined by European capitalism and colonialism.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that in 2018, I don't think (someone like Roswynn) needs lessons on &quot;slavery is bad&quot; more than <i>modern slavers</i>. Sorry, but I simply don't think <b>you</b> are the problem to focus on in 2018. You seem nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pot calling the kettle black and vice versa?</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, wait, germ theory wasn't absolutely needed by anyone with half a brain to know how diseases spread. Long before germ theory if you had the plague they nailed your door and burned your house with you and your family in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you're presuming.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The second</b> the Spanish got off a boat - the locals were doomed. The Spanish had <b>zero forewarning</b> to guess that the locals would be vulnerable (because <i>everywhere else they went</i>, foreign peoples <i>weren't</i> vulnerable - this was a completely new situation in the Americas).<br /> <br /> <b>And again, English and Spanish history are different</b>. <br /> <br /> The Anglo Saxons had the &quot;Trail of Tears&quot;, &quot;Thanksgiving&quot; and the whole &quot;Wild West&quot; genre - conflict between European vs Native <i>was a thing</i>. <br /> <br /> <b>By contrast</b>, the first Spaniards in the Caribbean (100 years before the English ever sailed) had no way of knowing the Taino would die-off by <i>mere contact. </i>When Cortes (and his native allies) fought the Aztecs - it's recorded that the Aztecs were <i>already weak from a plague and famine.</i><br /> <br /> And note - the Anglo Saxons <b>prohibited </b>&quot;</span></span></span>miscegenation&quot; <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- for the Spanish, it was <i>policy. </i>The Tainos were doomed on contact - but their blood is still a large part of Puerto Rico and the Dominican Republic. Modern Mexicans are (on average) 45% Native, 45% Spanish and 10% African. The Human Genome project had a thing exploring LATAM's mixing.<br /> <br /> It boggles my mind for people to suggest that people <i>intermarrying with the locals as policy</i> are <b>equal</b> to people <i>trying to wipe out the locals entire lineage</i>.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well that's not actually nicer. Considering the horrible conditions Native Americans still live in today...</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that &quot;intermarrying with the intent to produce a new race&quot; <b>is nicer</b> than &quot;genocide&quot;. What on earth is worse than genocide?<br /> <br /> Please explain how North American natives (who were killed and displaced and live on plantations) are <b>better off</b> than South Americans (who have dual-heritages and entire countries unto themselves)? <br /> <br /> Most of my friends are Hispanic - from different countries - with different mixes. Our regional rivalries are <i>nothing</i> compared to the way North Americans treat one another. Our cultures are much more mixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sure, don't be too harsh on me, I try not to be racist,</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my <b>entire point!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Race usually refers to Black, white, Latino, Native American, Middle Eastern, South Asian, East Asian, South East Asian, Pacific Islander, Semite... stuff like that. I'm quite sure when people talk about race they're not talking about a given ethnicity's adaptations and biological quirks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is different from my experience - but hey, we're in different countries/cultures! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1215822#post1215822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We also already have some stereotypes in Exalted. I mean you don't need baked in modifiers. That said you could start homebrewing something, posting it around here and where other Exalted players congregate, and see what people think.<br /> <br /> Harder restrictions... perhaps it's just because I'm not used to them in Exalted, but it's a little hard to imagine, for humans I mean. Isn't the way their cultures are characterized usually enough?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem is (and the source of this whole thread) is that - as I read more 2E vs 3E - 2E conflated OOC and IC knowledge.<br /> <br /> I mean, <i>it makes sense</i>. There has to be a god or Sidereal who <i>knows</i> everything about certain topics. <b>But it's</b> not helpful for a brand-new player who just needs a quick-and-dirty regional vibe.<br /> <br /> <b>And it does exist to an extent</b> - but usually for Dragon-Blooded - with &quot;required stats&quot; for Dynasts and Lookshy. <b>So all I want</b> is to extend it to other major cities. <br /> <br /> I've also been looking at <b>13th Age</b> which builds it's setting using &quot;13 NPCs&quot; (a king, a druid, an infernalist, etc). I'm a huge fan of strong tropes.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> All in all, thanks for writing back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This has been a fun back-and-forth (and certainly helped clarify what to try / avoid when putting together fantasy ethnicities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T16:33:38-07:00","id":1216374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>And it does exist to an extent</b> - but usually for Dragon-Blooded - with &quot;required stats&quot; for Dynasts and Lookshy. <b>So all I want</b> is to extend it to other major cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is no longer true. Third Edition Dragon-Blooded character generation does not have required stats of any kind save for the fact that you have to have one dot in your Favored Abilities, which is true of every group which possesses Favored Abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T16:59:05-07:00","id":1216383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't see how Roswynn in 2018 is guilty of Mussolini or whoever else.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The past can't be changed, but cultural legacy can still inform actions in the present and the future. I imagine that of those people Roswynn mentioned that pine for the Fascists, some of them engage in active violence in accordance with that ideology, and many others tolerate or turn a blind eye to that.<br /> <br /> I think at least one reason that Americans can still be hung up on race is because marches by actual Nazis are still things that happen there, as well as all kinds of institutionalized marginalization and violence with skewed demographics on the basis of race.<br /> <br /> The past is not a different country. Things get set in motion.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T21:04:40-07:00","id":1216473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216374#post1216374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is no longer true. Third Edition Dragon-Blooded character generation does not have required stats of any kind save for the fact that you have to have one dot in your Favored Abilities, which is true of every group which possesses Favored Abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, all Dragon-Blooded get a more impressive, Solar-level spread of Attribute dots, regardless of where they were raised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T06:38:17-07:00","id":1216613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216374#post1216374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is no longer true. Third Edition Dragon-Blooded character generation does not have required stats of any kind save for the fact that you have to have one dot in your Favored Abilities, which is true of every group which possesses Favored Abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have required specialities* depending on their educational background. All Lookshyans either have a speciality in War and Integrity, or War and Lore, or Integrity and Lore.<br /> <br /> *Well, choose 2 from a list of 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> If that's what you want to do, Salagism, you could. Give all Sijanese specialties in Lore, Medicine or Occult. Give all Coralese* specialties in Athletics, Melee or Sail.<br /> Or whatever.<br /> That seems enough to represent cultural stereotypes without limiting players.<br /> <br /> But I'll admit, it seems pretty unnecessary to me. I mean, character gen is flexible enough (more so than DnD) that if your swordsmen comes from a tribe of canoe-riding fisherfolk you can just give him Sail, you don't need the rules to tell you that his culture means he starts with 1 dot of Sail.<br /> <br /> And I mean, you can already play against stereotypes. I played a sorcerer from Medo. Everyone expected him to be a horse-riding archer who lived in a yurt, not a sorcerer with Lore 5 who was rubbish at both archery and horse-riding (which the other PCs constantly mocked him for).<br /> <br /> *What is the adjective for people from Coral? Or Nexus? Or Wavecrest? Or the Lap? This has suddenly opened up a new question I didn't previously consider.<br /> <br /> <br /> But to go back to the original point of races with a distinct culture, I don't see why you can't do that with beastmen or other mutants. Everyone knows Elkmen are mystics, and wolfmen are savage raiders. So you can be a greedy Elkman merchant, or an intellectual wolfman.<br /> <br /> I think, essentially, things like Orcs, Dwarves, Elves, etc, have much more thematic weight in terms of stereotypes. Everyone knows elves are aloof and artistic and like trees, because they've read tons of books in which elves are like that.<br /> And that's not a problem Exalted can really solve. If Exalted had the magical Blah-di-blah race who were well-known for being honourable yet ferocious warriors and worship a cat goddess and love getting incredibly drunk... that's just not going to be as deeply embedded into player's minds as Elves or Dwarves or whatever.<br /> (And in fact, often when authors make very distinct fantasy races, people go &quot;Oh, those are Elves&quot;, or &quot;Oh, it's Dwarves, they've just changed some stuff.&quot; For example, Melniboneans are often considered elves by readers. Any race of short guys who are good at making things is going to be considered to be a derivative of dwarves.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-08-2018, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T09:02:40-07:00","id":1216690,"title":"","content":"I think what you're referring to is what TVTropes calles &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FiveRaces\" target=\"_blank\">the Five Race</a>s&quot;:<ul><li><b>Stout (Dwarf)</b> - hyper masculine features, more warlike, industrious - <b>can include</b> warlike aliens, robots - strength, honor, martial values</li> <li><b>Fairy (Elf/Angel) - </b>high magic or technology - hyper feminine usually (long hair, delicacy, ranged weapons) - psionics, monster girls</li> <li><b>Mundane (Human) </b>- least magical, jack-of-all-trades, what most identify with</li> <li><b>High Men (High Elf/Human) </b>- most powerful (magically or technologically) - precursor races in speculative fiction - empires at their peak</li> <li><b>Cute (Hobbit or Gnome) </b>- weak but clever, fun, trickster - the newest of the 5 types</li> </ul>But these aren't foreign to White Wolf games. <b>Werewolves</b> were Stouts, <b>Vampires</b> were Fairies, <b>Mages </b>were High Men, <b>Changelings</b> were Cute and <b>Hunters</b> were Mundanes. In Exalted, we roughly map <b>Lunars</b> are Stouts, <b>Solars</b> are High Men, <b>Sidereals</b> are Fairy,<b> Dragon Blooded</b> the Mundane. The 5th (Cute) is omitted (Fair Folk? ha!). Abyssals &amp; Infernals are corrupt Solars (which fits into depictions of &quot;High Men&quot; as precursors and on the verge of decline).<br /> <br /> We have it somewhat in the Castes - although only Dragon-Blooded really have it hard-coded (since they're born and raised within an entire society dedicated to it).<br /> <br /> But you don't need traditional Orcs, Elves, Dwarves, etc.<br /> <br /> Mass Effect was pretty good at hitting the tropes with new races. It takes 30 seconds to see the Krogan are Stouts, the Asari are Fairy, etc.<br /> <hr /><br /> Mechanically, it boils down to:<br /> <br /> All RPGs let the &quot;default character&quot; invest dots around. But do we either:<ul><li>(A) <b>Require</b> dots be invested?<ul><li>This works like in Exalted - where <i>ultimately</i> - a dude from a peaceful village could (hypothetically) &quot;catch up&quot; one day and become a bigger warlord than anyone from Lookshy.</li> </ul></li> <li>(B) <b>Give bonus</b> dots to an ability?<ul><li>This is more ESO/D&amp;D - where built-in bonuses represent biology and a lifetime of culture - no catching up possible (but praise is instead given to those who provide &quot;cross-benefits&quot;.... I think Half-Orcs, for example, aren't &quot;as big/violent&quot; as pure Orcs - but they are smarter and more active during the day due to their human blood - so within human-society they're &quot;strong&quot; but within orc-society they're &quot;shrewd leaders&quot;.</li> </ul></li> </ul><hr /><br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216613#post1216613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*What is the adjective for people from Coral? Or Nexus? Or Wavecrest? Or the Lap? This has suddenly opened up a new question I didn't previously consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wasn't rushing deadlines for ads today, I'd spend a few hours digging up ethnonyms from around the world. What do we liken regional tongues to?<br /> <br /> How big are language families in Exalted?<br /> <br /> For real-world comparisons, you have the Indo-European languages (from India to Britain, linguistics noticing common roots). But for intelligibility, most of the Romance languages can get on pretty well (I speak Spanish - but Italian and Portuguese sound like &quot;cousins&quot; - French a tad artificial). But Latin &gt; Greek &gt; Phoenician &lt; Aramaic &lt; Arabic is another way to link tongues (so even though we use different roots, I found Arabic a lot easier than the Anglos in class.... because we share common syntactic tricks).<br /> <br /> Is it &quot;Sijani&quot;, &quot;Sijanese&quot; or &quot;Sijanian?&quot; Nexian? <br /> <br /> Or for some Spanish ones.... Argentina &gt; Argentinian (English) or Argentino (Spanish)..... Coralino? Chile &gt; Chilean (English) or Chileno (Spanish)....Cuba, Cuban, Cubano.... I mean, I know &quot;words&quot; (like Coral or Lap) sound odd to conjugate, but Argentina is Argent (Silver), Dominican is from Domingo (Sunday), I think Portuguese is from Porto (Port). <br /> <br /> God, I must work on ads. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216613#post1216613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to go back to the original point of races with a distinct culture, I don't see why you can't do that with beastmen or other mutants. Everyone knows Elkmen are mystics, and wolfmen are savage raiders. So you can be a greedy Elkman merchant, or an intellectual wolfman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beastmen are so often depicted as tied to the Lunar Exalted &gt; Silver Pact &gt; edges-of-the-Wyld that I simply loathed using them. Plus their &quot;common origin&quot; <b>as</b> Anathema spawn brings up other odd questions.<br /> <br /> It wasn't until I re-read An-Teng (how the Snake-men aren't even <i>thought of</i> as Beastmen, but misinterpreted as some kind of other race) that I saw Beastmen in a <i>useful</i> light. Like &quot;oh wow, I could turn a niche of Beastmen into a custom race....and the players don't need to know what they are, because the characters won't either&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I'll admit, it seems pretty unnecessary to me. I </div> </div> </div>For the most part, it probably is. But my group is very new to tabletop - and it's easier for them to latch on to a 1-3 paragraph trope - over reading entire chapters of regional history (which most won't do or are too busy to do). <br /> <br /> And with that, I'm off to work. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T12:46:27-07:00","id":1216776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216690#post1216690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these aren't foreign to White Wolf games. <b>Werewolves</b> were Stouts, <b>Vampires</b> were Fairies, <b>Mages </b>were High Men, <b>Changelings</b> were Cute and <b>Hunters</b> were Mundanes. In Exalted, we roughly map <b>Lunars</b> are Stouts, <b>Solars</b> are High Men, <b>Sidereals</b> are Fairy,<b> Dragon Blooded</b> the Mundane. The 5th (Cute) is omitted (Fair Folk? ha!). Abyssals &amp; Infernals are corrupt Solars (which fits into depictions of &quot;High Men&quot; as precursors and on the verge of decline).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, all of the WoD monsters were exactly that - monsters. Their narrative or literary niches were quite different from bands of adventurers as a matter of course; only Changeling could really be said to have it, and they distributed it among various different kiths, though they were still missing AD&amp;D-esque dwarves that had a preferred warrior lifestyle. Likewise, too, types of Exalted don't really fall into this, because they aren't born, but realized from across all of humanity at some point between puberty and... well, before they die of old age; there really isn't much of an upper limit if Karal Fire Orchid comes into the ring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have it somewhat in the Castes - although only Dragon-Blooded really have it hard-coded (since they're born and raised within an entire society dedicated to it). </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't classify any given element as &quot;cute&quot; or higher than the others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you don't need traditional Orcs, Elves, Dwarves, etc. </div> </div> </div>And, indeed, WW is pretty good about killing that trope dead when it isn't twisting it around in Changeling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIf I wasn't rushing deadlines for ads today, I'd spend a few hours digging up ethnonyms from around the world. What do we liken regional tongues to?<br /> <br /> How big are language families in Exalted? </div> </div> </div>Ambiguously large. We're never really given a head count of languages; the four local languages per dot of language family isn't really a good signpost for it, either. A lot of characters seem to be what we would consider extreme polyglots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it &quot;Sijani&quot;, &quot;Sijanese&quot; or &quot;Sijanian?&quot; Nexian? </div> </div> </div>Sijanese and Nexan have shown up in the texts. The former is a derivative of Forest-tongue and the latter of Riverspeak, though both tend to do a lot of business with foreign clients and keep up to date on a wide breadth of foreign customs, so they're going to speak a lot of other languages as a matter of course, which means scads of loanwords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> \u200bBeastmen are so often depicted as tied to the Lunar Exalted &gt; Silver Pact &gt; edges-of-the-Wyld that I simply loathed using them. Plus their &quot;common origin&quot; <b>as</b> Anathema spawn brings up other odd questions. </div> </div> </div>Past lore, not current lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T13:43:55-07:00","id":1216798,"title":"","content":"This conversation seems a little difficult to have around what will actually happen with the game when not everyone is aware of how these things work differently in third edition, honestly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T04:10:36-07:00","id":1217928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216690#post1216690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what you're referring to is what TVTropes calles &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FiveRaces\" target=\"_blank\">the Five Race</a>s&quot;:<br /> ...<br /> Mass Effect was pretty good at hitting the tropes with new races. It takes 30 seconds to see the Krogan are Stouts, the Asari are Fairy, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, I think the &quot;five races&quot; is overcomplicating it.<br /> You're right that Mass Effect was good at establishing trope-led characters (which individual characters can rebel against). But I didn't see &quot;oh, Krogans are like dwarves&quot;. No, Volus are like dwarves.<br /> <br /> Rather, each race had 2-3 distinguishing tropes that were easy to understand;<br /> Krogans - Savage Warriors<br /> Turians - Honourable Warriors<br /> Asari - Magic ladies<br /> Volus - short, fat, wear suits<br /> Quarians - nomadic, hate robots, wear suits<br /> Etc.<br /> Some of those are similar to your &quot;five races&quot;, but I think they're a bit simpler than that.<br /> <br /> So, anyway, for making your own non-human species, I don't think you need to have &quot;elf-like,&quot; &quot;dwarf-like&quot;, etc. You can easily give each one 2-3 clear traits and players will have enough to go on.<br /> For example: <br /> Cunning snake-men who love gold<br /> The huge honourable warrior race<br /> The decadent magical green-skinned race<br /> Furry barbarians who live in trees and worship elephants<br /> <br /> Or whatever. 2-3 traits is enough for each.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How big are language families in Exalted?<br /> <br /> For real-world comparisons, you have the Indo-European languages (from India to Britain, linguistics noticing common roots). But for intelligibility, most of the Romance languages can get on pretty well (I speak Spanish - but Italian and Portuguese sound like &quot;cousins&quot; - French a tad artificial). But Latin &gt; Greek &gt; Phoenician &lt; Aramaic &lt; Arabic is another way to link tongues (so even though we use different roots, I found Arabic a lot easier than the Anglos in class.... because we share common syntactic tricks).<br /> <br /> Is it &quot;Sijani&quot;, &quot;Sijanese&quot; or &quot;Sijanian?&quot; Nexian?<br /> <br /> Or for some Spanish ones.... Argentina &gt; Argentinian (English) or Argentino (Spanish)..... Coralino? Chile &gt; Chilean (English) or Chileno (Spanish)....Cuba, Cuban, Cubano.... I mean, I know &quot;words&quot; (like Coral or Lap) sound odd to conjugate, but Argentina is Argent (Silver), Dominican is from Domingo (Sunday), I think Portuguese is from Porto (Port). </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a very serious question... because I'm talking about English words, and obviously no-one in Exalted speaks English. I doubt people from Wavecrest actually call it Wavecrest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bBeastmen are so often depicted as tied to the Lunar Exalted &gt; Silver Pact &gt; edges-of-the-Wyld that I simply loathed using them. </div> </div> </div>Do you really dislike Lunars? Or just because you set your game far away from the edges of the Wyld?<br /> When I introduced beastmen to a group used to playing DnD, it worked very well, for your purposes. They immediately grasped that cat-people were decadent and arrogant, wolf-people were raiders, pig-people were fat and greedy, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the most part, it probably is. But my group is very new to tabletop - and it's easier for them to latch on to a 1-3 paragraph trope - over reading entire chapters of regional history (which most won't do or are too busy to do). </div> </div> </div>Ah! Now I understand. I didn't really get what the point of all this was.<br /> <br /> In that case, I think your best bet, if you're keen on running Exalted without changing the setting utterly massively, would be to pick where your game is set, and write one to two sentences about each neighbouring country.<br /> <br /> Something like:<br /> Medo: Ghost-worshipping horse-riding nomads. They must give soldiers to the Realm.<br /> Linowan: Like Native North American warrior tribes, they worship the sun, moon, and a tree god. They're allied with the Realm.<br /> Port Calin: A land of peasant farmers ruled by a Shogun. There's lots of political intrigue between daimyos.<br /> Etc. Maybe do about 6 or 7. You could put in some strange race of beastmen people don't know are beastmen, since you liked that, or other mutants. Maybe a country of people who are partially elemental, or partially Fae, or something like that.<br /> That should immediately give them some spaghetti ethnic groups and tropes to pick from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T12:00:08-07:00","id":1218034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1217928#post1217928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I think the &quot;five races&quot; is overcomplicating it. You're right that Mass Effect was good at establishing trope-led characters (which individual characters can rebel against). But I didn't see &quot;oh, Krogans are like dwarves&quot;. No, Volus are like dwarves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, now I think you're overcomplicated it, lol.<br /> <br /> The &quot;5 Races&quot; Trope isn't suggesting that Krogans are reskinned Dwarves.<br /> <br /> Rather, it argues that if a setting has non-Human races - then you'll usually see 4 predictable extremes. <br /> <br /> <b>Hyper-Masculine</b> (Stouts or Savages - usually muscular, warlike, hirsute)<br /> <b>Hyper-Feminine</b> (Fairy or Eldritch - usually magical, aloof/alien, ranged)<br /> <b>Older-Wiser-Powerful</b> (High Men or Fallen - often counselors, leaders)<br /> <b>Younger-Trickster</b> (Cute or Crafty - smart, cunning, clever)<br /> <br /> These are all in contrast to the <b>Average</b> (Mundane or Humanoid).<br /> <br /> So for example, Krogans and Turians; Dwarves, Dragonborn and Half-Orcs; Orcs, Tauren, Worgen; Ogres and Giants -- all Stouts / Savages. They're all hyper-masculine, muscular or hirsute (or both), grim or dour.<ul><li>Krogan females are a mere 1 in 2,000 of all births now because of the genophage.</li> <li>Bearded-Dwarven ladies was such a long running joke it became a trope.</li> <li>Warcraft Race/Gender demographics also reinforce this. The most masculine races are Dwarves (87.6%), Tauren (86.4%), Orc (81.1%) and Worgen (75.3%) - players simply don't look at those races neutrally (the way Humans, Pandaren, etc are).</li> </ul><hr /><br /> No one is saying &quot;Krogan are Dwarves&quot;.<br /> <br /> They're saying &quot;these are the 4 most common archetypes that splinter away from average/mundane/human&quot;. <br /> <br /> <b>And then</b> each of these archetypes has different cliches, tropes, perspectives, etc - <b>by selecting one of these races</b>, the player is deciding to <b>engage in those tropes</b> (whether to play along them or rail against them).<ul><li>This is why I take issue with the idea that &quot;muscular, bellicose Orcs&quot; is a bad trope. The trope<b> is </b>what forms Orcs.<ul><li>So when my friend plays a Half-Orc Fighter... he's declaring to the world (the DM &amp; players).... &quot;this is the trope I'm cleaving to - please don't expect me to engage in deep philosophy or social parties or similar frivolous things&quot;.</li> <li>And when I play a Half-Orc Bard or Wizard.... I'm declaring to the world (the DM &amp; players).... &quot;this is the trope I want to play..... no, my character does not like the stereotypes.... but I, the player, <b>want</b> to engage in that conflict...... a Half-Orc Bard struggling to prove the greatness of his verse - or a Half-Orc Wizard striving to prove their worth against Elves &amp; Co..... is a much more exciting and engaging motivation than being Elven Wizard #458,423.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Meanwhile, I'd consider Quarians &quot;mundanes&quot; - if you swapped their models for humans, they'd be little different story-wise (in fact, you can even <i>date one</i>, that's how compatible you are). And it's not a strictly platonic relationship when the issue of circumventing her suit comes up.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Asari? Fairy (hyper-feminine, magical/biotics, alien). And the &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FantasyAxisOfEvil\" target=\"_blank\">evil races</a>&quot; counterpart to Fairy is Eldritch (Demon, Undead, etc). Ever notice how much more popular Succubi are over Incubi? Or with undead - why do females get banshees and skew Vampire while we see more male Werewolves? <b>And then</b> bringing it back to Asari, when this <i>blue race of aliens</i> just <i>happens to look like human females</i> and they play up on the sexuality/drain/vampirism/banshee tropes?<br /> <br /> Or we can discuss Volus - who are kind of irrelevant to the group, as a mere background race - but effectively fall into the Cute/Crafty trope (inhabited by Goblins, Gnomes, etc). Neither &quot;hyper-masculine&quot; nor &quot;hyper-feminine&quot;, their write-up says &quot;volus genders are apparently a mystery as well. The volus themselves consider the question both intrusive and hilariously irrelevant&quot; and they have &quot;cloacae&quot;. And like the Goblins all over Warcraft they &quot;make their influence felt through trade and commerce&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1217928#post1217928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt people from Wavecrest actually call it Wavecrest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cresta De Ola?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1217928#post1217928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really dislike Lunars? Or just because you set your game far away from the edges of the Wyld? When I introduced beastmen to a group used to playing DnD, it worked very well, for your purposes. They immediately grasped that cat-people were decadent and arrogant, wolf-people were raiders, pig-people were fat and greedy, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Lunars (and the direction they seem to be taking in 3E). <br /> <br /> But I really really really loathed them in the past - due to Lunar <b>players</b> (mostly online). People who presume &quot;if you play a Lunar, then you <b>must love</b> psuedo-shamanic, macho-posturing, tattooed-warlord living-in-the-woods wannabe-Werewolf RP&quot; (who used various chunks of 2E Lunars to validate the Silver Pact as a clingy, kidnappery cult). Last time I played one online, in a really large game, I ended up with an <i>Abyssal </i>circle - but I periodically got the &quot;nudge&quot; from &quot;benign&quot; players/STs trying to reign all the Lunars together (despite my extremely blunt disinterest).<br /> <br /> And yeah - if <i>those</i> players dominate a game - then <i>their view of beastmen</i> inevitably dominates as well. Eventually <b>Infernals</b> came out - and suddenly I could do all the awesome shapeshifting &amp; mutations without being kidnapped and tattooed by hippies.<br /> <br /> An-Teng and D&amp;D Dragonborn &amp; 3E in general are letting me re-evaluate how to use them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1217928#post1217928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah! Now I understand. I didn't really get what the point of all this was.<br /> <br /> In that case, I think your best bet, if you're keen on running Exalted without changing the setting utterly massively, would be to pick where your game is set, and write one to two sentences about each neighbouring country.<br /> <br /> Something like:<br /> Medo: Ghost-worshipping horse-riding nomads. They must give soldiers to the Realm.<br /> Linowan: Like Native North American warrior tribes, they worship the sun, moon, and a tree god. They're allied with the Realm.<br /> Port Calin: A land of peasant farmers ruled by a Shogun. There's lots of political intrigue between daimyos.<br /> Etc. Maybe do about 6 or 7. You could put in some strange race of beastmen people don't know are beastmen, since you liked that, or other mutants. Maybe a country of people who are partially elemental, or partially Fae, or something like that.<br /> That should immediately give them some spaghetti ethnic groups and tropes to pick from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!<br /> <br /> The thread began with &quot;non-human races&quot; &gt; then Elder Scrolls came up (and I remembered they have multiple human races - with regional mutations/buffs) &gt; and then boiled down to &quot;okay, how about just ensuring 4-6 strong tropes exist within the human categories&quot;. So the 1.5 Human idea might be:<br /> <br /> Sijan - A funeral city next to a shadowland. <br /> (1-2 mutations/merits representing a distinctively Sijanese trait)<br /> <br /> Lookshy - A military city where all must enlist and serve.<br /> (1-2 mutations/merits representing a distinctively Lookshyan trait)<br /> <br /> Give each one a 1-2 sentence synopsis. Then pluck a trope-appropriate bonus. So even if they go against &quot;type&quot;, that bonus represents their heritage.<br /> <br /> ...and with that, I'm off to booster draft woooo!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T08:45:12-07:00","id":1218222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I first - and most frequently - heard it used for when &quot;a guy gives a girl preferential treatment&quot; (especially online, where the only thing that should matter are our ideas, not our genitals). If we believe in gender-equality, then girls don't need special coddling or protection in online debates.<br /> <br /> Then, by extension, it began to apply to all &quot;white knights&quot; who feel a need to &quot;defend&quot; women, minorities, etc - to the point that they think we can't participate in such discussions. In divine irony, it's the 2018 version of &quot;white man's burden&quot;, except it's the far-Left who feel this &quot;duty&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm fond of the term because I give my male friends grief over this all the time. I've literally &quot;hung out with the girls&quot; to grab cocktails and we talk about BJs and politics - but if my friends / their boyfriends show up, the guys self-censor as if their significant others are these dainty, fragile little angels. It makes my eyes want to roll into the back of my skull, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I can totally understand, and sympathize. Of course women don't need any coddling/protection. And the idea that someone who feels the need to defend minorities thinks we can't participate in discussions is... out of this world. I honestly have never seen it at work, but if you say it exists I'm inclined to believe you (the idiocy of some people knows no bounds apparently).<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily condemn your friends' boyfriends though. One doesn't need to necessarily intervene in a discussion if they feel they're not qualified enough, if they're not confident in their opinions, and so on. It doesn't mean they think their girlfriends are fragile little angels necessarily. Of course you know them and I don't, so, perhaps it's just chivalry and machismo and whatnot - although I usually see those traits manifesting in much more hideous forms. Anyways I appreciate people who want to be allies, and I also understand when some prefer to usually steer clear.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're only talking 500 years ago (when the New World period started).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dum_Diversas\" target=\"_blank\">Dum Diversas</a> was a <b>reaction</b> to the Eastern invasion of Europe (by the Ottomans) and the Western invasion of Europe (by the various Caliphates for 700 years). <i>The founding document that re-authorized slavery was a response</i>. There are books on <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=zsQ2DwAAQBAJ&amp;pg=PT164&amp;lpg=PT164&amp;dq=basque+slaves&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=ohmWZ7slA0&amp;sig=tkqedkbs9jEFSUOG4ABFoto8Mqw&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjv46n-5vPaAhUjwlkKHaoTAykQ6AEIYTAI#v=onepage&amp;q=basque%20slaves&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">Female Slaves in Islamic History</a> - and yes, from Andalusia to the Basque, they took Europeans as slaves. This isn't some obscure fact either - my friend and I (both Hispanic, both Arabic-studying) have looked at it (I hadn't realized how prevalent Basque slaves were until he explained how it resulted in the &quot;whitening&quot; of the Berber leadership to the point that over centuries they began looking more Spanish than North African).<br /> <br /> <b>The problem is</b> that every culture likes to focus on their glories - not on their losses. It's more flattering to say &quot;Spain kicked ass for 2-3 centuries&quot; than &quot;Spain was preyed upon for 7 centuries&quot;. So people forget <b>where</b> the ass-kicking originated from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Jews focus on their losses, mostly (and some people apparently think the Holocaust is all a fantasy, but that's par for the course). USA Black people do a little of both, they exalt (not Exalt!) their culture and roots but also talk about how their whole race was enslaved and deported by Whites, and the myriad ways they're still marginalized and exoticized. It's also difficult to focus on your glories when you know your glories consist of enslaving a people, genociding a couple others, and similar niceties. Sure, you can always point at some detail you're proud of, but chances are in the past something was going badly anyways - here in Europe we had the Renaissance, and in Italy we had powerful city states like Genoa, Florence, Naples, Venice... but there was also a lot of poverty and inequality, and of course we had monarchies anywhere.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that even though Spain was under the Umayyads, the rest of Europe wasn't. France, England, Italy, Germany etc had never been under the yoke of some foreign invader. But they still perpetrated atrocities upon native people worldwide. And the West is still enjoying its privileges at the expenses of those people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if you want to talk about the British or French or whoever? Go for it. But I sustain:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>the religious re-authorization of slavery <b>originated</b> as a reaction to invasions</li> <li>I can't condemn the initial &quot;victor&quot; countries who had been &quot;victims&quot; for the better half of a millennia</li> <li>I can't blame &quot;all Europeans&quot; (including those without colonies) for the handful of major empires</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the countries which had been subjected to slavery had a right to enslave other people. I also don't see the justification where those countries enslaved peoples who had never even touched them. I can't accept that the Catholic Church, or any religious institution, can legitimize slavery. But no, of course you can't blame all of Europe for the Age of Sails-and-onwards empires, only the major powers subjugated native peoples. Still, today, the net result is that if you're white you have it much easier than if you're Black, Asian, Native American... anything else really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mongols? Entire nations eradicated. Exterminated the half the Mongol tribes, genocide in Afghanistan - in Assyria, killed all the Christians, tons of Muslims &amp; Jews.<br /> <br /> The Chinese General Ran Min exterminated the Wu Hu for having &quot;high bridged noses and bushy beards&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Armenian Genocide was Turkish; the Rape of Nanking was Japanese; the Rwandan genocide was Hutu vs Tutsi.<br /> <br /> Lack of power does not denote a lack of will.<br /> <br /> The rest of the world isn't &quot;less murderous&quot; than Europe - the only difference is <i>reach</i>. There are plenty of modern atrocities going on, unrelated to Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> Absolutely. But we had the longest reach, we still do, and we're still benefitting from it. Sure, there's a lot of genocidal wars and other horrible things in the world, most of all parts of the world which are still struggling with poverty and exploitation by foreign powers - like us. And no one's doing anything to stop them, except for some rare relief agencies. We just prefer to ignore some conflicts, and focus on those that directly impact our wealth (like whenever an oil-rich territory is threatened).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a grotesque &quot;white-washing&quot; of history. They took <a href=\"http://Trade and traders in Muslim Spain, Fourth Series, Cambridge University Press, 1996.\" target=\"_blank\">slaves in Spain</a> half-a-thousand years before Columbus was ever born. They took women as sex slaves to the point that they <i>recolored their own bloodlines</i>.<br /> <br /> They were bad enough that - 2,000 years after the Romans &quot;unified&quot; the Iberian peninsula - regional rivalries and separatist movements remain strong...... yet 500 years ago, they were willing to put those aside just to get rid of the invaders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, sorry for the grotesque whitewashing. I still maintain that enslaving a whole people, deporting it, subjecting it to inhuman conditions, colonizing a subcontinent, making a whole generation disappear, taking huge expanses of land from natives, using dirty tricks like disease-ridden blankets, alcohol, opium, erasing whole cultures... and so on, it's a bit worse than what the Muslims did to Spain, or to the Byzantine Empire. Not because they're less murderous per se... but Europe was really incredibly hungry for colonies, saw everyone who wasn't white as a savage evil being in need of christian redemption, actively erased any divergent traditions and culture, and exploited everything and everyone to feed its nascent capitalism. Even now, media tell a mainly white narrative. In the US there's a corner in libraries for Black Literature. Because you gotta keep it separated from white literature apparently. It'll scare off customers. Other literatures? Sorry, what's that? Movies are always predominantly directed by whites, acted out by whites, financed by whites, telling stories of white people. Vgs? Same, tabletop rpgs, same, comics and most figurative arts, same.<br /> <br /> So, considering the actual current repercussions of Europe's colonialism and white imperialism in general... yeah.<br /> <br /> Oh and remember we're still having the Muslims pay for what they've done 5 centuries ago. Muslims in Europe or in the US? Yeah, no luck. Oh, but those people are all terrorists! Oh, if they wanna build a mosque tell them to go back to their country! No, we won't remove crosses from lay public spaces! Oh, those veils, no, you can't wear them! Jesus Christ.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree.<br /> <br /> You use &quot;us&quot; loosely - I don't see how Roswynn in 2018 is guilty of Mussolini or whoever else.<br /> <br /> And I disagree <b>even more</b> at the idea that a Bosnian is held responsible for Italy - or that a Ukrainian is responsible for France - or that (any country) is guilty for what (another country) has done. Should we blame the Chinese for Japan's behavior in Nanking? Are the Azerbaijani guilty of the Armenian genocide? Do we blame Egypt for Rwanda just because they're on the same continent?<br /> <br /> [/I]My point is that in 2018, I don't think (someone like Roswynn) needs lessons on &quot;slavery is bad&quot; more than <i>modern slavers</i>. Sorry, but I simply don't think <b>you</b> are the problem to focus on in 2018. You seem nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Grotesque whitewashing notwithstanding?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Anyways, yes, agreed, Roswynn is not exactly a world-wide problem. Roswynn's compatriots, and Roswynn's race, well, let's talk about it. Again, blanket statements are stupid. But a lot of white people are involved in white supremacist movements, fascist movements, neonazi movements... and so on. Those who are not shrug and let them be. A lot of European and US governments have committed atrocities and hidden them from public scrutiny. A lot of bigots are still allowed to exploit and harm People of Color. Don't warp what I'm saying - of course Azerbaijan has nothing to do with the Armenian genocide, and Ukraine didn't enslave West African people, but the West is still, generally speaking, profiting from all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you're presuming.</div> </div> </div> </div>WTF, what did I say??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The second</b> the Spanish got off a boat - the locals were doomed. The Spanish had <b>zero forewarning</b> to guess that the locals would be vulnerable (because <i>everywhere else they went</i>, foreign peoples <i>weren't</i> vulnerable - this was a completely new situation in the Americas).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><br /> <br /> Of course. Did I imply the Spanish knew they were gonna infect the Aztecs? Sorry, I misspoke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>And again, English and Spanish history are different</b>.<br /> <br /> The Anglo Saxons had the &quot;Trail of Tears&quot;, &quot;Thanksgiving&quot; and the whole &quot;Wild West&quot; genre - conflict between European vs Native <i>was a thing</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>By contrast</b>, the first Spaniards in the Caribbean (100 years before the English ever sailed) had no way of knowing the Taino would die-off by <i>mere contact. </i>When Cortes (and his native allies) fought the Aztecs - it's recorded that the Aztecs were <i>already weak from a plague and famine.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I know my history. I didn't mean to say that the Spanish invaded North America, if I said that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And note - the Anglo Saxons <b>prohibited </b>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">miscegenation&quot; <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- for the Spanish, it was <i>policy. </i>The Tainos were doomed on contact - but their blood is still a large part of Puerto Rico and the Dominican Republic. Modern Mexicans are (on average) 45% Native, 45% Spanish and 10% African. The Human Genome project had a thing exploring LATAM's mixing.<br /> <br /> It boggles my mind for people to suggest that people <i>intermarrying with the locals as policy</i> are <b>equal</b> to people <i>trying to wipe out the locals entire lineage</i>.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, at this point you'll probably have told me where do I suggest stuff like the one you're responding to, but it bears reiterating: I'm not saying that intermarriage is the same as genocide.<br /> <br /> Although, considering that the dominant race was always the white Spanish and never the natives, and a lot of original native culture has gone the way of the dodo, not really cool either. But certainly Native North Americans had it toughest. Also, some interesting cultural hybrids have arosen, like Santer\u00eca. Still, the Spanish and Portuguese had many Black slaves from West Africa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is different from my experience - but hey, we're in different countries/cultures! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. Or I might be wrong and race is meant as a more complex social construct universally than what I referred to. Honestly I don't know, we were talking about fantasy races and look where we ended up...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1216163#post1216163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the problem is (and the source of this whole thread) is that - as I read more 2E vs 3E - 2E conflated OOC and IC knowledge.<br /> <br /> I mean, <i>it makes sense</i>. There has to be a god or Sidereal who <i>knows</i> everything about certain topics. <b>But it's</b> not helpful for a brand-new player who just needs a quick-and-dirty regional vibe.<br /> <br /> <b>And it does exist to an extent</b> - but usually for Dragon-Blooded - with &quot;required stats&quot; for Dynasts and Lookshy. <b>So all I want</b> is to extend it to other major cities.<br /> <br /> I've also been looking at <b>13th Age</b> which builds it's setting using &quot;13 NPCs&quot; (a king, a druid, an infernalist, etc). I'm a huge fan of strong tropes.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> All in all, thanks for writing back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This has been a fun back-and-forth (and certainly helped clarify what to try / avoid when putting together fantasy ethnicities).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know about that thing in 13th Age, the Icons? Which are introduced as very basic concepts and further delineated through chargen and play? Someone was praising that system on Reddit I think.<br /> <br /> So, as for required stats, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23657_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23657\" data-vbnamecard=\"23657\">VioletDreamer</a> said, those are no longer a thing. But you and the others have talked about that in more recent posts, so even though it's bad form, for once I'll make an exception and do another post right away to see if I can contribute anything regarding the latest subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T09:28:42-07:00","id":1218232,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I like the way you elaborate on the 5 Races trope, I think it's very apt.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in seeing what you come up with for the description and traits of the various people of Creation.<br /> <br /> Even without mechanical traits it would work imo, but hey, why not?<br /> <br /> As for ethnonyms, of course each language in Creation is different... based on names coming up in the setting, for instance Haslanti should have mostly Inuit and other Eskimo-Aleut names, with Icelandic patro- and metronymic particles (-sson, -sdottir). I expect people in Ixcoatli to speak mostly Nahuatl and Mayan, and Old Realm appears to be similar to Mayan too.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of Creation, I think the West has mostly Oceanian toponyms, the South, African and Middle Eastern, the East, Central and South American, the South-West, various Indian languages, the Realm, Chinese languages, and the North... I don't really know. Also it appears like there's an exception every other step you take. Like there's a place in the North called Pneuma but it has nothing to do with Greek culture afaik. The Delzahn, who seem inspired by Arabs or Turks, have a city called Chiaroscuro. And Lookshy uses a lot of Japanese-sounding words but the toponym is English and there are gentes called typical generic fantasy names like Nefvarin.<br /> <br /> It's not really a problem - Creation isn't Earth and follows narrative rules, like rule of cool, plus if the languages replicated real life ones players might start expecting societies to follow their RL counterparts, which is not desirable. Creation is Creation. It is a mythic version of the world viewed through a time-compressing, Warp-infused lens.<br /> <br /> That said, I like to have my High Realm sound somewhat like Mandarin, and I give Delzahn Turkish names, Harborheaders (who are actually called Harborheadites in canon) various African names, Lookshyans Japanese names, and so on. As for the ethnonyms, I think it's Coraline for Coral (kidding, I just loved the movie... probably Coralese), Nexan or Nexian for Nexus, perhaps Wavecrester for Wavecrest?, Laplander for the Lap, Sijanese for Sijan. Usually the various Compasses of Terrestrial Directions give good ethnonyms, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> TL;DR... I go with what sounds cooler <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:07:13-07:00","id":1218245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218232#post1218232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I like the way you elaborate on the 5 Races trope, I think it's very apt.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in seeing what you come up with for the description and traits of the various people of Creation.<br /> <br /> Even without mechanical traits it would work imo, but hey, why not?<br /> <br /> As for ethnonyms, of course each language in Creation is different... based on names coming up in the setting, for instance Haslanti should have mostly Inuit and other Eskimo-Aleut names, with Icelandic patro- and metronymic particles (-sson, -sdottir). I expect people in Ixcoatli to speak mostly Nahuatl and Mayan, and Old Realm appears to be similar to Mayan too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing much of an Aleut influence on the Haslanti in prior material. Also, Old Realm is even wider than that in where it lifts from - its script looks Mayan, uses Korean hangul grouping for how to fit the syllables rather than letters into place, and kind of follows the Ainu use of katakana for terminal consonants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the rest of Creation, I think the West has mostly Oceanian toponyms, the South, African and Middle Eastern, the East, Central and South American, the South-West, various Indian languages, the Realm, Chinese languages, and the North... I don't really know. Also it appears like there's an exception every other step you take. Like there's a place in the North called Pneuma but it has nothing to do with Greek culture afaik. The Delzahn, who seem inspired by Arabs or Turks, have a city called Chiaroscuro. And Lookshy uses a lot of Japanese-sounding words but the toponym is English and there are gentes called typical generic fantasy names like Nefvarin. </div> </div> </div>(Puts on &quot;read up too much on Lookshy&quot; hat)<br /> <br /> Though the Nefvarin family head in The Outcaste has a French given name (Alixa) and there are a number of Chinese names as well - the gentes Chan, Tsung, and possibly Yan Tu, as well as the gentes heads Mehela Qiao Yin, Nerigus Shen, Toriki Laoshe, to say nothing of Karal Linwei or sky guard taimyo Nefvarin Shou-Yu. They also have a lot of descriptive names showing up, such as Hightower, Stonefist, or Fire Orchid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not really a problem - Creation isn't Earth and follows narrative rules, like rule of cool, plus if the languages replicated real life ones players might start expecting societies to follow their RL counterparts, which is not desirable. Creation is Creation. It is a mythic version of the world viewed through a time-compressing, Warp-infused lens.<br /> <br /> That said, I like to have my High Realm sound somewhat like Mandarin, and I give Delzahn Turkish names, Harborheaders (who are actually called Harborheadites in canon) various African names, Lookshyans Japanese names, and so on. As for the ethnonyms, I think it's Coraline for Coral (kidding, I just loved the movie... probably Coralese), Nexan or Nexian for Nexus, perhaps Wavecrester for Wavecrest?, Laplander for the Lap </div> </div> </div>That seems like it could cause confusion with a real life ethnic group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:57:05-07:00","id":1218272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218245#post1218245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not seeing much of an Aleut influence on the Haslanti in prior material. Also, Old Realm is even wider than that in where it lifts from - its script looks Mayan, uses Korean hangul grouping for how to fit the syllables rather than letters into place, and kind of follows the Ainu use of katakana for terminal consonants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, you're right. I was thinking about Dragon Kings terminology - don't ask me the precise terms right now, I should dig out the books - they sounded Mayan. But demons and gods use Old Realm too to speak and they have all manners of names from Adorjan and Szoreny (Hungarian) to Florivet (French, Spanish...) and Jorst (Danish). So I really don't know what it would sound like.<br /> <br /> Aaand I'm looking back at some Haslanti names and they all look Germanic, actually... I was quite sure there were some Aleut phonemes in there, weird...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218245#post1218245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Puts on &quot;read up too much on Lookshy&quot; hat)<br /> <br /> Though the Nefvarin family head in The Outcaste has a French given name (Alixa) and there are a number of Chinese names as well - the gentes Chan, Tsung, and possibly Yan Tu, as well as the gentes heads Mehela Qiao Yin, Nerigus Shen, Toriki Laoshe, to say nothing of Karal Linwei or sky guard taimyo Nefvarin Shou-Yu. They also have a lot of descriptive names showing up, such as Hightower, Stonefist, or Fire Orchid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense, you can't possibly read too much about Lookshy. I love those damn fascists.<br /> <br /> I had forgotten about Linwei - you're right, there's a lot of Chinese names there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218245#post1218245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like it could cause confusion with a real life ethnic group.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that. Let's hope the 3e writers can come up with a better ethnonym.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T14:28:04-07:00","id":1218322,"title":"","content":"Howdy - and Happy Mothers Day to all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly have never seen it at work, but if you say it exists I'm inclined to believe you</div> </div> </div> </div>I work in the Arts - which already skews to the Left - and is often a self-aggrandizing &quot;pat yourself on the back&quot; echo-chamber. Major theater organizations often focus so much on a very narrow definition of &quot;inclusivity&quot; - that they often forget to produce good <i>theater</i> - while simultaneously excluding (and alienating) clients. <br /> <br /> And <i>then</i> there's the &quot;soft bigotry of low expectations&quot;, where in trying to be <i>inclusive</i>, they fail to be <i>selective</i> - in turn reinforcing negative stereotypes.<ul><li>So for example, if you decide to &quot;only do plays be female playwrights&quot; (which is a <i>sexist</i> decision and unworthy of bragging about) - and if only 3 of your 8 play choices are actually <i>good</i> - it reinforces to the audience &quot;oh wow, female playwrights must be sub-par on average&quot;. A <b>good</b> director will select <b>good</b> plays because of the writing - not the gender or color or identity of the playwright (which is <i>irrelevant</i> to the audience).</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily condemn your friends' boyfriends though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The males are &quot;my friends&quot; - their significant-others, by extension. <br /> <br /> And my condemnation is less &quot;white knights&quot; (thankfully, they're not) - and more about &quot;benign sexism&quot;. Good guys who are simply too nervous, embarrassed or weirded-out at being uncensored around females. <i>Coincidentally tho</i>, a convo a week ago turned to heckling the most censorious - so they became <i>too embarrassed to censor</i> - so now everyone shares an unfiltered chat full of Mother's Day, car accident gore, political arguments, cocktail recipes, video games and penises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the Jews focus on their losses, mostly (and some people apparently think the Holocaust is all a fantasy, but that's par for the course). USA Black people do a little of both, they exalt (not Exalt!) their culture and roots but also talk about how their whole race was enslaved and deported by Whites, and the myriad ways they're still marginalized and exoticized. It's also difficult to focus on your glories when you know your glories consist of enslaving a people, genociding a couple others, and similar niceties. Sure, you can always point at some detail you're proud of, but chances are in the past something was going badly anyways - here in Europe we had the Renaissance, and in Italy we had powerful city states like Genoa, Florence, Naples, Venice... but there was also a lot of poverty and inequality, and of course we had monarchies anywhere.<br /> <br /> There's also the fact that even though Spain was under the Umayyads, the rest of Europe wasn't. France, England, Italy, Germany etc had never been under the yoke of some foreign invader. But they still perpetrated atrocities upon native people worldwide. And the West is still enjoying its privileges at the expenses of those people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your response meanders a little (but I love meandering). This is long-ish (group by group) so I'll fold it:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>re: Iberia (Spain &amp; Portugal)</b><br /> The point is I don't group &quot;all white people&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unlike Italy or Britain or (etc), the Iberian provinces were under foreign rule for centuries (under the Romans), then 300~ years (Visigoths), then 700~ years (NW African Islamists) - long before they unified and went on the offensive for 200-300 years. The provinces who removed the Caliphates first were the most warlike - <b>proving</b> that aggression is a virtue (because as far as natural selection goes, pacifists end up in the ground). It's impossible (and unethical) to try to extrapolate &quot;guilt&quot; upon Iberia when they were victimized for 2-3 times as long as they were victors.<br /> <br /> <b>re: Jews</b><br /> Jewish &quot;focus on their losses&quot; is what I think inoculates them against &quot;white-washing&quot; and loss of cultural identity. Much like with Iberia, a sense of &quot;joint ancestral foes&quot; helps any group decide which differences are minor &amp; permitted - and which differences are taboo. We do lots of Jewish plays and almost all of them resonate as a Hispanic (similar dynamics, similar topics, etc). <br /> <br /> <b>re: West Africans</b><br /> Much like &quot;whites&quot;, I don't like using the term &quot;black&quot; people as if they're homogeneous. They're both overly broad - and like &quot;Yellow&quot; or &quot;Red&quot;, rarely used by anyone with an actual sense of their ancestry. <br /> <br /> Besides which, the majority <i>weren't</i> enslaved - they stayed in Africa. The girl I dated whose parents were doctors from Ghana - none of them expressed any feelings regarding slavery - because <i>they and everyone they knew</i> lived in Ghana. Moreover, <i>they migrated to the US</i> because they considered the US better. They had no interest in being grouped with dark-skinned Americans because they had nothing culturally in common with them.<br /> <br /> And the reason West Africa was focused upon was because <i>they already had slave markets and culture</i>. As aforementioned, it's Iberian history that the Moors took European slaves (so lots of the early Portuguese ships &quot;seeking adventure&quot; included the pursuit of enslaved kin). The fact that the Portuguese wanted to repatriot them <i>via the sword</i> (as opposed to diplomacy or whatever) doesn't diminish the fact that it was Iberians who were slaves first.<br /> <br /> One of our oldest theater companies in this city is 'Black' - but they have a great history component, trying to look into source-cultures (as opposed to conflating all Africans together). And I remember one of their books - <i>by page 2</i> - was discussing West African slave trading culture. Of a half-dozen major kingdoms, the <i>majority</i> traded slaves.<ul><li>There was a difference in tone - with slavery combining ideas of &quot;prisoners of war&quot; and reparations. IE, &quot;better to enslave an enemy soldier and force them to repair what they broke&quot; than to &quot;simply kill them&quot;. Slavery was more human than execution. <b>Plus</b> there were passive bonuses discussed (so maybe 4-8 years down the line, when you release your slave and they return home? now that experience means both sides have more cross-cultural awareness.... so an ex-soldier turned ex-slave is now older, wiser, better to try translating during quarrels or counseling younger soldiers into showing restraint, etc).</li> </ul><b>re: Italians</b><br /> I'm glad you acknowledge the Renaissance, city-states and other good things Italy has done. And you also note poverty and inequality.<br /> <br /> Now my question is - how about places that <b>never</b> had the Renaissance or city-states, etc - but <b>always</b> had poverty and inequality?<br /> <br /> There <i>mere fact</i> that you - as an Italian - can view Italy as 50% Great, 50% &quot;Stuff to be Improved On&quot;..... <b>is miles ahead</b> of places that are 0% Great and see 0% to be improved upon. <br /> <br /> Like <i>wow</i>. Italy isn't full of saints - but jeeze, you actually <i>aspire</i> to sainthood? There are countries today that torture, starve and rob their people.... and you guys think you're bad because &quot;well, we could do <i>more</i> to help the poor.... we haven't achieved perfection, so we're pretty bad&quot;.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Any time I hear an American say &quot;oh this country is the worst! look how we treat migrants!&quot; - I think &quot;well, the people in the country of <b>my</b> birth are starving to death in the streets or prostituting themselves over the border.... the country my <b>parents</b> were born in is so bad, I've met 4 year olds who act sexual for food, people who raft 50 miles at sea and risk drowning to get here, that uncle I have who spent 30 years in a political-prisoner closet-cell (and now can't move because his joints atrophied).....yeah, what the fuck are Americans complaining about?<br /> <br /> I know Central Americans <i>who love Trump</i>. Because they came to the US legally <i>fleeing the lawlessness</i> and gangs - so they're 100% on board with enforcing the borders (because people - no matter how &quot;harmless&quot; - who don't respect the law are <b>precisely</b> why our home-countries fell apart). Not gangs, not crime, not war - the &quot;soft&quot; law-breakers, who whittle away respect for government in little PR-friendly steps - until it all devolves into tribalism.<br /> <br /> My point is, <b>if your country has migrants</b>, then your country is <b>already better</b> than wherever we fled from. Please quick kicking yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>re: France, etc</b><br /> France was the worst and I've never said otherwise. But it'd be gross to say &quot;white people&quot; for what the French did. I remember a 100 year old book on mercenaries &amp; foreign policy (discussing the French Foreign Legion) - and even 100 years ago, before the World Wars, other Europeans agreed that the French had fucked up every colony they had.<ul><li>In the Americas, they imported more slaves than the British - but we don't see their descendants because the French preferred to <i>work them to death</i>. The fact that they lost Haiti - while the Dominican Republic <i>returned</i> to Spain willingly - only highlights further how incompetent and barbaric they were.</li> <li>Coincidentally, Americans celebrate <b>Cinco De Mayo</b> - but it's celebrated more in the US than in Mexico. Why? Because in the Battle of Puebla (<b>1862</b>) 4,500 poorly armed Mexican militia beat 6,500 better armed French soldiers. The Mexicans had roughly 200 killed-or-wounded while the French suffered 700+. It was a hell of a morale boost, despite that the French (in later battles) took and temporarily held Mexico City.<ul><li>Why does this matter to the US? Texas was still a part of Mexico until <b>1836</b>. The American Civil War was <b>1861-1865</b>. In short, many think France wanted to take Mexico and then interfere with the Civil War (to help the Confederates). If they could do so, slavery would have continued - the North &amp; South would be split - and France could try claiming Mexico and the West Coast of the Americas.<ul><li>Also, Napoleon III knew that the US opposed his plans for a &quot;Mexican Empire&quot; - but the Confederate States had no problem with it. He knew he couldn't go to war with the US without allies.... but if he could take Mexico soon enough, he could trade and help the South surreptitiously. <b>Instead</b>, it all took so long that the French couldn't enthrone Maximilian until <b>1864</b> - and by then, it was all too late.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>There's also another area of discussion regarding North Africa - how their colonies (and favoritism to monotheistic Arabic-speakers) led to much of the currently conflict we have today. And this was seen <b>100 years ago</b>. Countries that had myriad ethnicities we re face with French diplomats who had no interest in local groups - and if they had to train and deal with someone, it was easier to learn 1 language (Arabic) - and then let the bilingual natives (who spoke indigenous tongues + Arabic for religious purposes) translate.<ul><li>The long-and-short of it is that in countries that once had different religions and languages.... the French served as &quot;natural selection&quot;, turning Arabic into the language of translators, office clerks, police, judges, administrators. It went from &quot;one among many&quot; to the &quot;favored&quot; tongue - and since (unlike ethnic tongues) it was a <i>religious tongue</i>, people aspiring for a better life could merely <i>convert</i> and learn it. The French essentially reinvigorated and reunified the religious fundamentalists who later kicked them out.</li> </ul></li> </ul>But notice the specificity in this. <br /> <br /> I don't blame &quot;all whites&quot; - I very specifically discuss the French.<br /> <br /> And I don't say &quot;all colonialism&quot; - I very specifically pinpoint what the French did.<br /> <br /> And even now, I don't say &quot;all French&quot; - because people born in 2000 aren't guilty of what other people born in the 1600-1800s did.<br /> <br /> <i>And I don't even like French</i>. The language sounds like plastic to my Spanish ears. It's the audio-equivalent of seeing someone with too much plastic surgery.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how the countries which had been subjected to slavery had a right to enslave other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're religious, there are no &quot;natural born rights&quot;. Mother nature does not care about anyone's feelings or ethics. Lions don't ask lambs for permission to eat. It's as simple as:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Bad Muslims &quot;seek to convert the infidels&quot;? They enjoyed massive growth (fueled partially by the prohibition of enslaving other Muslims - meaning that as slaves converted and then had to be liberated, each generation had to conquer the next neighbor in order to fuel their trade).<br /> <br /> Good Christians &quot;turned the other cheek&quot;? They were enslaved and separated from their families (their pacifist inclinations flushed down the genetic toilet).<br /> <br /> Bad Christians repelled the invaders? They were viewed as heroes (and get laid as much as physically possible producing more sword-happy heroes).<br /> <br /> A few centuries later, it wasn't diplomacy or kindness that liberated them - it was admiration for masculine values of warfare, bravery, conquest. If you don't like the idea of military-heroes defining right-and-wrong, then Exalted might not be the setting for you. lol</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't see the justification where those countries enslaved peoples who had never even touched them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're looking for moral/religious justifications, they're as irrelevant as kindness, diplomacy and feelings.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for tactical justifications, it's super obvious - &quot;X territory has preyed upon our territory for centuries - so only by pacifying and converting X can we ensure our own safety&quot;. Then &quot;oh wait, now Y territory endangers X - let's take over Y&quot;. Then &quot;Z is nearby and could risk Y, lets handle that too.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>No nation</b> in history is innocent (unless they're extinct). This is not an ethical discussion, it's a tactical one. Ethics failed for 700 years, so tactics took over for the 300 afterward.<br /> <br /> You balk that a religious institution could justify war or slavery - I balk that the victims waited 700 years faithfully for permission to fight back. Dodo's went extinct because they knew neither to flee nor fight (and the same applies to civilizations).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't accept that the Catholic Church, or any religious institution, can legitimize slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you can accept that the Church prohibits slavery?<br /> <br /> <b>We must be consistent</b>. <br /> <br /> Either the Church had zero authority over ethical behavior - whether prohibiting or authorizing.<br /> <br /> Or the Church had full authority over ethical behavior - whether prohibiting or authorizing.<br /> <br /> But as aforementioned, this isn't an ethical discussion - it's a tactical one. &quot;Good Christians&quot; died against Ottomans' and Moors - so bellicose &quot;Bad Christians&quot; survived, reproduced and got to re-decide policy generations afterward. <b>If</b> I'm going to blame the &quot;Bad Christians&quot; for wanting to live unmolested - then I'll also blame the &quot;Good Christians&quot; for tolerating the initial aggressions that led to this all. If both &quot;good and bad&quot; extremes had contributed to mutual defense, then maybe the entire invasion, war &amp; slavery period could have been averted - <b>instead</b>, the &quot;good guys&quot; only reinforced to the invaders that &quot;yeah, this is worthwhile, we can take their shit and they won't fight back&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But no, of course you can't blame all of Europe for the Age of Sails-and-onwards empires, only the major powers subjugated native peoples. Still, today, the net result is that if you're white you have it much easier than if you're Black, Asian, Native American... anything else really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Travel the world and this will change.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I'm Hispanic. If you go to Latin America - and are too obviously white - you are a tourist and thus a target. You think people &quot;treat you better&quot; and yet - <i>specifically for your complexion</i> - you will be viewed in a way that endangers you (in a way that no local will ever be endangered by). Light-skinned Hispanics speaking Spanish obviously prove their ethnicity - but an Anglo or German or Swede in Columbia is just a lost foreigner with too much money.<br /> <br /> In the US, I've seen rural towns where <i>tan</i> people are &quot;too dark&quot; and unwelcome - <b>but I've also seen</b> adjacent towns were <i>tan</i> people are &quot;too white&quot; and unwelcome. Your skin color doesn't make you magically pampered in the abstract - it's all local and situational. I would not want to be &quot;black&quot; in some of those places - but I would not want to be &quot;white&quot; in several others.<ul><li>This is probably what helps me cleave to my Hispanic identity - regardless of phenotype, language is our group-identifier, not skin tone.</li> </ul>Shit, if I go to China with a squad of friends... I expect it to privilege <i>the Chinese</i>. That's the purpose of a society - to maximize privilege for inhabitants. The problem therefore isn't &quot;giving extra privileges to locals&quot; so much as &quot;non-locals being unaware or unable to plug in to those systems&quot;. I won't be upset if the Chinese know how to maximize benefits from living in China. And that's 20% of the world population..... 20% of the world population favoring &quot;non-whites&quot; despite colonial influence.<br /> <br /> My family didn't come to the US to decry &quot;whites have it so much better here&quot;. Our <b>first</b> thought was &quot;this is way better than we were once lived&quot; and our <b>second</b> &quot;okay, the locals have hangups - but it's our job to overcome those hangups, not their job to embrace a bunch of strangers&quot;. <br /> <br /> <b>Anyone</b> who thinks &quot;whites&quot; are so vicious to non-whites.... <i>are welcome</i> to try living in the home-countries <i>we</i> fled from. I can show you video of people cut up by chainsaw while still alive - or a guy getting his face carved off because he spoke to the wrong girl - and it's not the USA this takes place in.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. But we had the longest reach, we still do.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The Mongols are estimated to have killed 5% of the world population - and redefined 10% of the DNA of Asia. They didn't &quot;accidentally infect locals with the cold&quot; or give out diseased blankets - they <i>catapulted cadavers</i> into cities to spread plagues.<br /> <br /> Persian historians wrote that in 1221 the city of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merv#Uzbeks_in_Merv_and_its_final_destruction\" target=\"_blank\">Merv</a> opened it's gates to the Mongols.... and the Mongols had them butchered anyways, &quot;the whole population, including women and children, no one be spared&quot; such that by nightfall the &quot;mountains became hillocks&quot; (so many corpses, the mountains looked like hills) and &quot;the plain was soaked with blood&quot;. The city was rebuilt but never recuperated and finally was razed a few centuries later.<br /> <br /> Then there is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nishapur\" target=\"_blank\">Nishapur</a> whose &quot;entire population was slaughtered by the Mongols in 1221&quot;. One of Genghis Khan's daughters lost her husband - so she requested the death of the city. In 10 days they beheaded the city and built a pyramid to stack them. It was never inhabited again.<br /> <br /> Half the population of the Rus, half the population of China, half the population of Hungary. <br /> <br /> So <b>no</b>, Europe does not have &quot;the longest reach&quot; - the Mongols get that honor, by eradicating entire civilizations out of existence and pre-empting the possibility of descendants decrying their crimes. The mere fact that colonies <i>lived</i> to decry the colonialists kind of proves that the colonialists were already kinder than Genghis Khan ever was (<i>by their own admission</i>). There never was - nor will be - &quot;Mervites&quot; or &quot;Nishapurians&quot; in 2019 who get to look back and be upset at history.<br /> <br /> And again, lack-of-power does not denote lack-of-will.<br /> <br /> If a Green human has a gun - and a Blue human has a knife - and both want to kill me? Awful. I don't consider the Blue human more benign just because he's less competent. The fact that shooting-me is more effective doesn't make stabbing-me-to-death more pleasant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, sorry for the grotesque whitewashing. I still maintain that enslaving a whole people, deporting it, subjecting it to inhuman conditions, colonizing a subcontinent, making a whole generation disappear, taking huge expanses of land from natives, using dirty tricks like disease-ridden blankets, alcohol, opium, erasing whole cultures... and so on, it's a bit worse than what the Muslims did to Spain, or to the Byzantine Empire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The blankets, booze and opium were British - not Spanish.<br /> <br /> The land-grab, colonization and enslaving.... is <i>precisely</i> what the Moors were doing in Iberia and the Ottoman's in Greece. It's been over half-a-thousand-years and the Ottoman's descendants (Turkey) <b>still</b> owns one of the oldest Greek cities (Alexandria / Constantinople / Istanbul). <b>They killed the inhabitants and took the land</b> - how is this not precisely the same thing?<br /> <br /> If a Blue human tribe and a Green human tribe take turns attacking each other? They're both scummy. And if generations later the Blue tribe is triumphant? That doesn't make the Green tribe honorable victims - it makes them scummy losers vs scummy winners. And if history shows the Green tribe initiated the conflict with the Blue tribe? Then that's Karma. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the US there's a corner in libraries for Black Literature. Because you gotta keep it separated from white literature apparently. It'll scare off customers. Other literatures? Sorry, what's that? Movies are always predominantly directed by whites, acted out by whites, financed by whites, telling stories of white people. Vgs? Same, tabletop rpgs, same, comics and most figurative arts, same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm an immigrant and I'm baffled.<br /> <br /> Yes, whites dominate in the US - because they're the majority of the population. Same thing with Indians dominating in India, Chinese dominating in China, Nigerians in Nigeria and <b>every other society</b> on this planet. It is nothing but <i>self loathing</i> to tell a majority-population &quot;you should be ashamed of your existence&quot;. Would you tell Israelites that they're too Israeli? Maybe I should hate my Hispanic heritage for having too many Hispanics on our TV channels and writing our books.<br /> <br /> You're proposing a &quot;no win&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> A special &quot;black literature&quot; section <b>is great</b> - when you have 100,000 books, I can see why they might want to call special attention to a niche. <b>This applies to all niches in a book store</b>. Sure, you can throw all RPG books together - but it's awesome when D&amp;D or Exalted or whoever get their own sections (helpful for the D&amp;D fans only interested in D&amp;D - and helpful for non-D&amp;D books who don't want to be buried within Wizard of the Coast publishing). <br /> <br /> <b>We have Hispanic heritage festivals</b> and no one claims &quot;those damn Anglos don't appreciate Hispanic culture&quot;.... <i>why should they?</i> It's our section, our festival for our people and our language and our culture. I don't get upset with non-Hispanics having their events - nor do I demand/expect that non-Hispanics come to ours.<ul><li><b>Pro-Tip:</b> And when you don't try to guilt each other into attending, you end up having more cross-cultural attendance. <b>Conversely</b>, the groups who I see using more &quot;guilt tactics&quot; are the ones with the lowest attendance. They're <i>blind </i>to their own <i>lack of empathy</i> for other groups - and then think themselves the victim when they alienate those groups.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and remember we're still having the Muslims pay for what they've done 5 centuries ago. Muslims in Europe or in the US? Yeah, no luck. Oh, but those people are all terrorists! Oh, if they wanna build a mosque tell them to go back to their country! No, we won't remove crosses from lay public spaces! Oh, those veils, no, you can't wear them! Jesus Christ.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is unfair to caricature people's concerns:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">There has been a rise of <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2017/05/11/health/female-genital-mutilation-fgm-explainer-trnd/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">female genital mutilation</a> in the US, the Canadian <a href=\"https://youtu.be/WL-E-Q2L9MM?t=46s\" target=\"_blank\">school play featuring beheadings</a>, the <a href=\"https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/europe/iraqi-refugee-raped-10-year-old-boy-swimming-pool-vienna-austria-sentence-conviction-overturned-a7377491.html\" target=\"_blank\">rapist of a 10 y/o Austrian</a> whose sentence was overturned for cultural reasons and then the infamous <a href=\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/2018/02/23/newcastle-grooming-gangs-acted-arrogant-persistence-serious/\" target=\"_blank\">UK grooming gangs</a> (where in one story, a father knew where his little girl was - and was banging on the assailants door - but the police simply arrested him and called him a racist). <br /> <br /> Islam is not a race or phenotype or biology - it's a religion. If we can criticize Christianity and other faiths - then Islam is included. <b>If you don't</b>, you get the above situations.<br /> <br /> <b>This is also</b> where people like Milo Yiannopoulos come from...... a gay, Jewish-born, Catholic-leaning Greek immigrant married to a black man.... and he's Right-wing in his politics because the political-Left is so self-loathing, they refuse to truly engage in cultural differences.<br /> <br /> If you believe in diversity, then you believe in differences.<br /> <br /> And some differences are irreconcilable. <br /> <br /> The same way a Nazi favoring &quot;racial purity&quot; would never reconcile with my Spanish &quot;mixing <i>is the best</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can't just scream &quot;racism&quot; when people bring up legitimate differences they want to discuss.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'll also interject with the Hispanic angle. My (Left-leaning) boss sometimes tries to nudge me into tribalism by arguing &quot;they (right-wing Anglo Americans) think (X, Y, Z) about Hispanics!&quot; ... to which I often reply &quot;but X, Y, Z are true? so why should I fault them for disliking what we bring? they're not being bigoted, they're being astute...&quot;<br /> <br /> I refuse to cry &quot;mindless bigotry!&quot; when (group A) dislikes (group B). Sometimes groups are <i>well aware</i> of each other and have <i>legitimate</i> differences. The <b>best</b> resolution (for me) is either:<ul><li>(a) to each their own (I got my neighborhood, you have yours)</li> <li>(b) we talk it out (without demonizing the opposition)</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, yes, agreed, Roswynn is not exactly a world-wide problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, according to the Chinese - you might be! <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baizuo\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baizuo</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No, I don't think Roswynn is going to lynch my cousin or spit in my arepa.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are people who think self-loathing Europeans are unwittingly defending groups who are far more relevant threats.<br /> <br /> There's a documentary - <b>Empire of Dust</b> - covering the Chinese in the Congo. And there is a very poignant moment where the Chinese man is baffled by the locals - because the locals scream &quot;colonialism&quot; and &quot;oppression&quot; <b>but</b> the Chinese <b>were also</b> colonized and <b>now</b> they're an Empire of their own. So the Chinese man points out that the Dutch left <i>half a century ago</i> and left behind infrastructure and technology that China didn't have - and yet the locals let it rot.<br /> <br /> <b>The point</b> is that the &quot;Bai-Zuo&quot; problem is that if we <b>forever</b> are in this trope - then no one ever moves forward. Europeans start &quot;tolerating&quot; the intolerant because they're afraid of being called bigots - and &quot;colonies&quot; never get independent because they're forever guilting the colonialists for reparations. <b>Meanwhile</b>, the Chinese have neither concern (they don't demand handouts from the British - and they don't tolerate religious extremists defying laws). In Empire of Dust, the Chinese are building roads and cities - but have no sympathy for <i>any peoples</i> who are negligent of their own futures and demanding to be saved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WTF, what did I say??</div> </div> </div> </div>You (and another) conflated some Anglo-Saxon behaviors (like genocide or blankets) with Iberian behaviors (which sought to <i>interbreed</i> with the locals, not murder them). <br /> <br /> And it got to my skin since it's contrary to a lot of our history. There are statues in Central America honoring the progenitors of the first Mestizos (a Spaniard who &quot;went native&quot;); there were countries that prohibited same-race marriage in order to discourage English/French and encourage a new mixed-race identity. Hell, of 200 Spaniards who left Columbia's coast to found Bogota.... I think only 20 survived to the destination. How do 20 men build a city? By intermixing with locals and Africans (some slaves, some not-slaves).<br /> <br /> Yes, native cultures went the way of the dodo - <b>but that's nature</b>. There are tons of languages vanishing because everyone is switching to the big &quot;world languages&quot;. Culture, fashion, everything changes. The &quot;pure Aztec&quot; culture (with raiding, human sacrifice and demanding tribute from other nation-states) was never going to survive into the 20th century - but we can still enjoy the artwork and aesthetic and symbols without reveling in the bloodier parts. (Same thing with Celts and Nords in Europe - they were all eventually 'civilized by force' so people think of Celtic knots and fairies instead of ritual-drownings and wicker men).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting. Or I might be wrong and race is meant as a more complex social construct universally than what I referred to. Honestly I don't know, we were talking about fantasy races and look where we ended up...</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably my favorite part about fantasy! The ability to have complex conversations that reference real-world topics.<br /> <br /> Look at Black Panther. When the hero is discussing that they can't &quot;handle the migrants&quot; because &quot;they bring their problems&quot; and his priority is &quot;the safety of his own people&quot; - I was like:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Wow, if they had &quot;real&quot; people say that, they'd call them a racist... but because it's a fictitious country, the <b>hero</b> can evince the viewpoints of political isolationists <b>without</b> demonizing them. He's a rational, thoughtful, protective leader - and it's the American, Killmonger, with his warped pan-identitarian politics who ends up killing people and blaming others for everything.</i></div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even though it's bad form</div> </div> </div> </div>The only bad form is censoring yourself! Type away. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218222#post1218222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TL;DR... I go with what sounds cooler</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my English is pretty good (and long forum posts certainly serve as practice, lol) - but man, I love the ethnonyms you come up with. Spanish &amp; Arabic are a little more formulaic and consistent - so my &quot;first guesses&quot; are no where near as diverse as the examples you provided.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T15:11:05-07:00","id":1218339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218232#post1218232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I like the way you elaborate on the 5 Races trope, I think it's very apt.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in seeing what you come up with for the description and traits of the various people of Creation.<br /> <br /> Even without mechanical traits it would work imo, but hey, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucky me, my group floats from one game to another - so I can mull this at leisure. Exalted Castes certainly work for tropes (but since I'm going low-powered to start, Exalted are off the table) - although even then, there's no hard-fix where Dawn-Castes are all stoic, gruff warlords, etc.<br /> <br /> More and more, obfuscation comes to mind. The more people compared 3E and 2E, the more I realize the sort of &quot;omniscient perspective&quot; of 2E precluded a lot of mystery.<br /> <br /> So for example, don't introduce a bunch of new players playing merely-mortals to &quot;the Lunar Exalted chosen by Luna create Beastmen races&quot; - but break it down into &quot;the renown Cattalestae archers&quot;, the cult of the &quot;Third Eye Pyramid&quot;, followers of &quot;Zatesh&quot; and all those other aspects of Luna. Instead of a simplified, uniform, omniscient &quot;all Beastmen are X&quot;, it could be a dozen &quot;god-touched&quot; peoples with physical mutations or the like. Players don't even need to realize they're all the same deity.<br /> <br /> Likewise for other X-Blooded types.<br /> <br /> Take Demon-Blooded. Instead of &quot;all Demons are born from Demons, spawned by the Yozis&quot; - break it down into &quot;Vigilants of Granalkin&quot;, the &quot;Golden Jannisary Templars&quot;, and other demon-hunting groups (with different origins)..... as well as one-shots like &quot;dead children resurrected by Naamah&quot;, etc. OOC, as a ST, I can know they're Demon-Blooded - but IC, they could all have different origin myths. The function OOC/IC is that &quot;whoever picks one of these obviously wants me to engage in more spooky-dooky content&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm giving this thought. It's been fun seeing the conversation back-and-forth meanwhile, as well as reading up on other RPGs (to see what works for them).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T18:40:51-07:00","id":1218386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218322#post1218322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know Central Americans <i>who love Trump</i>. Because they came to the US legally <i>fleeing the lawlessness</i> and gangs - so they're 100% on board with enforcing the borders (because people - no matter how &quot;harmless&quot; - who don't respect the law are <b>precisely</b> why our home-countries fell apart). Not gangs, not crime, not war - the &quot;soft&quot; law-breakers, who whittle away respect for government in little PR-friendly steps - until it all devolves into tribalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was the case he wouldn't pardon people who recklessly disregard the rule of law like Joe Arpaio and openly call on police to commit more acts of illegal brutality. Please do not conflate the &quot;unquestioned authority of law enforcement&quot; with &quot;rule of law&quot; - those are in fact mutually exclusive principles as in a society governed by the rule of law there are civil rights protections and police are not unaccountable to law themselves, able to create desert torture camps and get away with it.<br /> <br /> No one gets to support a guy who openly suggests banning people from entering the country based on religion and is open to a registry of religious identity, and then pretend their AGAINST tribalism. His entire political ascent is based on tribalism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-13-2018, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T18:48:08-07:00","id":1218387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218322#post1218322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Look at Black Panther. When the hero is discussing that they can't &quot;handle the migrants&quot; because &quot;they bring their problems&quot; and his priority is &quot;the safety of his own people&quot; - I was like:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Wow, if they had &quot;real&quot; people say that, they'd call them a racist... but because it's a fictitious country, the <b>hero</b> can evince the viewpoints of political isolationists <b>without</b> demonizing them. He's a rational, thoughtful, protective leader - and it's the American, Killmonger, with his warped pan-identitarian politics who ends up killing people and blaming others for everything.</i></div></div> </div> </div> </div>... did you leave before the end of the movie or something? Because they specifically highlighted that T'Challa's earlier isolationism was in the wrong and made Wakanda complicit in what shaped Killmonger, hence the changing of his policies at the end of the film.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, speaking as a person who benefits from the perception of whiteness in the US - I have no self-loathing over it. I'm just capable of recognizing when a system benefits me at the expense of someone else in the present, as the US criminal justice system and media objectively do based on a mountain of empirical evidence, and wanting them not to, because despite your &quot;lions and lambs&quot; analogy, human beings evolved the capacity for empathy for other humans for a reason, and it is in fact of central importance to the survival of the species. Guilt has nothing to do with it. That's just a natural part of existing in a society - the question is how broadly you draw your &quot;society&quot; and extend your empathy, vs who you see as other. Hence the aforementioned Tribalism that has become central to the modern American Right Wing under Trumpism (to the chagrin of a lot of international free market, US leadership, NATO supporting conservatives who i greatly respect)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-13-2018, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T22:45:59-07:00","id":1218415,"title":"","content":"As this thread drifts in-and-out of politics - one wonders if maybe the hypothetical &quot;fantasy races&quot; should be political tropes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218386#post1218386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that was the case he wouldn't pardon people who recklessly disregard the rule of law</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether he defends or disregards the rule-of-law is <i>irrelevant</i>.<br /> <br /> And lets be clear - this is <b>not</b> a defense (nor condemnation) of Trump. He's <i>irrelevant</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>My point is</b> that there are a lot of left-leaning people who <i>take for granted</i> the idea that X, Y, Z demographics <i>owe them a vote</i>. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> And in a fit of divine irony, that same presumption then turns people away from them (because they simply blind themselves to the topics-of-debate among those demographics). Any question or belief that deviates from &quot;party ideology&quot; risks labeling you a horde of horrors. It's is <i>insidious </i>(on the Left) that any deviation from &quot;politically correct&quot; belief is tantamount to being a bigot.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Conservative Christians don't need Trump to be a Christian (nor are they less Christian for appreciating him) - they liken him to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyrus_the_Great_in_the_Bible\" target=\"_blank\">Cyrus the Great</a>. IE, Cyrus was never Jewish but the Israelites viewed him as a &quot;tool&quot; of God's will - likewise, Evangelicals can <i>personally</i> disapprove of Trump (lies, pornstars, etc) while <i>in the large scheme of things</i> view him as a tool of their deity. <br /> <br /> <b>Just look at </b>all the flack Kanye got a week ago for <i>daring</i> to express admiration for a conservative black female speaker (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BSAoitd1BTQ\" target=\"_blank\">her interview with Dave Rubin</a> months back explains how she switched politically). Others got flack for <i>daring</i> to say &quot;Black People don't need to be Democrats&quot;.<br /> <br /> I work in theater. I'm a socially-liberal, immigrant, Hispanic, non-Christian and favor black women - and yet <i>I've</i> had to deal with raving political extremists trying to conflate <i>me </i>with bigots because <i>I dare listen to both sides of the political aisle?</i> <br /> <br /> This happens all over the place. Ben Shapiro <i>is a conservative Jew</i> - but he gets called a Nazi? Milo Yiannopoulos <i>is flamboyantly gay</i> and married a black man - but he gets called a white supremacist<i>? </i>Ayaan Hirsi Ali is a <i>black Muslim female</i> and victim of genital mutilation - but she gets called <i>Islamophobic </i>for criticizing her faith and wishing they had a Reformation like Martin Luther? Sarah Haider is a <i>Pakistani American ex-Muslim</i> - but if she criticizes her former faith, people call her ignorant? Over and over, the groups the Left <i>pretends</i> to care about get tossed to the side the second they deviate from the political script.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218386#post1218386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His entire political ascent is based on tribalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>How exactly does your &quot;tribalism&quot; claim work into this equation though - when Central Americans are the tribe he disparages? You can't be telling me that Trump-favoring Central-Americans were wooed <b>by</b> his rhetoric?<br /> <br /> Hate (or Like) Trump all you like - <i>he's irrelevant</i>.<br /> <br /> My point is that with (any demographic) you need to <i>listen to their concerns</i> and not merely <i>caricature them</i>. The people &quot;on your side&quot; might not be &quot;on your team&quot; for the reasons you imagine - and the people &quot;on the opposite side&quot; might not be as villainous as you imagine. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> If you're a purist - then sure - his support for people who disregard the law is abhorrent! But most people aren't purists - they're practical. And <i>practically</i> speaking, lawlessness <i>is worse</i> &quot;back home&quot; than anything Joe Arpaio is doing - so if a little brutality <i>now </i>prevents a lot of brutality <i>later</i>, that sounds like a fair trade. Google &quot;Mexican cartel corpses&quot; - and the day Joe Arpaio is arrested for murdering and dismembering people <i>and then hanging the corpses from the express way</i>, then sure, I'm sure some of my peers will reconsider Joe.<br /> <br /> I knew something was up with the election in the winter of 2015 at a Christmas party. Almost all Hispanic. Everyone was engaged in the debates and news - but the &quot;oh that's interesting&quot; moment arose when I realized the only one excited about Clinton was <i>the lifelong Republican</i> - and everyone else had this weird vibe that the Republicans were getting a better range of choices (all of this 2 years before <a href=\"https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2017/11/02/clinton-brazile-hacks-2016-215774\" target=\"_blank\">Donna Brazile</a> explained why). Hate Trump all you like, that only shows how badly the opposition botched the job.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218387#post1218387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they specifically highlighted that T'Challa's earlier isolationism was in the wrong and made Wakanda complicit in what shaped Killmonger, hence the changing of his policies at the end of the film.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the &quot;isolationism was in the wrong&quot; any more than I can consider a &quot;shy bookworms desire to stay at home&quot; a &quot;crime&quot; or &quot;sin&quot;. No one owes anyone anything (and thus kindness can <b>only </b>be repaid with <i>gratitude</i>). The mindset that <i>anyone</i> <b>owes</b> their time, energy, resources, etc to anyone else only breeds thanklessness. T'Challa is benevolent in trying to fix American-problems through diplomacy - he was not <i>wrong</i> in prioritizing Wakanda earlier in the film.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Besides which, there's the issue of scale. Killmonger's father started the mess - via a crime of compassion - <i>stealing</i> from <i>Wakanda </i>and risking their safety in order to help <i>Americans</i>. <b>Then</b> he tried to murder a peer. <b>And this is the guy</b> whose reading material Killmonger inherited?<ul><li>In this thought-exercise, how do you blame Wakanda for wanting to be left alone? What guilt is there in that? Why isn't the guilt on the short-sighted, emotion-driven thief who imperilled his own country in order to fund armed conflict? And why is the isolationist culture responsible for a <i>clearly American</i> villain who (like many Americans) thinks <i>their personal experiences</i> reflect how the world works?</li> </ul>By your logic, if Greece has a bad economy - then Germany is &quot;complicit&quot; - because for some reason (Country A) is responsible for the problems in (Country B), and a refusal of (Country A) to invest resources to fix (Country B) makes (Country A) the bad guy?<br /> <br /> I'm baffled. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218387#post1218387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, speaking as a person who benefits from the perception of whiteness in the US - I have no self-loathing over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218387#post1218387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just capable of recognizing when a system benefits me at the expense of someone else in the present, as the US criminal justice system and media objectively do based on a mountain of empirical evidence, and wanting them not to, because despite your &quot;lions and lambs&quot; analogy, human beings evolved the capacity for empathy for other humans for a reason, and it is in fact of central importance to the survival of the species.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm aware that the criminal justice system has flaws - that doesn't amount to a &quot;benefit&quot; in favor of (Group A) so much as a &quot;detriment&quot; to (Group B).<br /> <br /> I've never seen or felt that &quot;us Hispanics are being victimized&quot; in order to &quot;benefit Anglo-Saxons&quot;. That isn't the case. And the few times my family has known someone in trouble with the law, <i>they deserved it</i> (and the harshness of any outcome was irrelevant - it was only a net-positive to see a couple troublemakers removed before they could endanger the community).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Sure, there are some people with biases who discriminate - but that's not <i>systemic</i>. There are laws against that. I've never seen a formal document at a company saying &quot;we do not hire Hispanics&quot;. <br /> <br /> <i>And in fact</i>, &quot;the system&quot; does the opposite. I earned 3 scholarships for school - and I'm grateful - but I <i>know</i> being Hispanic favored me. And I <i>know</i> there must be some non-Hispanic who wishes they could have competed for the same scholarships. I know there are jobs that <i>prefer</i> me because I'm multi-lingual (either to hit a quota or to handle other migrant customers).<br /> <br /> When looking at <i>systemic </i>factors, the US does an amazing job of trying to foster and empower minorities. <b>It's our prerogative</b> to do something with it. Asian-Americans usually do better than Anglo-Americans in school and work - but I'd find it hard to see someone argue that &quot;racist whites created a system to empower Asians!&quot; <i>It just doesn't make sense</i>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218387#post1218387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guilt has nothing to do with it. That's just a natural part of existing in a society - the question is how broadly you draw your &quot;society&quot; and extend your empathy, vs who you see as other. Hence the aforementioned Tribalism that has become central to the modern American Right Wing under Trumpism (to the chagrin of a lot of international free market, US leadership, NATO supporting conservatives who i greatly respect)</div> </div> </div> </div>The topics you list are way more productive than the broad-strokes of whether-or-not someone loves/hates the President's personality.<br /> <br /> The &quot;free market&quot; vs &quot;isolationism&quot; debate is great. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Back in the 90s, I remember when they pushed NAFTA as a &quot;great deal&quot; for everyone - but it upended Mexican society. The US subsidizes it's agricultural industry - Mexico doesn't - so it was suddenly cheaper to import corn grown in the US than to buy it from local Mexican farmers. <b>The result</b> is multi-generational family farms closing - male suicides skyrocketing (imagine being the farmers who thought themselves &quot;such failures&quot; that they personally destroyed their ancestral land). <b>Or</b> if suicide wasn't an option, they swapped to illicit crops (drugs) that the US couldn't compete with. <b>Meanwhile</b> <i>real sexism in hiring</i> took place, as maquiladoras exclusively favored hiring women (because they're cheaper and docile). <b>So now</b> mothers are working all day - fathers see legitimate businesses flounder - and children <i>grow up in that</i>. Yeah, there are some very anti-NAFTA Hispanic voices who would love to see Trump kill the treaty so they can untangle themselves from American influence.<br /> <br /> Even if Trump is a &quot;bull in a china shop&quot;, at least the discussion <i>is being had</i>. <br /> <br /> Or we can discuss how the &quot;peace&quot; claimed by international market liberalism doesn't work. The old claim was &quot;if country A has the water but country B grows the food, then trade will force them to never engage in war!&quot; ..... but lo', as Turkey builds dams to boost their own growth and agriculture, Syria gets less (so they want dams to save what they can) - and then Iraq gets less (so farms turn into desert). Free trade doesn't work when different countries have better locations/resources (like water) or laws/industries (like the US subsidizing its farmers - and competitors can't). <br /> <br /> It reminds me of the relationship Latin America had with Europe before the World Wars..... where we'd &quot;export raw materials&quot; - Europeans would craft them - and they'd &quot;export finished goods&quot;... and that was good? But then Europe destroyed itself twice over with 2 World Wars and Latin America (depending on that trade) found itself without factories or craftsmen to handle the demand. This is why Argentina notoriously favored Axis escapees - hoping that German and Italian engineers and craftsmen would let Argentina be independent from Europe. <br /> <br /> &quot;Peace through trade&quot; only made Latin America vulnerable to Europe's apparent suicide.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Or when talking about US leadership - I know a lot of <i>Americans</i> cringe at how Trump might be perceived - <i>but how is that exactly?</i> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">How did you feel when <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/asia_pacific/south-korean-president-credits-trump-with-bringing-north-korea-to-the-table/2018/01/10/ae0ee266-f606-11e7-91af-31ac729add94_story.html?utm_term=.15a316521012\" target=\"_blank\">South Korea credited</a> Trump with bringing North Korea to the table? Even China said he was crude but honest (and then <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2017/11/07/politics/trump-forbidden-city-beijing-china/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">welcomed him into the Forbidden City</a>, to which no foreign dignitary was invited in half a century).<br /> <br /> I feel like I hear some &quot;Americans&quot; constantly say &quot;what does the world think of us?!?!&quot; - and they <i>presume</i> the worse - instead of <i>actually asking</i>. Americans might think him a buffoon, but I think a lot of the world <i>takes him seriously</i>. You don't need to like nor admire a rottweiler in order to respect it &amp; avoid pissing it off.<br /> <br /> And why the self-consciousness? The Venezuelan bol\u00edvar is worth so little, anything below 100 <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-03-02/venezuelans-are-paying-a-100-premium-for-cash\" target=\"_blank\">is used as confetti</a> at baseball games ($100 bolivars = $0.0005). What Venezuelan in their right mind would be &quot;looking down upon&quot; US leadership - when our own leadership is so flawed, that people are <a href=\"http://www.foxnews.com/world/2017/03/23/starving-venezuelans-dying-for-eating-poisonous-yuca-sold-in-black-market.html\" target=\"_blank\">dying of poisoning</a> from eating the wrong roots? The average Venezuelan has lost 19lbs in the last year - and you think we're thumbing our noses, our wrist to our foreheads, thinking about Trump's tweets?<br /> <br /> Again - it <i>really feels</i> like Americans have an inflated sense of how Presidential decorum is valued. Some countries have monsters (who are looting their lands to get rich and flee) - and other countries have incompetents (who ignore local demands in favor of &quot;looking good&quot; on the world stage - and neither of those categories is taking the US less seriously just because your new President is blunter than the previous one.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All in all, <b>I have no personal feelings</b> - I won't earn a penny defending nor disparaging any side of the political aisle.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">But as a Hispanic immigrant - no, I don't believe America deserves anything <i>except gratitude</i> for how amazing this place is. Anyone who believes otherwise is welcome to &quot;take my spot&quot; and go live in Venezuela or Cuba. When in the history of the world were &quot;countries so full of oppression&quot; <i>so rabidly sought by migrants to go live there</i>? <br /> <br /> And no, I don't believe in demonizing any political extreme. I am <i>personally</i> liberal - but I have no tolerance for identity-politics-focused, emotionally-driven attacks on &quot;the opposition&quot;. <i>It makes us look bad</i> and it alienates people and it blinds us to &quot;real concerns&quot; when we reduce people to caricatures.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> I've said it before (I think) but thanks for the posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The back-and-forth is always useful (especially as I don't think I've ever played a game that really engaged in politics too heavily - or rather, I thought I did until now). Maybe Exalted could use a few Expys:<br /> <br /> I've never seen a floundering economy and starvation (ala Venezuela) or an NPC politician (like Trump) or even the odd ethnic exchanges the West has. Could you imagine people from Nexus arguing that they need to do more to help Sijanese immigrants? Do the Bull of the North's forces feel a need to help the people they conquered? Is there any ethnic strife between the people of Chiaroscuro? Do Realm tributaries in the West see themselves as victims (of the Realm), trade partners (who enjoy the Empire) or something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T22:46:26-07:00","id":1218416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218322#post1218322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you're religious, there are no &quot;natural born rights&quot;. Mother nature does not care about anyone's feelings or ethics. Lions don't ask lambs for permission to eat. It's as simple as:</div> </div> </div> </div>Show me in the human skull where there are carnassial molars, and you might have some consistency in making this statement. Hint: there aren't, and statements like the above are only ever used to shut people up in the process of inflicting something terrible on them. They also tend to come from Europe's social Darwinist streak, which is not actually very Darwinist, since it was cooked up by people who didn't know what was actually inheritable and what wasn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bad Muslims &quot;seek to convert the infidels&quot;? They enjoyed massive growth (fueled partially by the prohibition of enslaving other Muslims - meaning that as slaves converted and then had to be liberated, each generation had to conquer the next neighbor in order to fuel their trade).<br /> <br /> Good Christians &quot;turned the other cheek&quot;? They were enslaved and separated from their families (their pacifist inclinations flushed down the genetic toilet).<br /> <br /> Bad Christians repelled the invaders? They were viewed as heroes (and get laid as much as physically possible producing more sword-happy heroes). </div> </div> </div>Pacifism is generally taught rather than inherited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A few centuries later, it wasn't diplomacy or kindness that liberated them - it was admiration for masculine values of warfare, bravery, conquest. If you don't like the idea of military-heroes defining right-and-wrong, then Exalted might not be the setting for you. lol </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Exalted generally also portrays the use of arms as being something that escalates and complicates. And that's where we presently are - listening to you trying to load a kind of apologia for the US's worst parts because they apparently don't meet a bare minimum cruelty index.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're looking for moral/religious justifications, they're as irrelevant as kindness, diplomacy and feelings. </div> </div> </div>Which is an odd thing to say since without those, humans and most other social species wouldn't be very successful. Portraying rampant cruelty as &quot;the way of nature&quot; is a fallacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're looking for tactical justifications, it's super obvious - &quot;X territory has preyed upon our territory for centuries - so only by pacifying and converting X can we ensure our own safety&quot;. Then &quot;oh wait, now Y territory endangers X - let's take over Y&quot;. Then &quot;Z is nearby and could risk Y, lets handle that too.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>No nation</b> in history is innocent (unless they're extinct). This is not an ethical discussion, it's a tactical one. Ethics failed for 700 years, so tactics took over for the 300 afterward.<br /> <br /> You balk that a religious institution could justify war or slavery - I balk that the victims waited 700 years faithfully for permission to fight back. Dodo's went extinct because they knew neither to flee nor fight (and the same applies to civilizations). </div> </div> </div>Dodos went extinct because a large number of invasive species came across them and destroyed their habitat. If the islands hadn't been stripped bare, some kind of recovery could have been possible. In any case, it sure wasn't a cultural war, there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <b>Anyone</b> who thinks &quot;whites&quot; are so vicious to non-whites.... <i>are welcome</i> to try living in the home-countries <i>we</i> fled from. I can show you video of people cut up by chainsaw while still alive - or a guy getting his face carved off because he spoke to the wrong girl - and it's not the USA this takes place in. </div> </div> </div>No, the US organizes systematic machinery to ignore cops killing minorities, tacit approval of racist housing compacts, pricing affordable apartments in the toxic waste parts of town... shocking acts of singular violence eventually .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So <b>no</b>, Europe does not have &quot;the longest reach&quot; - the Mongols get that honor, by eradicating entire civilizations out of existence and pre-empting the possibility of descendants decrying their crimes. The mere fact that colonies <i>lived</i> to decry the colonialists kind of proves that the colonialists were already kinder than Genghis Khan ever was (<i>by their own admission</i>). There never was - nor will be - &quot;Mervites&quot; or &quot;Nishapurians&quot; in 2019 who get to look back and be upset at history. </div> </div> </div>Industrialization more than makes up for that, especially when it clears away and reshapes regions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The land-grab, colonization and enslaving.... is <i>precisely</i> what the Moors were doing in Iberia and the Ottoman's in Greece. It's been over half-a-thousand-years and the Ottoman's descendants (Turkey) <b>still</b> owns one of the oldest Greek cities (Alexandria / Constantinople / Istanbul). <b>They killed the inhabitants and took the land</b> - how is this not precisely the same thing? </div> </div> </div>What's different here is that Eastern and Southern Europe were largely left out to dry by Western Europe and Russia. It's a short trip to exploit people for resources or have proxy wars<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, whites dominate in the US - because they're the majority of the population. Same thing with Indians dominating in India, Chinese dominating in China, Nigerians in Nigeria and <b>every other society</b> on this planet. It is nothing but <i>self loathing</i> to tell a majority-population &quot;you should be ashamed of your existence&quot;. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Whites&quot;, really most western european protestants, in the US have their cultural power because of systematic machinery to keep everyone else out of power. It's not simply being the majority, it's being the majority and also racists taking pains to institute policies of white supremacy, like purging voter rolls, concern trolling over voter fraud, and various forms of de-regulation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you tell Israelites that they're too Israeli? </div> </div> </div>Kind of. You bring up Israel, I can only think about how Mike Pence and like minds in power want to instigate a war in the region that pits it against other ME powers so as to, in his view, usher in the end times. Yes, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>We have Hispanic heritage festivals</b> and no one claims &quot;those damn Anglos don't appreciate Hispanic culture&quot;.... <i>why should they?</i> It's our section, our festival for our people and our language and our culture. I don't get upset with non-Hispanics having their events - nor do I demand/expect that non-Hispanics come to ours. </div> </div> </div>Per the white supremacist policies of the US, Anglos have them all the time - it's pretty much day to day life, punctuated particularly hard during a standardized holiday. The trick is to get them to see it for what it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> If you believe in diversity, then you believe in differences.<br /> <br /> And some differences are irreconcilable.<br /> <br /> The same way a Nazi favoring &quot;racial purity&quot; would never reconcile with my Spanish &quot;mixing <i>is the best</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can't just scream &quot;racism&quot; when people bring up legitimate differences they want to discuss. </div> </div> </div>You can when someone says &quot;take pride in being white&quot;. That's not a good thing, it's an endorsement of white supremacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a documentary - <b>Empire of Dust</b> - covering the Chinese in the Congo. And there is a very poignant moment where the Chinese man is baffled by the locals - because the locals scream &quot;colonialism&quot; and &quot;oppression&quot; <b>but</b> the Chinese <b>were also</b> colonized and <b>now</b> they're an Empire of their own. So the Chinese man points out that the Dutch left <i>half a century ago</i> and left behind infrastructure and technology that China didn't have - and yet the locals let it rot. </div> </div> </div>The Dutch were extremely efficient at removing all the wealth from the region. There probably wasn't much left to maintain the infrastructure - it was all lining Leopold II's pockets... and still is. This isn't the work of centuries past, it was extremely modern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, native cultures went the way of the dodo - <b>but that's nature</b>. </div> </div> </div>No, it's apathy and cruelty. Western Europeans and Russians directed it and weaponized it. It was a conscious effort, and it continues mostly because of the inertia from when its architects first set it into motion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T01:49:27-07:00","id":1218441,"title":"","content":"Disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T07:06:44-07:00","id":1218516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218339#post1218339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lucky me, my group floats from one game to another - so I can mull this at leisure. Exalted Castes certainly work for tropes (but since I'm going low-powered to start, Exalted are off the table) - although even then, there's no hard-fix where Dawn-Castes are all stoic, gruff warlords, etc.<br /> <br /> More and more, obfuscation comes to mind. The more people compared 3E and 2E, the more I realize the sort of &quot;omniscient perspective&quot; of 2E precluded a lot of mystery.<br /> <br /> So for example, don't introduce a bunch of new players playing merely-mortals to &quot;the Lunar Exalted chosen by Luna create Beastmen races&quot; - but break it down into &quot;the renown Cattalestae archers&quot;, the cult of the &quot;Third Eye Pyramid&quot;, followers of &quot;Zatesh&quot; and all those other aspects of Luna. Instead of a simplified, uniform, omniscient &quot;all Beastmen are X&quot;, it could be a dozen &quot;god-touched&quot; peoples with physical mutations or the like. Players don't even need to realize they're all the same deity.<br /> <br /> Likewise for other X-Blooded types.<br /> <br /> Take Demon-Blooded. Instead of &quot;all Demons are born from Demons, spawned by the Yozis&quot; - break it down into &quot;Vigilants of Granalkin&quot;, the &quot;Golden Jannisary Templars&quot;, and other demon-hunting groups (with different origins)..... as well as one-shots like &quot;dead children resurrected by Naamah&quot;, etc. OOC, as a ST, I can know they're Demon-Blooded - but IC, they could all have different origin myths. The function OOC/IC is that &quot;whoever picks one of these obviously wants me to engage in more spooky-dooky content&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm giving this thought. It's been fun seeing the conversation back-and-forth meanwhile, as well as reading up on other RPGs (to see what works for them).</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're suggesting, I think... similar to An-Teng's serpentfolk, right? Who no one sees as &quot;serpentfolk&quot;, they see them simply as a particular subset of Tengese.<br /> <br /> Lucky you indeed, my group wants <i>consistency</i> from me... pfah, <b>consistency</b>! How can you not see there are so many beautiful settings and we <b>NEED</b> to explore them <b>ALL RIGHT NOW</b> (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> Anyways, yeah, I like the idea of presenting different beastfolk as completely unrelated groups, at least at first, when the players still don't know what exactly beastfolk are (although at this point in Ex3 I'm not sure I know either... I mean, I don't think the only way to create them will be for Lunars to practice bestiality. But we'll see).<br /> <br /> It's interesting that you mention &quot;dead children resurrected by Naamah&quot;, as there is no true resurrection in Exalted - but of course all manners of rumors can be spread about the progeny of a certain demon, and they can also culturally see themselves as a group as dead and reborn, etc.<br /> <br /> I think these are really interesting points that add even more variety to Creation. I'll bear them in mind - obfuscation for the win! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T07:19:30-07:00","id":1218521,"title":"","content":"Appeals to nature as a note often fall into the is-ought problem. Namely that there's no reasonable way to derive an &quot;ought&quot; statement from an &quot;is&quot; statement. Which is often what appeals to nature do: It's how it is so we should jsut perpetuate it, or it's how it is so there's no moral issue due to it being hwo it is.<br /> <br /> They often are circular and not pretty helpful. And often used quite a bit since Greece for groups in power to justify their being in power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T08:09:13-07:00","id":1218545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218441#post1218441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like.. what did you expect? Seriously?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:01:12-07:00","id":1218595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything</div> </div> </div> </div><b>re: Molars, Industrialization, Cruelty, Dodos &amp; Pacifism (taught or inherited)</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The contents of our mouth are irrelevant - the point (and reality) is that we're not peaceful herbivores grazing on a field. Human beings in <i>every culture</i> in <i>every age</i> have engaged in violence. I refuse to demonize Europeans as somehow &quot;more evil than everyone else&quot;. The analogy to &quot;lions and prey&quot; is to say that &quot;if (Group A) invades (Group B), diplomacy won't amount to anything if they don't want to be diplomatic&quot;.<br /> <br /> And you bring up &quot;industrialization&quot; - but that goes back to <i>reach</i> vs <i>intent</i>. If two groups want to kill me - (Group A) has a gun and (Group B) has a knife - the difference in technology <b>does not</b> equate to a difference in intent. (Group A) is not more malevolent than (Group B) - merely more competent. If Genghis Khan had nukes, he'd fire them off without flinching.<br /> <br /> Cruelty and Success are two different things. I agree it's not a success-tactic in the long-term - the Mongols are far from dominant today. <b>But</b> long-term success is irrelevant compared to long-term extinction. The Mongols <i>at least still exist</i> while the various bloodlines they ended <i>don't</i>. So I am <b>not advocating</b> for cruelty - I just refuse to praise or admire &quot;peaceful martyrs&quot;. A large chunk of the Mongols success was <i>their reputation</i>, with people surrendering rather than fighting - including some of those cities they decided to annihilate anyways.<br /> <br /> I don't get your point with Dodos. Yes, an invasive species (humans) destroyed them. Yes, they might have recuperated if left alone. How is this not comparable to humans? The Mongols were invasive to Merv and Nishapur and destroyed them. <i>Sure</i>, if they were left alone, they might have recuperated - <b>but is that admirable?</b> Does anyone hate warfare <i>to the extreme</i> that they'd rather be slaughtered like Dodos and then just rebuild (hopefully)?<br /> <br /> Which leads me to pacifism - it doesn't matter if inherited or taught - <i>if the pacifists are dead</i>, then they won't be around to teach or sire future generations. The Moors didn't arbitrarily leave Iberia - they avoided / left the most warlike provinces <i>first</i>. Pacifists who embraced &quot;the new rulers&quot; <i>enabled and empowered and encouraged</i> the conquerors - hawks eager to fight <i>discouraged and removed them</i>. <b>Ergo</b>, if I blame anyone for anything, it'd have to be the peaceful provinces who made it easy to settle-in. One of the reasons the Inquisition focused on the Basque (but left the pagan Galicians alone) was because the Basque were favored by the Moors (while the Galicians were so bellicose, the Moors left almost as soon as they arrived).<br /> <br /> All in all, Europeans don't have some special status as &quot;most evil&quot; race. I don't see any virtue or logic in demonizing an entire phenotype.<br /> <br /> <b>There's also some irony</b> in that some people are uncomfortable with &quot;all Dwarves are like stodgy and masculine&quot; and &quot;all Tieflings are like chaotic evil&quot; - and yet, when I refuse to demonize Europeans with a caricature, that ruffles feathers?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's where we presently are - listening to you trying to load a kind of apologia for the US's worst parts because they apparently don't meet a bare minimum cruelty index.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inaccurate.<br /> <br /> Miami is 70% Hispanic, 20% Black (usually Haitian or Jamaican) and the 10% remainder <i>other immigrants</i>. The city wouldn't be so full of migrants unless our home-countries are <i>infinitely worse</i>. It is <b>rare</b> to hear any &quot;of us&quot; talk about &quot;going back&quot; (with the exception of the elderly who want to retire somewhere cheap).<br /> <br /> <b>Therefore</b>, I can <b>only express gratitude</b> to the kindness of this country.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Does this upset you?<br /> <br /> Is there something offensive that I'm missing - in immigrants saying &quot;this country is good&quot;?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's perfect.<br /> <br /> But it's not Cuba, where I've met 4 year olds being raised for prostitution <i>by the government</i>. Where political dissidents are locked in cells the size of a closet, without light, with food poured from the ceiling (to fall on you and mix with the water and piss on the floor). Where every 3-6 months, as soon as you have a moderately decent business, someone in the government will confiscate the property and you have to restart (or stay poor enough they don't notice you). Every Cuban male in my family spent some period of time in prison <i>for wanting to leave</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not Venezuela, where teenagers have died of poisoning - because they were eating <i>raw roots</i> from plants in the street - to combat starvation. Where women (mothers, wives, daughters) are crossing over to Columbia to prostitute themselves so they can feed their family (to the prevalence that Columbia has actually said they won't consider it criminal, because the need is too great). The US is not Venezuela - which my parents fled due to child-kidnappings in their neighborhood. You couldn't even wear jewelry without the risk of someone ripping it off your ear. (And in case you think I'm far removed - Miami's &quot;City of Doral&quot; is predominantly Venezuelan immigrants who fled in the last few years. People who preferred to be poor / middle-class in the US over rich in Venezuela.)<br /> <br /> It's not Honduras where the murder rate is the highest in the world (82 per 100,000).<br /> <br /> It's not Mexico where <i>even Hispanics</i> talk (among ourselves) about where we can't vacation because the cartels own X town or Y hotel chain.<br /> <br /> (etc etc etc)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Is the US perfect? I never said that.<br /> <br /> But it's <i>far from the worst</i>. And if we lacked gratitude, we'd <i>go back to where we came from</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the US organizes systematic machinery to ignore cops killing minorities, tacit approval of racist housing compacts, pricing affordable apartments in the toxic waste parts of town... shocking acts of singular violence eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does the <b>US</b> list this? I know you had Jim Crow laws and anti-miscegenation laws (removed with Loving vs Virginia) - but most of those were overturned a half-century ago.<br /> <br /> At this point, yes - <b>individual</b> politicians and bureaucrats engage in sleazy practices - but there's no <b>systemic</b>, 50-state wide law or amendment mandating bigotry. My cousin was not prohibited from becoming a cop; I was not prohibited from going to college; my family was never prohibited from starting a business; no one has ever knocked on my door saying I can't date outside &quot;my race&quot;.<br /> <br /> Say that there are individuals who are corrupt or bigoted?<br /> <br /> <b>Agreed!</b><br /> <br /> But condemn an entire phenotype for some kind of collective crime?<br /> <br /> <b>Abhorrent.</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I remember in Elementary I had a fairly racist teacher, Mrs. Green. I think she was German-American. She mispronounced our names on purpose (so that we'd abandon Spanish names and adopt English nicknames); if I played with the other boys, they were just &quot;rough-housing&quot; but I was &quot;fighting&quot; (and get dragged off); if the Anglo-boys used foul-language they were &quot;being boys&quot; but if I asked her what a word meant (because I barely spoke English), she dragged me off arguing I should &quot;be expelled for disrespect&quot;. It was a dozen little things trying to get me expelled or removed from the class.<br /> <br /> But was that <b>systemic?</b> No. It was one bigot with a little authority who I eventually got away from.<br /> <br /> I then went to another school - an all Black Baptist private school - for a brief time. <i>They also</i> weren't fond of Hispanics nor Catholics. It upset some that I was <i>clearly irreverent</i> but I knew the religious materials <i>by memory</i> (so I could cite scripture off-the-cuff while others fumbled through their books to verify). They also tried to give me grief.<br /> <br /> But was that <b>system?</b> No. It was a few religious bigots with a little authority who I eventually got away from.<br /> <br /> And neither extreme was enough for me to demonize either demographic. <i>The world is full of assholes</i>. I refuse to condemn 100 because 5 or 10 are unpleasant. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Whites&quot;, really most western european protestants, in the US have their cultural power because of systematic machinery to keep everyone else out of power. It's not simply being the majority, it's being the majority and also racists taking pains to institute policies of white supremacy, like purging voter rolls, concern trolling over voter fraud, and various forms of de-regulation.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet Jews, Irish, Italians, Poles and a host of other Europeans had to - at various stages - sue and fight to be considered &quot;white&quot;. Hispanics of various shades are currently &quot;up in the air&quot; as to how they're categorized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's different here is that Eastern and Southern Europe were largely left out to dry by Western Europe and Russia. It's a short trip to exploit people for resources or have proxy wars</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't follow you here - please elaborate?<br /> <br /> My point is that (a) the Moors invaded Iberia (with intent to enslave people and take land) - and (b) the Ottoman's invaded Eastern Europe (with intent to enslave people and take land). Both had different levels of success (Iberia was much more deliberate in joining-forces and purging them later).<br /> <br /> What do you mean by &quot;left out to dry by Western Europe and Russia&quot; - are you implying it's their fault? Why should I blame France or England for what the Moors did to Iberia - and why should I blame Russia for what the Ottoman's did to Eastern Europe?<br /> <br /> It <b>really feels</b> like you're just trying to reframe those invasions in such a way that you can &quot;blame other Europeans&quot; somehow? Or maybe I'm misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full stop.<br /> <br /> I asked &quot;Would you accuse Israel of being too pro-Israel?&quot; <i>What else could they be?</i><br /> <br /> Is Ghana too pro-Ghana? Do you think South Korea is too pro-Korean?<br /> <br /> What is the purpose of a country if not to take care of their people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the white supremacist policies of the US, Anglos have them all the time - it's pretty much day to day life, punctuated particularly hard during a standardized holiday. The trick is to get them to see it for what it is.<br /> <br /> You can when someone says &quot;take pride in being white&quot;. That's not a good thing, it's an endorsement of white supremacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you link some examples? I'm sincerely curious to see what they're like.<br /> <br /> The chief criticism I have for &quot;them&quot; is the idea of &quot;whiteness&quot; (just like &quot;blackness&quot;, &quot;redness&quot;, &quot;yellowness&quot;, etc). &quot;White&quot; just sounds like a term for confused people divorced from their ancestry (because Europe is full of contradictory and clashing cultures).<br /> <br /> <b>However, </b>I can grok an Irish-heritage, Italian-heritage, Polish-heritage, etc - each culture has art and language and history that makes them unique. And while I don't doubt there are bigots - I <i>know</i> some just wish they had a heritage to attach to.<br /> <br /> So the same way I differentiate different Hispanic sub-groups - I usually engage &quot;whites&quot; based on sub-group.<br /> <br /> So for example, I would never regard Roswynn as &quot;white&quot; - because her skin color tells me nothing about her character.<br /> <br /> But I would 100% try to engage her on Italian-ess (because I have some Italian friends and the cultural overlap is a great intro).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218416#post1218416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dutch were extremely efficient at removing all the wealth from the region. There probably wasn't much left to maintain the infrastructure - it was all lining Leopold II's pockets... and still is. This isn't the work of centuries past, it was extremely modern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your theory is contradicting the Chinese engineers <b>on the ground</b> there. So maybe the documentary was wrong? Maybe you're right and the Chinese repairing infrastructure are wrong in their evaluation of the remains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 05-14-2018, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T10:33:08-07:00","id":1218607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218516#post1218516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, yeah, I like the idea of presenting different beastfolk as completely unrelated groups, at least at first, when the players still don't know what exactly beastfolk are (although at this point in Ex3 I'm not sure I know either... I mean, I don't think the only way to create them will be for Lunars to practice bestiality. But we'll see).<br /> <br /> It's interesting that you mention &quot;dead children resurrected by Naamah&quot;, as there is no true resurrection in Exalted - but of course all manners of rumors can be spread about the progeny of a certain demon, and they can also culturally see themselves as a group as dead and reborn, etc.<br /> <br /> I think these are really interesting points that add even more variety to Creation. I'll bear them in mind - obfuscation for the win! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup! More and more, it's <b>less about fantasy races</b> and more about <b>playing up the mystery</b> of existing groups. In hindsight, the <b>best</b> thing I can do is <b>not</b> let my players read too much on the lore. <br /> <br /> I mean, I understand the importance of &quot;omniscience&quot; as an ST - given that it's a setting with gods and Sidereals who can (and should) be aware of history &quot;from an omniscient&quot; perspective. <br /> <br /> But now I grok the value in obfuscation (for player enjoyment).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218521#post1218521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appeals to nature as a note often fall into the is-ought problem. Namely that there's no reasonable way to derive an &quot;ought&quot; statement from an &quot;is&quot; statement. Which is often what appeals to nature do: It's how it is so we should just perpetuate it, or it's how it is so there's no moral issue due to it being who it is.<br /> <br /> They often are circular and not pretty helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed! <br /> <br /> Science tries to explain &quot;what is&quot; vs Religion tries to explain &quot;what should be&quot;. Little good comes from the overlap.<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>But again, &quot;just to be clear&quot;</b> - I'm <b>not </b>defending atrocities, lol. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">The sum all of my posts are:</span></b><ul><li>I find it unethical and unproductive to condemn an entire phenotype for a &quot;collective guilt&quot;. It's not accurate; it doesn't win allies; it doesn't help dialogue.</li> <li>Even when &quot;foul things happened&quot; - we need to look at <i>history</i> to see what-caused-what. I can't blame Romania for France nor Japan for China nor Aztecs for Incas.</li> <li>I don't like to caricature real-life groups of people - give everyone a fair listen and you often find commonalities. <i>Individuals</i> are good or bad.</li> <li>&quot;Virtue&quot; - without the will to defend it - isn't virtuous.</li> </ul>And as a migrant, <i>the US is fucking great</i>. If you're upset and want things to get better? <i>Awesome - that's just a further testament to how great the people are here</i>. I refuse to be an ingrate when I compare cousins overseas who have it infinitely worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:44:15-07:00","id":1218628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1218607#post1218607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup! More and more, it's <b>less about fantasy races</b> and more about <b>playing up the mystery</b> of existing groups. In hindsight, the <b>best</b> thing I can do is <b>not</b> let my players read too much on the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to this, I completely keep the books away from my players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They don't have much time to read them anyways - work, kids... - but they're new to Exalted and I want them to discover everything very, very gradually. Right now, for them, &quot;Exalted&quot; are the Realm's Dragon Blooded (and some lost eggs) - the rest are conceivably Anathema, according to the predominant narrative (Immaculate Faith). Of course, they've met a Lunar who doesn't seem evil... and the Realm is notorious for substituting local faiths with their state religion... so they're not exactly trusting the &quot;official version&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yes! Playing up the mistery of existing groups is a great way to give the players a realistic perspective of what their characters know (most of the time - of course a Sidereal learns a lot about the true history of the setting quite soon while in Yu-Shan - while an Abyssal, hah, that really depends on the Deathlord and how they spin it...).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, I understand the importance of &quot;omniscience&quot; as an ST - given that it's a setting with gods and Sidereals who can (and should) be aware of history &quot;from an omniscient&quot; perspective.<br /> <br /> But now I grok the value in obfuscation (for player enjoyment). </div> </div> </div>Exactly! You can really give individual traits to various communities and peoples, make them different from anything else, mix and match themes and tropes - and you'll still have a lot of individual npcs who will each be their own version of the shared background! It can work very well!<br /> <br /> Oh, since you put together a summary of the main ideas you are writing about here, and I'm really not able to keep up with you and the others, I'll seize the occasion to comment on what you've summed up:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>But again, &quot;just to be clear&quot;</b> - I'm <b>not </b>defending atrocities, lol.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">The sum all of my posts are:</span></b><ul><li>I find it unethical and unproductive to condemn an entire phenotype for a &quot;collective guilt&quot;. It's not accurate; it doesn't win allies; it doesn't help dialogue.</li> <li>Even when &quot;foul things happened&quot; - we need to look at <i>history</i> to see what-caused-what. I can't blame Romania for France nor Japan for China nor Aztecs for Incas.</li> <li>I don't like to caricature real-life groups of people - give everyone a fair listen and you often find commonalities. <i>Individuals</i> are good or bad.</li> <li>&quot;Virtue&quot; - without the will to defend it - isn't virtuous.</li> </ul>And as a migrant, <i>the US is fucking great</i>. If you're upset and want things to get better? <i>Awesome - that's just a further testament to how great the people are here</i>. I refuse to be an ingrate when I compare cousins overseas who have it infinitely worse. </div> </div> </div>Okay, so:<ul><li>I absolutely agree - blanket statements and generalizations are <i>the worst</i>, whomever one is applying them to - and you're right, it's not accurate, and self-loathing doesn't absolutely help anyone - at most it annoys other people who have much more serious concerns than listening to you wallowing in self-pity.</li> <li>No, you can't blame someone only because of cultural/geographical proximity to the culprit.</li> <li>I absolutely agree about caricaturing people - same with finding commonalities, definitely.</li> <li>Virtue... mmm. I would say it differently, like: &quot;Ethics need to be defended if you want them to take root and grow&quot;?</li> <li>And as you're a migrant I understand, from what you told us of poorer countries you've had experience with and relatives in, that you love the US! Of course - from that point of view it's really a great country, no argument there. But, <i>yes</i>, it would be really cool to make things better - in the US and in Europe - while self-loathing and saying &quot;Whites are eeebul!!&quot; doesn't help in the least, some self-critique and sociopolitical awareness could make our lands more hospitable towards minorities, and could also make us stop - or at least reduce - our exploitation of other countries and peoples. That'd be great. It would also help finding commonalities if minorities received a fairer treatment - it would promote a truly global melting pot where everyone could be equal in all their diversity and individuality.</li> </ul>Personally, <i>I'm not saying </i>we whites are evil and everyone else is good and needs to be coddled - what I'm trying (without much success!) to express, is that <i>I believe we can do much better, </i>and also <i>I'm really disgusted with the resurgence of various white-supremacist/neonazi/fascist movements in my culture</i>.<br /> <br /> There are other things I'd like, but they're... difficult, at present. Also they don't have much to do with race, which is what this thread originated about - so that's it! I think, if not in all the details, we basically agree in the end <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13651,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","user":"Roswynn","date":". 05-15-2018, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T15:15:43-07:00","id":1303197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1212325#post1212325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should be noted that Lintha as they exist today are actually not anything to do wiht the Lintha of the past and their being non-human or not is implied as potentially propoganda in the <b>Blood &amp; Salt</b> depiction. A big thing I think with their &quot;not really human&quot; thing was that it was as I gather supposed to be an example of nationlaistic racism and how people in that mindset are very prone ot build up mythologies for themselves.<br /> <br /> 2e took a lot of the Lintha origin story they told themselves as fact, but seeing as Dukantha was an Exalt and they are human enough for most htings, I think what edition is being talked about and how much of htier origins are real or not should be kind of considered in a lot of this.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something like a demented twist on the &quot;descended from the Naga&quot; national myths of the Khmer? Never really thought of it even though it does loads of sense indeed.<br /> <br /> Now i'm thinking of making some civilization inspired by Theban legend of the Spartoi sprung from dragon's teeth. Might mix &amp; match with some other things along the way. Hmmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T16:37:05-07:00","id":1303217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303197#post1303197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something like a demented twist on the &quot;descended from the Naga&quot; national myths of the Khmer? Never really thought of it even though it does loads of sense indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like the game was made by people who incorporated aspects of real-world cultures and economics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T18:32:17-07:00","id":1303228,"title":"","content":"I hope this edition doesn't go the Lintha as not-entrely-human route again<br /> <br /> A demon worshippping cult sure, but still human","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T18:41:35-07:00","id":1303230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303228#post1303228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this edition doesn't go the Lintha as not-entrely-human route again<br /> <br /> A demon worshippping cult sure, but still human</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they have a history of demon blood carefully maintained by their most inbred family lines terrified of losing that trait, but nothing more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T19:19:56-07:00","id":1303231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303228#post1303228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this edition doesn't go the Lintha as not-entrely-human route again<br /> <br /> A demon worshippping cult sure, but still human</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I would personally prefer more non-human races.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T19:25:52-07:00","id":1303233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303228#post1303228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this edition doesn't go the Lintha as not-entrely-human route again</div> </div> </div> </div>They'd hardly be in bad company; there are hybrids between humans and gods or beasts dotted all across Creation.<br /> <br /> Mind, it's one of the quirks of this setting that one can be the product of such a union and still be entirely human. And not just in an ideological sense.<br /> <br /> Now, if this is a statement about not wanting them to be descendants of mingling between human ancestors and Kimbery specifically, that's a horse of a different colour.<br /> <br /> Or did you mean the middle Second Edition idea of the original Lintha being an entirely separate (but still humanoid) species that ultimately propagated and diluted itself by crossing with humans?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T21:17:22-07:00","id":1303242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303231#post1303231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I would personally prefer more non-human races.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the case of the Lintha, it's because their role got over-blown and over-emphasized on what amoutned to reifying myths as I noted before. And I think that of anything that was a not-human, they were actually pretty bad for it even in 2e. They were essentially Star Trek aliens in the weird hair and skin color and demon-based Charms and that was it? They didn't really even jusitfy their inhumanity besides it being an easy out for them being evil/eating people.<br /> <br /> Additonally, it's generally just a human-centric game, and while I am sure we'll see hints of other non-human races, they're just not important to a lot of Creation unless they add something interesting/exotic like Dragon Kings or plegials do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T21:31:14-07:00","id":1303244,"title":"","content":"My problem is twofold. One, i'm not a big fan of races that look almost exactly human but aren't and are therefore all magical. 2E presented the Lintha ancestors as not-human, but looked human. I hate that (and due to the feel of the setting, and Lintha specifically, I cant suspend my disbelief for this like I can for elves)<br /> <br /> Second, go read Scavenger Sons. The Lintha there were totally different from the later descriptions. They werent a race, or even a tribe. They were more like a crime syndicate. People could join in, others tried to leave (and got dragged back in). Totally different from the demon tribe that preached blood purity.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not against said syndicate being led by a Kimberry cult. Or against an Infernally descended tribe being somewhere else. But I liked the SS Lintha better than the B&amp;S version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 04-07-2019, 03:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T22:10:49-07:00","id":1303251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303231#post1303231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I would personally prefer more non-human races.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some actual nonhuman races would be cool. Humanoids with green skin and [X]-blooded powers are not actually nonhuman by Creation\u2019s standards.<br /> <br /> Dragon Kings should present the MINIMUM for how inhuman any new non-human sapient species in Creation are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T23:38:19-07:00","id":1303257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303217#post1303217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's almost like the game was made by people who incorporated aspects of real-world cultures and economics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or paleontology. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303251#post1303251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Some actual nonhuman races would be cool. Humanoids with green skin and [X]-blooded powers are not actually nonhuman by Creation\u2019s standards.<br /> <br /> Dragon Kings should present the MINIMUM for how inhuman any new non-human sapient species in Creation are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can totally dig that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T02:10:56-07:00","id":1303269,"title":"","content":"I thought the &quot;people descended from a non-human race&quot; as leaders of the crime family was fine, it's just that fans tended to forget that the guys with green skin, white hair, and slightly weird elongated bodies might think they're 80% Lintha but are actually about 5% Lintha. So presumably the original Lintha looked way, way more inhuman.<br /> (It also had that a lot of what the Lintha think is Lintha characteristics is actually from all the demons and other spirits they've interbred with. For example, there's many Lintha with gills, but this isn't actually something they got from the original Lintha.)<br /> <br /> I think it was partly because &quot;Lintha charms&quot; were talked about a lot, when really most Lintha with charms should have been using demon charms because they're demon-bloods.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T03:49:10-07:00","id":1303278,"title":"","content":"well, whatever the problem was, the writers focused too much on one aspect and undid another in the prospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T03:53:38-07:00","id":1303280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303269#post1303269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the &quot;people descended from a non-human race&quot; as leaders of the crime family was fine, it's just that fans tended to forget that the guys with green skin, white hair, and slightly weird elongated bodies might think they're 80% Lintha but are actually about 5% Lintha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or 0%. To reiterate, it might just be propaganda.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T04:11:05-07:00","id":1303282,"title":"","content":"IIRC Vance has said that in 3e the original lintha were demon blooded humans.<br /> <br /> Or primordial blooded or whatever.<br /> <br /> Kimbery + mortal = Lintha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T04:35:27-07:00","id":1303287,"title":"","content":"I have some outlines for an &quot;actual&quot; non-human race that I might put up on the forums for feedback if I ever get the time to finish their write-up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T04:38:46-07:00","id":1303288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303282#post1303282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Vance has said that in 3e the original lintha were...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I get that, but keep in mind that the modern folks calling themselves Lintha might well share zero blood with the Lintha of old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T04:47:40-07:00","id":1303290,"title":"","content":"Personally I loved Lintha as a seperate but close to human species. Their mechanics were a bit wonky, the little we got, but I wouldnt personally mind if they were just Kimberrys version of humans as long as they were stable enough of a line to be considered a race of their own. Demon Charms work fine for them but again I would have liked for them to have something of their own like the Dragon King\u2019s got.<br /> <br /> But then again the only thing that generally bothers me in Exalted, aside from second editions only exalted matter frame of mind, is it\u2019s worlds humanocentricism. I am personally annoyed how almost every fantasy setting out there, no matter how ingenious it is otherwise, has humans in it and usually in a very central role of either being the race that is rising to prominence or the race that has already done so. That is propably why my first editions favored character template were the Fair Folk and to a lesser extent the Alchemicals, whom I didn\u2019t have any real chance to play as most St\u2019s didn\u2019t involve them in their creation, and the Dragon-Blooded whom I have always played very elementally including their looks being more reminescent of elementals in human shape than humans. And naturally for me the best thing out of second edition, and the one that finally got me to move on to that editions of the game from1st were the Infernal Exalted.<br /> <br /> So this is more of a personal beef with me. Still I welcome any even remotly non-human aspect that gets to stay in the game especially the Lintha whom I have always loved.<br /> <br /> Playable Lintha with their own power set would be my personal dream and I\u2019d take them rather than some new type of Exalted. I think the world of Exalted would be enriched by there being more variation in the actual beings living there in opposition to there just being more Exalted. <br /> <br /> But then again my opinion hardly matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Typos as per usual 04-07-2019, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T04:53:30-07:00","id":1303292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303287#post1303287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have some outlines for an &quot;actual&quot; non-human race that I might put up on the forums for feedback if I ever get the time to finish their write-up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T05:14:00-07:00","id":1303295,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303242#post1303242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They didn't really even jusitfy their inhumanity besides it being an easy out for them being evil/eating people.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Seriously, people <i>always</i> forget that the Lintha were portrayed as virtually always only ever eating <b>one another</b>. They regarded it as a respectful gesture (as many real life cannibalistic cultures have)!</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They were actually averse to eating the flesh of other humans, because they thought they were unworthy of the honour and that doing so would contaminate them, and they reserved a special ire for anybody else that might eat the Lintha. There's an implication that they'd eat fallen Exalted, and a particularly respectable mortal warrior might get a small portion of their heart consumed, but that was it.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sure they encouraged recruited members to the Family to also engage in cannibalism, which would thus be directed at other mortals, but by that point one is going far abreast of them engaging in cannibalism because of inborn evil due to inhumanity (which has to be a poor lookout for all real life cannibalistic cultures).</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303244#post1303244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I liked the SS Lintha better than the B&amp;S version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that. I wonder if an ideal version of the Lintha might be somewhere between the two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T05:37:53-07:00","id":1303300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again the only thing that generally bothers me in Exalted, aside from second editions only exalted matter frame of mind, is it\u2019s worlds humanocentricism. I am personally annoyed how almost every fantasy setting out there, no matter how ingenious it is otherwise, has humans in it and usually in a very central role of either being the race that is rising to prominence or the race that has already done so. That is propably why my first editions favored character template were the Fair Folk and to a lesser extent the Alchemicals, whom I didn\u2019t have any real chance to play as most St\u2019s didn\u2019t involve them in their creation, and the Dragon-Blooded whom I have always played very elementally including their looks being more reminescent of elementals in human shape than humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon-Blooded and Alchemicals are human, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T06:38:23-07:00","id":1303311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> IIRC Vance has said that in 3e the original lintha were demon blooded humans.<br /> <br /> Or primordial blooded or whatever.<br /> <br /> Kimbery + mortal = Lintha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this is kind of fine. While I actually like the Lintha as a demon-worshipping cult of cannibal pirates with a certain demonic exoticism, as a pre-human species the Lintha weren't really as good as Dragon Kings or Alaun or something, because they were, well, not very inhuman. So just being demon-blooded is fine.<br /> Any ancient pre-human race whose lost cities are well proportioned for humans isn't really doing a good job.<br /> And saying &quot;one large foe of the Exalted host were humans who were loyal to the Primordials because of their demonic blood&quot; is also fine.<br /> <br /> But I would still like to see plenty of bizarre non-human races.<br /> (Which, probably, is what the Gigants of Dis and the Backbenders are.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon-Blooded and Alchemicals are human, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, while Alchemicals and Dragonblood are metaphysically human, I could see that a player who thinks &quot;playing a human is pretty dull&quot; might gravitate towards them as somewhat physically inhuman (though I think Alchemicals much more than Dragonblood), even with human minds and souls (which makes them easier to roleplay than an entirely inhuman creature, potentially!).<br /> <br /> But then, saying that...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only thing that generally bothers me in Exalted, aside from second editions only exalted matter frame of mind, is it\u2019s worlds humanocentricism... the Alchemicals... the Dragon-Blooded</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Alchemicals and Dragonblood (played to look very elemental, which is fine with me) are inhuman enough for you, what about mutants and beastmen?<br /> <br /> My players just arrived at a human city where they met a holy order of Minotaur warrior-monks. They also saw some rat-people in the streets, and orca-people at the docks. And a lobster-man offered to buy one of the PCs (who was in red panda form).<br /> <br /> You can also do a lot with mutants that aren't beastmen. Cyclopses, winged people (one of my friends has played both a Dragonblood mutated by a wyld storm to get wings, and also a priest from a whole race of winged people). In the game I play, the nearby mountain peaks are home to the Thoth Mek Shar, a race of 7 foot tall, 3-eyed scaled people.<br /> <br /> I mean, I would like to see some more non-human races that aren't spirits, like the Dragon Kings (and 3rd ed I think is a bit better for this), or at least more stuff that's pre-human (ancient ruins, bizarre magicks, etc).<br /> But I find stuff like elves and dwarves, and tbh tall green thin guys with white hair (the Lintha) to be, well, just basically strange looking humans. I mean, a Djala is more out there than a Halfling, honestly. And I'm not sure that a setting that prides itself on mixing high fantasy with realistic socio-economics and a generally progressive influence does well with &quot;you can play a character that's not human, because they're a different colour&quot;!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am personally annoyed how almost every fantasy setting out there, no matter how ingenious it is otherwise, has humans in it and usually in a very central role of either being the race that is rising to prominence or the race that has already done so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I'm okay with the fact that Exalted says &quot;humans are the most important race because they're 99% of the world's sapient non-spirit population&quot;. Not that I wouldn't mind more stuff like the Dragon Kings per-se, but it is an explanation that makes sense.<br /> It makes a change from all those settings where there's several races that are massively long-lived, and either better at magic or tougher than humans, yet somehow there's not nearly as many of them and they're not very important.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, in my DnD game, I play the only human, and the other characters definitely do not consider humans prominent. They just think that humans are the horny perv race. They'll sleep with anything and anyone, which is why they have such a large population. I've explained that it takes two to tango, and it's not our fault that we're just the most attractive race, but unfortunately I'm outnumbered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Seriously, people <i>always</i> forget that the Lintha were portrayed as virtually always only ever eating <b>one another</b>. They regarded it as a respectful gesture (as many real life cannibalistic cultures have)!</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">They were actually averse to eating the flesh of other humans, because they thought they were unworthy of the honour and that doing so would contaminate them, and they reserved a special ire for anybody else that might eat the Lintha. There's an implication that they'd eat fallen Exalted, and a particularly respectable mortal warrior might get a small portion of their heart consumed, but that was it.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yeah, it is quite a key point.<br /> <br /> Though I can well imagine that it's the sort of thing where many people in the setting<i> think</i> the Lintha do eat people. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T08:30:20-07:00","id":1303323,"title":"","content":"Third Edition does seem to be the one that is most accommodating to the idea that there are non-humans present, even if in keeping with its sensibilities of more verisimilitude in social dynamics and pulp fantasy roots, they tend to exist on the margins.<br /> <br /> Recently, I've found myself somewhat averse to the idea implied or stated in other Editions that the beginning of the Realm coincided with the deliberate extermination of all non-allied inhuman races. Not out of a particular concern for the moral outlook of pre-historic Exalted, it just doesn't sit well with me.<br /> <br /> As an alternative, I've come to a notion that, for those who survived the War of the Gods (and it was still a significant toll from their own wills or those of the Primordials driving a lot of them to fight long past the point of reason), the new dynamic was one in which they initially fell under the hegemony of human beings.<br /> <br /> Over the millenia of the First Age, you might have gotten some who were further dwindled by war with the Realm in the manner of the Niobraran League (although I picture none of them having the good fortune to actually have their own non-human Exalted), but for the most part it was a matter of growing human populations and alterations to landscape to suit them left other kinds further and further marginalized, such that negative population growth was driven primarily by having fewer resources and thus less children. As well as something of a general cultural trauma which reduced a lot of motivation.<br /> <br /> In particular, I have this picture of the Alaun continuing to reside on the Blessed Isle for the first few centuries of the Age, but the departure of the Celestial Gods (with whom they would have become disillusioned anyway) and loss of the Primordials left them a lot more listless. As humans began to colonise the Isle, they simply retreated further and further into mountains in which they were poorly adapted to survive, until they just died out.<br /> <br /> These are, I think, best suited as ideas for mythology informing the actions of some surviving beings on the margins, as well as what the revelations of examining old ruins would be.<br /> <br /> That and a sense that one or two Infernal Exalted might style themselves as a patron for monsters and take a dim view of humanity (not just for a sense that the loss of other beings was an injustice), and incorporate such background into the ideology of an anti-human agenda.<br /> <br /> (I say one or two not to diminish the idea, but because there aren't many Infernals)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T12:35:37-07:00","id":1303384,"title":"","content":"I know I mentioned it, but I did have an idea for bringing back some extinct races. Not through resurrection, that's illegal. I was a bit more clever<br /> <br /> <br /> Also had a few ideas for some races, though one was a post RotSE idea. We need a seperate thread for that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T16:19:51-07:00","id":1303426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I loved Lintha as a seperate but close to human species. Their mechanics were a bit wonky, the little we got, but I wouldnt personally mind if they were just Kimberrys version of humans as long as they were stable enough of a line to be considered a race of their own. Demon Charms work fine for them but again I would have liked for them to have something of their own like the Dragon King\u2019s got.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in part since as I noted before, they originally just well, weren't. They had Solar Charms in <b>Blood &amp; Salt</b> purely as a stop-gap and minimize sourceobok cross-referencing. And as noted a bit, they're basically Ocean Elves/Orcs in how they're presented in 2e. They're weird-looking humans wiht pwoers, which never quite to me seemed alien enough to jusitfy being non-human. Them being non-human is just a weird bit of fanon evolving into canon as has happened at times in the line's history and htey were in the end an example to me of <i>lazy</i> non-human races. They were human save for some aeshtetic differences (which in Creaiton barely qualify you as non-human) and a history that was originally propoganda from a proto-nationalist racist sect. It reified the legend, rather than actually getting what it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then again the only thing that generally bothers me in Exalted, aside from second editions only exalted matter frame of mind, is it\u2019s worlds humanocentricism. I am personally annoyed how almost every fantasy setting out there, no matter how ingenious it is otherwise, has humans in it and usually in a very central role of either being the race that is rising to prominence or the race that has already done so. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted from Day One sort of stood out ot me actually on how human-centric it is. I think that often times, folks who want non-human stories focus often on things that just aren't relevant to humanity a lot of the time. Or their want for non-humans are in the end purely aesthetic, as I foten see most folks who insist on playing elves or dwarves want. I would also say it's not really every setting is like this. Many settings really have nothing that's really important about humans save a protagnoist, as many D&amp;D ones tend to be (Faerun, Eberron, and Dark Sun are all pretty human-agnostic). Additionally, many settings just don't have non-human races that are really relevant save as Star Trek aliens, where htey might have well been a human culture.<br /> <br /> Exalted focuses on humans because it wants to tell stories of myth, legend, and pulp fantasy, which is often well, human-centric. The Ramayana is about demigods, but thsoe demigods are ultimately human. The Book of New Sun has non-humans, but the story is ultiamtely about how humans survive in the world they broke. If the non-humans fit in the human stories, they might as well often just be humans. Elves and dwarves often don't do much save to have a group who lives long or is more powerful or something. And often settings waste time trying to charectierize why their barely-not-human races justify their presence rather than having just good cultures about. Being upset that Exalted, a game which draws on very human-centric stories for its inspriation, isn't more non-human centric feels like complaining a dog sucks because it doesn't meow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That is propably why my first editions favored character template were the Fair Folk ...</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I actulaly think Fair Folk never should have been playable to begin with and are overladen with twee meta shit that it kind of shows my issues with them. They don't play the same game other characters in Exalted do in the 1e and cruddy 2e copy-paste. It's an exercise in my view of an alien thought project forced into a game about humans, rather than a genuinely interesting non-human race to play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and to a lesser extent the Alchemicals, whom I didn\u2019t have any real chance to play as most St\u2019s didn\u2019t involve them in their creation, ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemicals to me wer always very human or about human-adjacent stuff. If anything, alienation, nationalism, and their place in very human cultures in an alien environment. That they are often Chosen from the best of humanity, serve to help humans in their Nations, and so on actually kind of implies what I was saying earlier. It's not a matter that you want non-humans. You want the traditional fantasy non-human aesthetic that Exalted just doesn't assume is distinct enough to be called such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and the Dragon-Blooded whom I have always played very elementally including their looks being more reminescent of elementals in human shape than humans. And naturally for me the best thing out of second edition, and the one that finally got me to move on to that editions of the game from1st were the Infernal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's notable in my notes above that this is about complaining a game about human stories doesn't let you opt out of its themes to play a not-human. I would argue that Infernals were actually kind of bad for this as they basically were a wastebin bag of powers that also let you just kind of toss out the themes of the game. It also misses out that Dragon-Blooded you know, still have human children, nations, and wants. This again all feels like a want for aestheticlaly not-human, rathe than acutally not-human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is more of a personal beef with me. Still I welcome any even remotly non-human aspect that gets to stay in the game especially the Lintha whom I have always loved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lintha non-humanity was tenuous at best and was more evil Tolkien elf than it was anything I consider actually alien.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303290#post1303290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playable Lintha with their own power set would be my personal dream and I\u2019d take them rather than some new type of Exalted. I think the world of Exalted would be enriched by there being more variation in the actual beings living there in opposition to there just being more Exalted.<br /> <br /> But then again my opinion hardly matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game is called Exalted and the Exalted come from humanity. It's a game about myths, legends, pulp fantasy revival, epics, kung fu and anime action. These are in the end, just not the things that to me lend themselves to truly alien non-humans. I also honestly just don't get the appeal of playing non-humans besides I guess aesthetic preferences, rather than genuienly exploring something different, or which often feels like an undermining of the main goals and themes of the gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T21:23:33-07:00","id":1305395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212058-non-human-races?p=1303282#post1303282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Vance has said that in 3e the original lintha were demon blooded humans.<br /> <br /> Or primordial blooded or whatever.<br /> <br /> Kimbery + mortal = Lintha.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;God&quot;-blooded covers a lot of weird s**t that is not quite divine on principle, so god-blood is ok. Specially considering that after millenia of deals and interactions with a crapload of supernatural beings &quot;Lintha blood heritage&quot; might be an absurd morass of demonic, divine, elemental, fae, ghostly and who knows what else. Supposing it ever was anything but and not myth mixed with self-deluded propaganda.<br /> <br /> And i agree with Blaque's points on the subject of how humanity stands in the center of Exalted's tale from a mythic perspective and from that standpoint &quot;foreign&quot; or &quot;other&quot; might be far more appropriate &amp; resonant word overall than &quot;non-human&quot;, humanity having room for far greater strangeness in myth &amp; Creation than in real life, as shown by unusual skin colors, leaf for hair, lineages with descent from bestial deities and so on.<br /> <br /> Damn, it <b>is </b>the niche of dwarves &amp; elves (and giants) in norse mythology for that matter, being magical people as much as monsters, if not more so, might be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-20-2021, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}